    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter sp. has been isolated from the gut of greater wax moth and may contribute to polyethylene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a genus of bacteria capable of LDPE degradation, showing high abundance in PP-fed environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is isolated from the greater wax moth, involved in PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a genus within the Enterobacteriaceae family, involved in the degradation of plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a bacterium found in the gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus larvae, playing a role in the biodegradation of polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. plays a major role in the gut microbiome of Z. atratus larvae, aiding in the degradation of polypropylene."</data>
