    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLUS FLAVUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus flavus is a fungus found in the guts of wax moths, involved in biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a fungus isolated from the gut of greater wax moth, potentially involved in polyethylene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a fungus that aids in the PE degradation process within Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a lignocellulose-degrading fungus, isolated from wax moth, and known to upregulate laccase-like multicopper oxidases under plastic stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a fungus isolated from the gut of the greater wax moth, involved in PE degradation."</data>
