    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exiguobacterium is a genus of bacteria reported to degrade polystyrene in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterium capable of creating biofilms and degrading polystyrene in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterium isolated from the digestive tract of the mealworm larvae, recognized for its ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a strain of bacteria isolated from mealworms that can degrade polystyrene, indicative of its role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2, isolated from yellow mealworm, may play a role in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is one of the bacteria within insect gut microbiota involved in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial species capable of degrading low molecular weight polyethylene wax under sterilized compost conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of bacteria isolated from the gut of superworms, capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas Sp. is a genus of bacteria known for its ability to biodegrade various materials, including flexible polyurethane foams derived from castor oil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a genus of bacteria isolated from the gut of superworms (Zophobas aratus), involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium isolated from the gut of superworms, notable for its capability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp., isolated from the gut of superworm, potentially contributes to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a genus of bacteria known for its versatile metabolism, including the ability to degrade polystyrene and other complex organic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium identified for its ability to biodegrade polystyrene, isolated from the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is isolated from superworm, involved in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium capable of biodegrading polystyrene, which has been isolated from the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a genus of bacteria that has been studied for its ability to degrade styrene, a compound related to polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is known for a mixture that degrades polystyrene film, albeit with low efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a genus of bacteria known for its metabolic diversity, including the ability to degrade synthetic plastics."</data>
