c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRAHYDROFURAN (THF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solvent used for extraction in the experiment, provided by Aladdin, Shanghai, with a GC grade purity of ≥ 99.9%."&lt;SEP&gt;"A solvent used in the extraction and measurement of residual PS in frass during analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organic solvent used to extract residual polymers from mealworm frass for molecular weight analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used for the extraction of polystyrene (PS) and polyvinyl chloride (PVC) during plastic degradation analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is an organic solvent used in the extraction process of plastic fragments from frass for biodegradation evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used in polymer chemistry, including dissolving PVC for further analysis in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is added to stop biological activity in the samples at the end of the experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used in the extraction process to analyze the molecular weight of Styrofoam degradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is used as a solvent in the Soxhlet extraction process to extract compounds from the fecula of Styrofoam-feeding mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is an industrial solvent known for its ability to dissolve a wide range of chemical compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to dissolve PS materials for GPC analysis, important in studying biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is used as a solvent for extracting PS during plastic biodegradation characterization. It is noted for its high purity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is an industrial solvent used in the production of plastics and as a precursor to other chemical compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"A solvent used to extract PS and PVC during molecular weight analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is the extraction solvent for PS and PVC in the biodegradation analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE ELECTRICAL AND ELECTRONIC EQUIPMENT (WEEE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WEEE refers to discarded electrical and electronic devices, which are less preferred by G. mellonella larvae compared to pristine plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE RIGID POLYURETHANE (WRPU)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WRPU is a type of polyurethane waste material that is less preferred by G. mellonella larvae compared to pristine plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE POLYSTYRENE (WPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WPS is a type of polystyrene waste which shows lower preference by G. mellonella larvae when compared to pristine plastics due to different chemical structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRISTINE PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pristine plastics refer to unprocessed plastics that are preferred by G. mellonella over other waste plastics in degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENOL-FORMALDEHYDE RESIN (PFR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PFR is a type of plastic material that is part of the preference hierarchy of G. mellonella larvae relative to other plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMAL CHARACTERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermal characterization involves analyzing materials' thermal properties, such as decomposition and heat flow, using instruments like TGA analyzers under specific conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TGA ANALYZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The TGA analyzer is an instrument used for thermal gravimetric analysis, determining weight changes in materials under controlled temperature and atmosphere conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy (XPS) is used to analyze the elemental distribution on PS film surfaces to verify degradation behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS (X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy) is a technique used to investigate surface chemical components of materials by measuring kinetic energy and the number of electrons."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS, or X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy, is employed to analyze the chemical states of elements on the PS film surfaces, showing changes post-microbial incubation."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS (Extruded Polystyrene Foam) is a type of styrofoam used to feed mealworms in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a technique used for measuring molecular weights of polymers, providing information on polymer length distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC or Gel Permeation Chromatography, a method used for determining molecular weight, not applicable to polyether-PU Foam due to its chemical structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC, or Gel Permeation Chromatography, is used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of plastics in frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC, short for Gel Permeation Chromatography, is utilized for analyzing the degradation of plastics within worm guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel Permeation Chromatography, employed to study molecular weight changes in degraded plastic samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is used to analyze molecular weight distribution of EPS plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel Permeation Chromatography (GPC) is a technique used to analyze changes in the molecular weight of PS polymers after larvae processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel permeation chromatography (GPC) is used for analyzing the molecular weights and molecular weight distribution of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is used to assess the degree of PVC depolymerization, helping to measure molecular weight changes in the polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a technique used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers like polystyrene in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is used to characterize molecular weight distribution in depolymerized polymer samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC, or Gel Permeation Chromatography, is used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of mask layers before and after being degraded by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel Permeation Chromatography, a type of size exclusion chromatography that is used to determine the molecular weight distribution of the mask materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC stands for Gel Permeation Chromatography, and it is employed to confirm biodegradation by analyzing molecular weight distribution of plastics after mealworm digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel Permeation Chromatography, a technique used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIAL COMMUNITY ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbial community analysis studies the diversity and function of microorganisms in the mealworm gut using DNA sequencing techniques."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNEASY BLOOD AND TISSUE KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A kit used for DNA extraction from various tissues, crucial for preparing samples for microbial community analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 16S rRNA gene is a gene region used to analyze microbial communities in the environmental samples from the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;The 16S rRNA gene is a crucial component of prokaryotic ribosomes, specifically the 30S subunit, and serves multiple essential roles in the fields of microbiology and phylogenetics. As a genetic marker, it is widely used for sequencing bacterial samples to investigate microbial diversity and composition, particularly in gut microbiota. This gene is an integral part of the 16S ribosomal RNA sequences, which are fundamental in identifying and analyzing bacterial community structure. It is extensively utilized in both phylogenetic studies and the reconstruction of phylogenies, as well as in bacterial identification and microbial taxonomy.

In particular, the 16S rRNA gene is a pivotal tool in studying bacterial microbiome diversity in various environmental and specific contexts, such as the gut microbiome of mealworm larvae, especially those fed on plastic diets. It plays a significant role in metagenomics research by aiding in the analysis and identification of microorganisms within the digestive tracts of mealworms and facilitating studies on polyethylene degradation. The gene's application extends to PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) amplification, where it serves as a reliable marker in PCR amplicon sequencing. This is essential for exploring microbial community diversity and structure and constructing maximum-likelihood trees to classify and identify microorganisms, including specific bacterial strains like NyZ450 and NyZ451.

Furthermore, the 16S rRNA gene is instrumental in microbial community analysis, used to identify Operational Taxonomic Units (OTUs) within larvae, and is vital in the analysis of samples from mealworm guts. Overall, the 16S rRNA gene is an invaluable resource in understanding bacterial phylogeny and taxonomy, offering insights into microbial diversity and ecological interactions across various scientific studies.</data>
