    <node id="&quot;STAPHYLOCOCCUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterial group known to participate in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterium present in the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor that facilitates degradation of polystyrene and lignocellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus sp. is a genus of bacteria associated with the polyether-PU-fed microbiome and potentially involved in PU degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus species are bacteria involved in microbiome studies related to plastic degradation."</data>
