    <node id="&quot;Z. ATRATUS LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Z. atratus larvae are hosts for microorganisms that can aid in the degradation of various plastics, including PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae, also known as superworms, are used in biodegradation experiments to study plastic digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE) is a type of plastic polymer that exhibits limited depolymerization when ingested by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene (LDPE) is another common plastic product that is biodegraded by mealworms through their unique digestive mechanism."&lt;SEP&gt;Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE) is a type of polyethylene widely recognized for its linear structure with branching, which gives it a lower density and increased flexibility compared to other plastics. This makes LDPE a popular choice for numerous applications, including cling films, shopping bags, packaging materials, containers, tubing, and foams. Known for its chemical bonds and structure, LDPE is examined extensively in scientific research due to its unique biodegradation properties.

LDPE is subject to biodegradation primarily in studies involving insects such as the larvae of Tenebrio molitor and T. obscurus, which can ingest and partially digest the material. The degradation process is facilitated by specific bacterial strains, including Enterobacter sp. and Priestia megaterium S1, which are found in the gut of these insects. Although LDPE is relatively more resistant to biodegradation compared to other polymers like PET, the mealworms' gut microbiota enhances the breakdown efficiency, leading to a significant reduction in LDPE's molecular weight and structural integrity. This process is complemented by oxidative degradation in bioactive soils and has been found to be more effective than the degradation of other plastics such as LLDPE and HDPE, owing to LDPE's lower molecular weight and branching structure.

LDPE depolymerization has even been studied in the presence of antibiotics, showing that its breakdown can be independent of gut microbes. These findings are crucial for exploring biological solutions for plastic waste management and highlight LDPE's pivotal role in biodegradation and biofilm formation research. By understanding the interactions between LDPE, mealworms, and broader environmental factors, researchers gain valuable insights into innovative methods for addressing plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene (LDPE) is a type of plastic that has been subject to biodegradation processes similar to those observed with polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-109486cd939a227e73354d0478c59ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b364