hunk-bdf2753a9a78b282c1ca2c0539e3203d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f4c282fe2323dc6e310501af888c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYURETHANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic often studied alongside polystyrene for its chemical properties in food packaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"A synthetic polymer often used in plastics and foams, subject to biodegradation by certain bacteria and fungi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane, including kitchen sponge (PU1) and commercial thermal insulation foam (PU2), was investigated for biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane, referred to as PU, a polymer composed of organic units joined by carbamate (urethane) links, used in foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer composed of organic units joined by carbamate (urethane) links. It is used in many applications and its biodegradation is of interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PUR) is a polymer composed of organic units joined by carbamate (urethane) links, used in foams, elastomers, and coatings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer material, commonly used in the production of various consumer goods and industrial products, which can be degraded by certain bacterial consortia."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of polymer used in various applications for its durability and flexibility, often studied for biodegradation under different conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a commonly used synthetic polymer that can be recalcitrant in the environment. Degradation by landfill microbial communities is studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer composed of organic units joined by carbamate links, known for its flexibility and wide range of applications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f102938f307d7404d3f31b7200d93768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLUS TUBINGENSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fungus studied for its ability to biodegrade polyester polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus known for its ability to biodegrade polyester polystyrene, contributing to environmental pollutant reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus known for its ability to biodegrade polyester polyurethane, contributing to plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus known for its ability to biodegrade polyester polyurethane, contributing to environmental pollutant breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCR (POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A laboratory technique used to amplify DNA sequences, making it easier to study genetic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technique used to amplify DNA sequences, including those of nitrogen-fixing genes in isolates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR (FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to obtain an infrared spectrum of absorption or emission of a solid, liquid, or gas."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is used to analyze chemical changes in materials during biodegradation and oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An analytical technique used to identify chemical compositions and structures, commonly applied to studying plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is an analytical technique used to determine chemical changes and transformations in polystyrene samples after being processed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is a technique to obtain infrared spectrum of absorption of a sample, used to identify chemical changes and new functional groups in biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is a technique used to identify chemical functionalities in plastics, assisting in understanding biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc6b858a4eb57553f5b1ae041e1c7160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPC (GEL PERMEATION CHROMATOGRAPHY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of size exclusion chromatography that separates analytes based on their size."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is a method used to analyze the molecular weights of plastic polymers before and after being processed by superworms and yellow mealworms to assess the degree of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is an analytical method used to determine the molecular weight distribution of polymers extracted from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a type of chromatography used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is used to determine the molecular weights and weight distributions of Styrofoam and degraded products in fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers before and after larval consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is an analytical method used to determine the molecular weight distribution of polymers like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is a method used to measure the molecular weight of Styrofoam and its degradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is used to assess changes in molecular weight and distribution of residual polymers in plastics-fed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is a method used to analyze the molecular weight distributions of polymers like polypropylene during the study of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC is an analytical technique used to characterize polymer depolymerization by measuring molecular weight changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU (POLYURETHANE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A highly versatile polymer used in a wide range of products including cushioning foams and coatings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a type of plastic that undergoes biodegradation in the presence of microorganisms and certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU, or Polyurethane, is another type of plastic used to assess its impact on larvae growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic that Aspergillus tubingenis from soil is capable of degrading."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP (POLYPROPYLENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A thermoplastic polymer used in a wide variety of applications, including packaging and textiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is a plastic material similar to LDPE with reduced dependence on gut microbiomes for successful degradation by T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP, or Polypropylene, is studied to assess its biodegradation by analyzing its residual content in frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypropylene is another type of plastic that may be degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is a form of plastic tested in the study for its consumption rate by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypropylene is a type of plastic that is consumed by mealworms, ranked as the second most favorable for consumption in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is a linear hydrocarbon resin with a chemical formula (\(C_2H_4\))_n, known for forming various chain structures such as atactic, isotactic, and syndiotactic. It is a major source of plastic waste and pollutants in the form of microplastics and nanoplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC (POLYVINYL CHLORIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A widely produced synthetic plastic polymer, used in plumbing, electrical cable insulation, and more."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is another plastic material requiring gut microbes for its biodegradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is another synthetic polymer analyzed in the study to understand its degradation in frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is a commonly used plastic that mealworms have shown to consume, as documented in research."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is a type of microplastic whose crystalline structure was changed by mealworms from Tai'an and Shenzhen but not by those from Guangzhou."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is a type of polymer whose mass and crystalline structure changes were studied after being metabolized by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is a type of plastic in film form, used in the experiments, and includes various additives like plasticizers, flame retardants, and adhesives."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is among the plastics tested in the experiment, typically found as hard plastic bags, to evaluate its consumption by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl Chloride is included in the study and is less favored by mealworms compared to PS and PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is synthetic plastic polymer tested with mealworms to study its potential decomposition by gut bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCOA (PRINCIPAL COORDINATE ANALYSIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used in statistics to visualize the similarities or dissimilarities of data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEM (SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scanning electron microscope (SEM) uses focused beams of electrons to create detailed images of sample surfaces, useful in microbiology studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of electron microscope that produces images of a sample by scanning it with a focused beam of electrons."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a type of microscope used to analyze the surface structure and degradation progress of nanoplastic particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is used for morphology observation and micro area composition analysis of larval frass after plastic consumption."</data>
