    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO OBSCURUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrio obscurus is a related species to Tenebrio molitor, also studied for its ability to biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus is a species of mealworm beetle, investigated for its plastic degradation ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus, also known as dark mealworms, have the ability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio obscurus, commonly known as the dark mealworm, is a species of darkling beetle within the Tenebrionidae family, closely related to Tenebrio molitor. It is a worldwide-distributed insect demonstrating adaptability to various environments. The larvae of Tenebrio obscurus, often referred to as mealworms or mini mealworms, are particularly noteworthy for their ability to biodegrade synthetic polymers, including polystyrene and low-density polyethylene. This species has been extensively studied for its potential in environmental research, especially concerning the reduction of plastic waste. The larvae contribute significantly to biodegradation by modifying the polymer backbones, thus facilitating the breakdown of these materials and interacting with microplastics. Remarkably, Tenebrio obscurus shows the capacity to degrade plastics independently of gut microbes, offering promising solutions to tackle the global environmental challenge of plastic pollution through innovative, microbe-independent processes. Its effectiveness in reducing the molecular weight of polystyrene and participating in depolymerization processes makes Tenebrio obscurus a subject of considerable interest for developing sustainable methods to manage plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae contribute to the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85ab9c6af7915311ccbb4804160be5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c7b499dc783c21f764eb35989a449f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
