    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SP. D1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut microbiome during plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter Sp. D1 is a strain isolated from wax moth guts, associated with the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the guts of wax moth Galleria mellonella, known for its polyethylene biodegradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. d1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of wax moth Galleria mellonella, capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter Sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the guts of wax moth Galleria mellonella, involved in polyethylene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a strain of bacteria isolated from the guts of wax moth larvae, which has demonstrated the ability to degrade polyethylene."</data>
