    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYLACTIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polylactic Acid (PLA) is a biodegradable polymer derived from renewable resources, used as an alternative to traditional plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a biodegradable and bioactive thermoplastic made from renewable resources like corn starch or sugar cane, commonly used in 3D printing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable plastic that can be broken down by Tenebrio molitor larvae, contributing to waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources, subject to photolytic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable plastic that is degraded by yellow mealworms, aiding in resource recovery and waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a biodegradable plastic derived from renewable resources like corn starch, which is studied for biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable plastic used as an alternative to conventional plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a biodegradable polymer subject to studies on degradation through microbial adhesion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene is a common thermoplastic polymer used in a variety of products, known for its durability and resistance to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a synthetic polymer subject to microbial degradation and deterioration."&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene, commonly abbreviated as PE, is the most widely used plastic polymer, composed of repeating ethylene units. It is known for its resilience, chemical resistance, and simple structure, making it extensively employed in consumer goods, packaging, films, containers, and plastic bags due to its durability and flexibility. Despite these robust attributes, polyethylene poses significant environmental challenges as persistent plastic waste. It is commonly found as waste in landfill sites and is often studied for its decomposition and environmental impact.

Research has shown that polyethylene is subject to biodegradation under specific conditions. This polymer can be metabolized by certain organisms, such as the larvae of the Greater Wax Moth (Galleria mellonella) and the mealworm (Tenebrio molitor), within their digestive systems, aided by specialized gut microorganisms. Additionally, bacteria like Enterobacter sp. D1 and Rhodococcus ruber have demonstrated the ability to biodegrade polyethylene, with Rhodococcus ruber forming biofilms to enhance the process. The enzymes present in the saliva of waxworm larvae have also been identified as contributors to polyethylene degradation, suggesting potential avenues for its use as a carbon source by these organisms.

Moreover, marine microbes and specific insect larvae have shown the capability to biodegrade polyethylene, highlighting the material's susceptibility to breakdown under certain conditions. This discovery opens promising paths for reducing plastic pollution via biological means. Current innovative approaches aim to utilize these natural processes, improving plastic waste management strategies. Studies continue to investigate polyethylene's behavior under various environmental conditions, such as exposure to UV light and different chemical environments. Consequently, understanding these mechanisms could lead to more effective solutions for managing persistent plastic waste.

Although polyethylene remains resistant to degradation in typical conditions, its potential for biodegradation by specific insects, microorganisms, and fungi underscores the necessity for sustainable waste management explorations. These insights into natural biodegradation processes inspire optimism for minimizing polyethylene's environmental impact, making it a crucial focus of ongoing environmental research.&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a plastic polymer used in the study to observe the digestive capabilities of mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a synthetic polymer used as a substrate in mealworm larvae degradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a type of plastic whose degradation was studied in the mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372aa232f6e8aad1d8e0a93f16a42b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ee089593160e720e507848fa8c917a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367