      <data key="d2">chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect pests cause damage to packaging films, creating breaches that compromise storage and product integrity."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de</data>
      <data key="d1">"An essential process in reducing plastic waste, facilitated by organisms like specific bacteria and larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials that accumulate in the environment, causing ecological and health issues due to their persistence and non-biodegradable nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic Waste refers to the various plastic materials tested in the experiment to evaluate their degradation when consumed by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to the accumulation of plastic products in the environment, posing a significant pollution challenge."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to discarded plastic materials, whose hazardous classification and management are topics of discussion in environmental science."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials that can enter the environment, causing pollution and posing risks to wildlife and ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic products, causing severe air, water, and soil pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to plastic materials that are discarded or intended to be discarded, contributing to environmental pollution, especially in oceans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste is treated using mealworms, whose digestion process is outlined for potential environmental and economic benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to plastic materials discarded as waste, often accumulating in land and marine environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded or accumulated plastic products, such as polystyrene, that contribute to environmental pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials, such as polystyrene, that pose environmental pollution challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic Waste refers to discarded plastic materials that contribute significantly to environmental pollution, and are targeted for microbial degradation solutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials that pose environmental challenges due to their accumulation and slow degradation in natural environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste poses environmental challenges that are addressed through biodegradation with organisms such as mealworms and microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste, including items such as disposable surgical masks and foam plastics, is subject to biodegradation by insects and their associated microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic products that contribute significantly to pollution and pose environmental challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic products that contribute to environmental pollution, especially in oceans and soil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials, which pose significant environmental challenges. Research on Tenebrio genus offers potential solutions for degrading such waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials that contribute to environmental pollution and pose a threat to wildlife and ecosystems."</data>
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Mealworm larvae, specifically those of the species Tenebrio molitor, are insect invertebrates that have garnered significant interest for their unique capabilities and applications in scientific research and environmental sustainability. These larvae are primarily studied due to their remarkable ability to biodegrade various plastic materials such as polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene (PE), playing an important role in innovative waste conversion methods, including turning waste into biodiesel. This biodegradation capability is attributed to a multi-stage digestion process facilitated by microorganisms in their gut, including species such as Achromobacter and Pseudomonas aeruginosa. 

In scientific studies, mealworm larvae are utilized as model organisms to investigate the survival and biodegradation of microplastics, assessing their ability to ingest and biodegrade these materials, despite potentially experiencing oxidative stress and physiological damage. They are a focus of research on plastic waste management, serving as a source of microbiome samples to understand the effects of different substrates on gut microbiota and waste degradation processes.

Beyond their environmental benefits, mealworm larvae are investigated for their growth characteristics and protein content, responding to various feed types including bran, potatoes, whey, and polystyrene foam. Researchers examine their physiological responses, microbial counts, cytotoxic effects, and the impact of feed types on fatty acid composition. Commercially, these larvae are recognized for their nutritional value and rapid growth, making them a sustainable protein source in food systems and live animal feed.

Overall, mealworm larvae of Tenebrio molitor are promising entities for addressing plastic waste challenges and contributing to sustainable food systems, illustrating their value in both environmental science and commercial applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REACTIVE OXYGEN SPECIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reactive oxygen species (ROS) are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen, which can cause oxidative degradation of various substances, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemically reactive molecules involved in the oxidative degradation processes of plastics such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are molecules that indicate oxidative stress levels in organisms. Higher levels were found in mealworm larvae fed with pure polyethylene, though these levels could be mitigated by the inclusion of a bran supplement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive oxygen species are chemically reactive molecules containing oxygen that play a role in oxidative stress in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANT ENZYME ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of enzymes that help to prevent oxidative damage in mealworm larvae during plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Activities of antioxidant enzymes are elevated in mealworm larvae exposed to polyethylene, indicative of physiological responses to oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Activities of enzymes such as SOD, GST, and CAD that protect the body by neutralizing reactive oxygen species (ROS) and other free radicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Processes involving enzymes that mitigate oxidative damage, influenced by exposure to microplastics of varying degradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzyme activities involve enzymatic actions that protect against oxidative damage by neutralizing reactive oxygen species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID PEROXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biochemical process in which free radicals take electrons from lipids in cell membranes, resulting in cell damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"A process indicating oxidative degradation of lipids in mealworm larvae exposed to microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a process indicating oxidative degradation of lipids. It is observed at higher rates in mealworm larvae consuming polyethylene, revealing cellular stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation occurs in mealworm larvae as a result of oxidative stress from plastic ingestion and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation involves the oxidative degradation of lipids, often increased during oxidative stress conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a marker of oxidative stress indicating damage to lipids in cells, studied during the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oxidative degradation of lipids, which increases with higher toxic microplastic exposure, used as a measure of cellular damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a process in which free radicals take electrons from the lipids in cell membranes, resulting in cell damage, observed under oxidative stress conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oxidative degradation of lipids, indicating oxidative damage in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stress response caused by an imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants, leading to potential cell damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative Stress is a physiological response observed in mealworms when fed with ultrahigh-molecular-weight polymers, impacting their antioxidant systems and membranes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is a condition caused by plastics, affecting stress response pathways like glutathione metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a physiological condition characterized by an imbalance between the production of free radicals, such as reactive oxygen species (ROS), and the organism's antioxidant defenses. This imbalance can lead to potential cellular damage. Oxidative stress can be activated by environmental factors, such as exposure to micro- and nano-plastics, which promote excessive ROS production. The condition is notably observed in various organisms, including insects like mealworm larvae and Daphnia magna, especially when they are exposed to pollutants or engage in ingesting plastics, such as polyethylene (PE) or Styrofoam. In such situations, an increase in ROS levels during processes like PE biodegradation leads to oxidative stress, characterized by elevated reactive oxygen species and lipid peroxidation. Insects consuming a polymeric diet or exposed to toxic substances like PVC experience oxidative stress, impacting their cellular function and enzyme synthesis. This condition is a harmful response caused by the organism's inability to detoxify these free radicals efficiently, potentially leading to physiological damage in organisms like Tenebrio larvae assessed for damage due to PE microplastic exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is a condition involving reactive oxygen species, impacting nitrogen retention during the biodegradation of polystyrene in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is an imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants in the body, leading to cellular damage, and is induced in mealworms fed with microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress refers to an imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants in the body, leading to cell and tissue damage, studied in context with pollutants like microplastics and atrazine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress refers to the imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants in organisms, resulting in damage to cells and tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress refers to the physiological condition arising from the imbalance between the production of reactive oxygen species and antioxidant defenses, observed in mealworms exposed to microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56</data>
    </node>
