    <node id="&quot;COLEOPTERA: TENEBRIONIDAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A family of beetles known for certain species' ability to biodegrade plastics, such as those found within the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae is the taxonomic family to which Tenebrio molitor belongs, known for the biodegradation capabilities of its larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae refers to the beetle family commonly used in biodegradation research involving mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A family of beetles that includes species such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, known for their role in biodegradation and pest control."&lt;SEP&gt;"This order and family classification relates to the beetles including Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, known for their capacity to degrade synthetic plastics."</data>
