    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genotoxicity refers to the ability of harmful substances to damage genetic information in cells, a critical parameter in toxicological studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genotoxicity refers to the damaging effect on genetic material leading to mutations, observed with nanoplastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genotoxicity refers to the property of chemical agents that damage the genetic information in a cell causing mutations, which is important in assessing food safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genotoxicity refers to the property of chemical agents that damages the genetic information within a cell, leading to mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a</data>
    </node>
