      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources like corn starch used in various plastic products, degradable by the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources, subject to breakdown by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources like corn starch."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a biodegradable polymer used as a substitute for plastics, undergoing microbial degradation as part of waste management approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a biodegradable bioplastic that can be used in earthworms' diet and is easily degradable, though slow to excrete."</data>
