    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT-MICROBE-DEPENDENT DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process of polymer breakdown aided by microorganisms residing in the digestive tract, crucial in the biodegradation of plastics by superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A process where specific microbes within the gut of insects like mealworms break down polymeric materials, facilitating biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization refers to the biodegradation of polymers facilitated by microbial activity within an organism's digestive tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microbes in digestive systems break down polymers like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-Microbe-Dependent Depolymerization refers to the breakdown of polypropylene by microbial communities within the gut of insects like Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus."&lt;SEP&gt;"This process involves the breakdown of polymers such as plastics aided by gut microbes, as observed in Zophobas atratus and other larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DARK MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COMMON NAME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dark Mealworms, also known as Tenebrio obscurus, are studied for their effectiveness in biodegrading plastics such as polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dark mealworms refer to the larvae of Tenebrio obscurus, which have also been studied for their role in plastic biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dark mealworms, also larvae of beetles, differ from yellow mealworms and may exhibit different biodegradation capacities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dark mealworms refer to the larvae of Tenebrio obscurus, which are investigated for their capacity to degrade PS foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64</data>
    </node>
