      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pantoea characterized the gut microbiome of mealworm larvae consuming polyethylene diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea characterized the gut microbiome of mealworm larvae consuming polyethylene diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria identified in larvae fed with polyethylene diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of Gram-negative bacteria associated with plants, known for its ability to ferment sugars."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria isolated from the adult T. molitor gut, highlighting differences in microbial composition across life stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria present in T. molitor adults with the capability to degrade plastics like low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria isolated from the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria found in larvae fed polyethylene, showing involvement in waste degradation."</data>
