    <node id="&quot;LACTOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactococcus is a genus of lactic acid bacteria within the Streptococcaceae family, predominantly found in the gut microbiota of mealworms and superworms. It plays a significant role in the gut microbiome composition, particularly in larvae fed with various plastic diets such as polyethylene (PE), polystyrene (PS), and polyurethane (PU). Known for its involvement in fermentation, Lactococcus contributes to the digestion of plastics and possibly their degradation, which is evident in its association with the gut of Tenebrio molitor and other larvae on plastic-based diets. Additionally, the presence of Lactococcus is prevalent across different test groups, showcasing its importance in gut health maintenance and general gut ecology. Aside from its biological role, Lactococcus is also utilized in the dairy industry for the production of cheese and yogurt, emphasizing its versatility.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a603837ad5b989bafd614f5eeb8504c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40</data>
