      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrosomonas is a genus of ammonia-oxidizing bacteria involved in the nitrogen cycle within soil and water ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonas is a genus of ammonia-oxidizing bacteria involved in the nitrogen cycle within soil and water ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonas is identified as a diazotrophic bacterium linked with polystyrene diet adaptations in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonas is a genus of bacteria that participates in the nitrogen cycle by converting ammonia into nitrite."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonas is identified as a diazotrophic bacterium linked with polystyrene diet adaptations in mealworms."</data>
