      <data key="d1">"OAT diet refers to the oatmeal-based diet used in the experiment, which resulted in the lowest counts of larvae and high metamorphosis rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oat diet is one of the dietary conditions used in the study to observe changes in the gut microbiome of mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The OAT diet is based on oatmeal and serves as a control with optimal growth and development results in mealworm experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The OAT diet refers to a specific regimen involving oats, utilized in studies to observe its impact on microbial and metabolic parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The OAT diet uses oatmeal, providing a control for studying the growth impact on larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oat diet is one of the dietary conditions used in the study to observe changes in the gut microbiome of mealworm larvae."</data>
