    <node id="&quot;DIAZOTROPHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diazotrophs are bacteria capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen into a bioavailable form, often found in the intestinal tract of earthworms and other organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophs are bacteria capable of nitrogen fixation, some of which are specific to the polystyrene diet in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophs are bacteria capable of nitrogen fixation, some of which are specific to the polystyrene diet in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophs are microorganisms capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen into a form usable by plants, playing a role in nitrogen distribution in symbiosis with insects."</data>
