    <node id="&quot;CELLULOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organic compound and type of polymer waste included in the study of larval diet effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound forming the primary structural component of plants, used as a substrate for mealworm larvae in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound and the primary component of plant cell walls, subject to degradation by various organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound forming the primary structural component of plant cell walls, targeted for biodegradation by various microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a natural polymer that can be biodegraded by certain larvae as part of their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a polysaccharide that T. molitor larvae can degrade, found in their diets such as wheat straw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound, a polysaccharide consisting of a linear chain of several hundred to over ten thousand beta-linked D-glucose units, and is a primary component of plant cell walls."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a natural polymer that is part of the diet tested for mealworm larvae, noted for its lesser effect on their growth compared to synthetic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organic compound consisting of a linear chain of several hundred to many thousands of β(1→4) linked D-glucose units, used by Tenebrio molitor larvae in degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound forming the primary structure of plant cell walls, also studied for biodegradation alongside plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a component of plant cell walls, serving as one of the materials consumed and digested by larvae in the study on CS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a polysaccharide found in lignocellulose, converted into sugars like glucose during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic polymer that can be degraded by the enzymatic activity in Tenebrio molitor larvae's gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound and polysaccharide consisting of a linear chain of several hundred to many thousands of β(1→4) linked D-glucose units, found in plant cell walls."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a natural polymer that can be biodegraded by organisms such as Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is a type of polymer waste whose effects were observed in the metabolism of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulose is an organic compound forming the primary structural component of plants, used as a substrate for mealworm larvae in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteria present in the gut of larvae, particularly responsive to dietary changes such as PET and WB feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are microorganisms in the mealworm larvae that secrete enzymes to catalyze the decomposition of products like polystyrene and cellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria in mealworms play an essential role in the degradation of plastics like PS, highlighting the microbiome's impact on degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria in mealworms play a key role in the depolymerization and mineralization of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are microorganisms residing in the digestive tract of superworms, playing a crucial role in digestion and potentially in the decomposition of Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are microorganisms found in the digestive systems of mealworms, responsible for decomposing polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria in the larvae are responsible for digesting and degrading plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific bacteria present in the gut of mealworms that play a crucial role in the depolymerization and biodegradation of EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are microorganisms that contribute to the digestion and development of the velvetbean caterpillar, Anticarsia gemmatalis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria within mealworms contribute to the degradation of Styrofoam, exhibiting changes in molecular weight and CO2 production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria in T. obscurus play a critical role in the biodegradation of PS, as indicated by reduced depolymerization when inhibited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are part of the microbiome in yellow mealworms and work jointly with fungi in the biodegradation process of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are the bacterial communities found within the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae, affected by different diets of foam plastics, and play a role in plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria in mealworms and other organisms are central to breaking down plastics under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microorganisms present in the gut that were the target of antibiotic treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria are microorganisms in the mealworm larvae that secrete enzymes to catalyze the decomposition of products like polystyrene and cellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria in mealworms play a significant role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, including specific strains like Exiguobacterium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
