      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the digestive tract of the mealworms, which varies significantly with different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota are the microorganisms present in the mealworm larvae's intestines, crucial for breaking down complex substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota refer to microorganisms in the gut that influence digestion and decomposition of fatty acids produced from wax degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The intestinal microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the intestinal tract of mealworms, playing a role in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The intestinal microbiota comprises various bacteria within an organism's gut, facilitating processes such as degradation of materials like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota are the microorganisms present in the mealworm larvae's intestines, crucial for breaking down complex substrates."</data>
