    <node id="&quot;ILLUMINA MISEQ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used for analyzing the DNA of the gut microbiome in the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used for sequencing DNA in paired-end mode."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used in the study to examine microbial communities in the mealworm larvae samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used to analyze the 16S rRNA gene to assess the gut bacterial community composition and diversity in superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing technology used to analyze the shifts in bacterial and fungal communities in the gut microbiomes of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used to analyze gut DNA samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing technology used to analyze PCR-amplified 16S rRNA fragments to understand the mealworm gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is an advanced sequencing technology used for comprehensive DNA analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina Miseq is a device used for phasing amplicon sequencing, suitable for robust environmental microbial community analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used for paired-end sequencing of DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing technology utilized to analyze bacterial and fungal communities within the larvae's gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used for sequencing DNA in paired-end mode."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used in the study to examine microbial communities in the mealworm larvae samples."</data>
