    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical processes involving enzymes that can degrade plastic substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity involves the chemical processes and reactions catalyzed by enzymes within the bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biochemical activity of enzymes in the microbiome of larval digestive tracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biochemical processes taking place in the larva-gut intestine, contributing to the degradation and transformation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the catalysis of chemical reactions by enzymes, which increases the rate of polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown process evident in the production of various metabolites in larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the processes where enzymes, often from microorganisms, degrade materials like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity involves the catalysis of chemical reactions by enzymes within bacterial isolates, crucial for the degradation of substances like NPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity involves the function of enzymes in facilitating biochemical reactions, crucial for the breakdown of polystyrene by Achromobacter species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biochemical activity of enzymes in the microbiome of larval digestive tracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biochemical processes activated by enzymes, playing a significant role in the bacterial community's structure and function."</data>
