    <node id="&quot;BACTEROIDETES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial phylum with different presence levels in experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a diverse family of bacteria involved in breaking down complex molecules, including in herbivorous insect digestive systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a phylum of bacteria found in the gut microbiota of mealworm larvae, with proportions differing depending on the substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is an order of bacteria that includes Gram-negative, non-spore forming, anaerobic bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a phylum observed at lower levels in the PU diet compared to the bran diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a phylum with increased presence in the gut microbiota of larvae on PS and CS diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a group of bacteria well-represented in control samples but nearly absent in polystyrene samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes are part of the bacterial shift in the yellow mealworms' gut, especially in EVA-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is another phylum observed, notably in the EVA-fed group, highlighting differences in microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes are an order of bacteria found within the gut microbiome of mealworms, contributing to various microbial activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a bacterial phylum present in the gut microbiome of mealworms, indicating microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes are a phylum of bacteria involved in nutrient processing in the digestive tracts of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is a phylum of bacteria found in the gut microbiota of mealworm larvae, with proportions differing depending on the substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidetes is an order of bacteria that includes Gram-negative, non-spore forming, anaerobic bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
