    <node id="&quot;ALPHAPROTEOBACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A class of bacteria observed in the study, known for its abundance in certain microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is a class of Proteobacteria comprising bacteria with diverse metabolisms, many of which are capable of symbiotic nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is a dominant class of bacteria within the microbiota of mealworm larvae, with higher prevalence in OAT and CEL diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is identified among the seven bacterial classes within Tenebrio molitor's gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"A class under the Proteobacteria phylum, observed in smaller quantities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria identified in the study, involved in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria that was identified with one strain in the studied dataset."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is a class of Proteobacteria comprising bacteria with diverse metabolisms, many of which are capable of symbiotic nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphaproteobacteria is a dominant class of bacteria within the microbiota of mealworm larvae, with higher prevalence in OAT and CEL diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSTRIDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A class of bacteria in the study under the order Clostridiales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridia is a class of Firmicutes, consisting of obligate anaerobic bacteria, known for causing botulism and tetanus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridia is a class of bacteria found in mealworm larvae with varying presence depending on the diet, particularly high in OAT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridia is a class of anaerobic bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, known for spore formation and roles in fermentation and human gut health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridia is classified among the significant bacterial classes in the mealworm gut environment, potentially aiding in the digestive processes related to polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridia is a class of Firmicutes, consisting of obligate anaerobic bacteria, known for causing botulism and tetanus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridia is a class of bacteria found in mealworm larvae with varying presence depending on the diet, particularly high in OAT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAVOBACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flavobacteria is a class of bacteria, known for their yellow pigmentation, part of the Bacteroidetes phylum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flavobacteria is a class of bacteria, known for their yellow pigmentation, part of the Bacteroidetes phylum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flavobacteria is one of the dominant classes within the larvae microbiota, influenced by the substrates in their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flavobacteria, found abundantly in the gut microbiome, is part of the complex bacterial ecosystem in Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flavobacteria is one of the dominant classes within the larvae microbiota, influenced by the substrates in their diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A class of bacteria within the Firmicutes phylum, including Bacillales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class of aerobic or facultatively anaerobic, Gram-positive bacteria including significant lactic acid bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class of bacteria that is widely distributed across different feeding variants in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class within the phylum Firmicutes that includes aerobic, often rod-shaped bacteria known for forming spores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is among the predominant bacterial classes identified in the microbiome diversity of Tenebrio molitor, playing a potential role in digestion and degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A class within Firmicutes, detected in diversity analysis of microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class of aerobic or facultatively anaerobic, Gram-positive bacteria including significant lactic acid bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacilli is a class of bacteria that is widely distributed across different feeding variants in mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAMMAPROTEOBACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CLASS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A major class within the Proteobacteria phylum observed in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria can degrade lignocellulose and petroleum hydrocarbons, highlighting their ability to break down organic pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class of Proteobacteria containing a wide range of pathogens and environmental organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is prevalent in mealworm larvae, particularly associated with PE-oxo and PE-reg diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is one of the seven bacterial classes found predominantly in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor, suggesting its role in degradation activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria enriched in the gut microbiota of mealworms consuming PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria, within which the order Enterobacteriales, including the family Erwiniaeae, is found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class within Proteobacteria, noted for its significant presence, with genera like Pseudomonas and Cronobacter in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria identified in the study, involved in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria that includes several families, such as Enterobacteriaceae, Yersiniaceae, Aeromonadaceae, Pseudomonadaceae, and Moraxellaceae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is a class of Proteobacteria containing a wide range of pathogens and environmental organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammaproteobacteria is prevalent in mealworm larvae, particularly associated with PE-oxo and PE-reg diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENERICUTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dominated bacterial phylum in PE-fed yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a bacterial phylum that showed significantly higher proportions in the PE-oxo diet compared to other diets in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria lacking traditional cell walls, known for causing diseases in humans and livestock."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria lacking peptidoglycan cell walls, and includes Mycoplasma and related organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The phylum represented by Spiroplasma velicicrescens, showing high population densities in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is one of the bacterial phyla found in mealworms, implicated in studies involving polystyrene consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a dominant phylum within the microbiome that varied in abundance based on the diet (PU or bran)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is one of the bacterial phyla whose relative abundance increased in the gut microbiota of larvae fed plastic and cellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a genus found within the gut microbial communities of mealworm larvae, relevant to the diversity of the microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes are the dominant phylum in the gut microbiome of PP-fed mealworms, playing a role in the microbial response to plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is the dominant phylum in the PP-fed groups, indicating its prevalence over other phyla in those conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is an order of bacteria found in the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to the composition of the microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a bacterial phylum that showed significantly higher proportions in the PE-oxo diet compared to other diets in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria lacking traditional cell walls, known for causing diseases in humans and livestock."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANCTOMYCETES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Planctomycetes are abundant in surface ocean metagenomes and are known for their nitrogen-fixing capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planctomycetes are bacteria with mechanisms for nitrogen fixation and ammonia oxidation under aerobic and anaerobic conditions, aiding nitrogen uptake by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planctomycetes is a bacterial phylum with higher than average presence in the PS diet in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planctomycetes is a bacterial phylum with higher than average presence in the PS diet in mealworm larvae."</data>
