    <node id="&quot;ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkaline Phosphatase (ALP) is an enzyme linked to bile ducts and from liver damage or bone disorders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase catalyzes the release of phosphate groups from molecules under alkaline conditions, showing substantial activity in variant PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme found in many tissues, including liver and bone, involved in dephosphorylation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme found in many tissues, including liver and bone, involved in dephosphorylation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that catalyzes the breakdown of phosphorus bonds, playing a key role in rapid phosphorus and carbon transformations."</data>
