    <node id="&quot;BACTEROIDALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order observed with high counts in the OAT group, indicative of microbial diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria commonly found in larvae microbiomes across different dietary treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria commonly found in the intestinal microbiome, playing key roles in digesting complex molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria within the Bacteroidia class, known for their abundant presence in the human gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria that influence nitrogen-fixing communities, especially in dry-wood termites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is a genus of bacteria that serve as ectosymbionts of gut flagellates in dry-wood termites, influencing the nitrogen-fixing community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteroidales is an order of bacteria within the Bacteroidia class, known for their abundant presence in the human gut microbiota."</data>
