    <node id="&quot;SPIROPLASMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria within the Spiroplasmataceae family, classified under the Mollicutes class, and known for its wall-less structure. This genus is typically found in insect and plant environments and is recognized for playing significant roles in both. In particular, Spiroplasma is prevalent in the gut microbiome of mealworms, including both yellow and dark species, where it is a top dominant genus and is crucial for their digestion and survival. This genus is commonly present in the guts of Tenebrio species, where it can be associated with the degradation of synthetic polymers such as polyethylene (PE), polypropylene (PP), and polyethylene terephthalate (PET).

Spiroplasma's abundance in the mealworm gut varies depending on the diet; it is notably higher in larvae fed on bran as opposed to those fed with PE and polystyrene (PS). It is predominantly present in larvae maintained on PP diets, highlighting its specific role in such environments, contributing to PP biodegradation. While generally associated with pathogenicity, Spiroplasma's presence in the mealworm gut microbiome is indicative of its role within insect gut ecosystems, particularly under oxygen-limited conditions in the hindgut.

Nevertheless, despite its documented prevalence, Spiroplasma was not observed in some mealworms in certain studies, suggesting variability in its presence depending on experimental conditions. Overall, Spiroplasma's role in mealworm digestion and its ability to degrade various materials underscore its significance in both ecological and applied scientific contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049</data>
