      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteolytic enzymes are produced by Achromobacter, indicating their role in breaking down proteins as part of ecological adaptation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteolytic enzymes like leucine arylamidase, valine arylamidase, and alpha-chymotrypsin are referred to with varying activity levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteolytic enzymes like leucine arylamidase, valine arylamidase, and alpha-chymotrypsin are referred to with varying activity levels."</data>
