    <node id="&quot;T. MOLITOR LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T. molitor larvae are insects used in experiments to analyze growth and feeding conditions based on the Dynamic Energy Budget (DEB) model."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae exhibit changes in development dependent on reserve dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae, commonly known as mealworms, are the larval stage of the darkling beetle species Tenebrio molitor and are widely recognized for their remarkable capacity to biodegrade a variety of both synthetic and natural polymers. These larvae are extensively used in scientific research, particularly for their ability to digest plastics such as polystyrene (PS), expanded polystyrene (EPS), polypropylene (PP), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), low-density polyethylene (LDPE), linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE), high-density polyethylene (HDPE), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), polylactic acid (PLA), and polyurethane. 

In studies, T. molitor larvae have been used to measure survival rates when fed different diets, including bran and LDPE, and to examine the consumption and biodegradation of PE foams. Their digestive system, complemented by symbiotic bacteria, facilitates depolymerization and nutrient cycling, playing a crucial role in plastic degradation despite the fact that plastics do not nutritionally satisfy the larvae. The complex symbiotic relationship with their gut microbiota is essential for catalyzing the breakdown of plastic materials.

Research involving T. molitor larvae has yielded significant insights into the biodegradation processes and has potential applications for managing plastic waste, contributing significantly to ecological sustainability efforts. As model organisms, these larvae have demonstrated an ability to digest microplastics, producing various compounds through metabolic activities, thus aiding in the understanding of biological processes involved in polymer degradation and efforts to mitigate plastic pollution. T. molitor larvae serve as a pivotal biological system in biodegradation studies, particularly in the context of using macroinvertebrates to study the biodegradation processes of both biodegradable and non-biodegradable plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
