      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nasutitermes is a genus of termites with digestive tracts sustaining microbial communities that perform essential ecological functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIROCHAETES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spirochaetes are a family of bacteria playing roles in cellulose degradation and symbiotic nitrogen cycling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spirochaetes are a phylum of bacteria involved in nitrogen fixation and nutrient supply in termite digestive tracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBROBACTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fibrobacters are a family of anaerobic bacteria involved in the degradation of fibrous plant material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fibrobacters are bacteria involved in cellulose degradation within the digestive systems of insects such as termites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACIDOBACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYLUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acidobacteria are a family of bacteria that are often found in soil environments, playing roles in nutrient cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acidobacteria is a phylum detected in low abundance in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acidobacteria is listed as one of the main bacterial classes found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor, involved in its diverse microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acidobacteria is a phylum of bacteria playing roles in nutrient supply and environmental resilience in termite digestive communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMBIOTIC RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symbiotic relationship is an interaction between two different organisms that live close to each other, often benefiting one or both parties through nutrient exchange or habitat provision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Symbiotic relationship is the mutually beneficial interaction between insect larvae and their gut microorganisms, which aids in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18</data>
