    <node id="&quot;CLOSTRIDIUM SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clostridium species are bacteria known for decomposing organic materials such as cellulose and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium species are bacteria known for their roles in fermentation and are predominant in mealworm larvae fed with bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium spp. is found in various diet groups though its load is not specific to PS, contributing to the digestive microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium spp. are anaerobic bacteria identified in larvae, known for decomposing hemicellulose and polyethylene."</data>
