      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Obiales, Verrucomicrobiales, and Xanthomonadales are orders of bacteria referenced in studies regarding their role in certain microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOLBACHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria known for being symbiotic with various insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria known for forming symbiotic relationships with insect hosts, affecting reproductive biology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria known for symbiotic relationships with insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogenase is an enzyme complex responsible for converting atmospheric nitrogen to ammonia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenase is an enzyme whose activity is increased in Pantoee sp. upon inoculation in sugarcane, aiding in nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogenase is an enzyme involved in the fixation of atmospheric nitrogen by symbionts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
