      <data key="d1">"These are trace elements that are necessary for the function of nitrogenase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARABACTEROIDES SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Parabacteroides species are anaerobic bacteria involved in decomposing complex carbohydrates like hemicellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parabacteroides spp. is a genus of anaerobic bacteria involved in decomposing hemicellulose and polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGROBACTERIUM SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agrobacterium species are potential diazotrophic bacteria involved in nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agrobacterium spp. are identified as potential diazotrophic bacteria in polystyrene-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROSOMONAS SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrosomonas species are bacteria involved in ammonia oxidation, part of nitrogen cycling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonas spp. are potential diazotrophic bacteria identified in the microbiota of polystyrene-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROSIRA SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrosira species are bacteria participating in nitrogen cycling within the microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosira spp. are part of the potential diazotrophic community in the microbiota of polystyrene-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMBIOTIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteria that live in symbiosis with their host, promoting nitrogen assimilation for insect survival in nitrogen-deficient environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Symbiotic bacteria live in close association with host organisms, often providing essential metabolic or protective benefits, such as in insect gut systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Symbiotic bacteria are isolated from the mealworms' digestive tract and play a role in polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTERASE ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The enzymatic activity observed to increase in T. molitor larvae fed with polyethylene, involved in the hydrolysis of ester bonds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEXT-GENERATION SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to perform metagenetic analysis by sequencing the DNA of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A modern sequencing technology used to identify bacterial groups participating in waste degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a modern sequencing technology used to explore the diversity of the larval gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-Generation Sequencing is a method used to analyze changes in the gut microbiome associated with the degradation of plastics in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a technology used to investigate changes in the microbial community structure of mealworms based on their plastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is an advanced method used to analyze the gut microbiome of larvae to identify key microbes involved in PP biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiome consists of the microbial community in the guts of insect larvae, crucial for the biodegradation of polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome in the mealworm intestinal gut likely plays a role in digesting plastics and may influence detoxification processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the community of microorganisms, including bacteria, fungi, and viruses, living in the digestive tracts of the larvae, influencing PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome here refers to the collection of microorganisms within the mealworm gut, affected by different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;The microbiome in the context of Tenebrio molitor, commonly known as mealworms, refers to the diverse community of microorganisms residing within their digestive tract. This community plays a crucial role in the mealworms' physiological and biochemical processes, aiding in digestion, nutrient synthesis, and influencing health outcomes. The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae is particularly notable for its involvement in the biodegradation of materials such as polystyrene (PS) and low-density polyethylene (LDPE), showcasing efficient metabolic pathways capable of breaking down these plastics. The composition of this microbial community changes in response to different dietary treatments, such as bran, polystyrene, and low-density polyethylene, impacting the larvae's digestion and survival. This microbiome includes various species of bacteria, fungi, and viruses, and it is understood to adapt depending on the mealworms' diet, underscoring its role in waste degradation and nutrient absorption. Overall, the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor stands as a significant aspect of their biology, contributing to their potential capabilities in environmental biodegradation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome in mealworm guts is involved in digesting plastics, influencing mass change during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in the insect gut and playing a critical role in PS biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in a specific environment, such as the gut of mealworms, which can be affected by diet and environmental changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The community of microorganisms found in the digestive tracts of the larvae studied, affected by their diet and exposure to plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome of mealworms, which may influence their ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome refers to the microbial communities in the digestive tract of T. molitor larvae, involved in waste degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372aa232f6e8aad1d8e0a93f16a42b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
