      <data key="d0">"MICROBIAL COMMUNITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nitrogen-fixing community involves microorganisms converting nitrogen into a biologically usable form, essential in ecosystems like those associated with termites."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nitrogen-fixing community refers to a group of microorganisms that collaborate in converting atmospheric nitrogen to a form usable by host organisms, such as dry-wood termites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3</data>
