      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marine Environment refers to oceanic ecosystems where microplastics can accumulate and persist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marine environment encompasses the ecological settings found in oceans and seas, susceptible to pollution from polymeric materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The marine environment refers to the oceans and seas, which are habitats for diverse organisms and are affected by pollution such as microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marine Environment refers to the oceans and seas where organisms like Blue Mussel Mytilus edulis L. encounter and interact with pollutants such as microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The marine environment refers to oceanic and sea areas, potentially threatened by materials such as drifting polymers."</data>
