    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER ASBURIAE YT1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biodegradable PE strain isolated from the intestine of Indian meal moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from waxworm gut, known for its capacity to degrade polyethylene films at notable rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is an LDPE-degrading bacterium found in insects known for its plastic degradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a gut bacterium that can degrade approximately 6.1% of LDPE films after 60 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of waxworms, capable of degrading polyethylene (PE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a strain capable of degrading polyethylene, demonstrated to decompose LDPE film."</data>
