    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIALLY EXPRESSED GENES (DEGS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEGs are genes that show different levels of expression when mealworms are fed on different diets, highlighting changes due to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentially expressed genes (DEGs) are genes showing significant differences in expression levels under varying conditions, such as changes noted in larvae with different PP diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes that show differential expression in T. molitor larvae when fed with PP polymers compared to a wheat bran diet, showing up-regulation associated with digestive and degradation functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes whose expression varies significantly between different experimental conditions such as PS, CS, and CB diets; analyzed using volcano and heat maps."</data>
