    <node id="&quot;RT-PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RT-PCR (Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a technique used to amplify and quantify RNA sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR, or reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction, is a laboratory technique used to measure RNA expression levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real-time PCR, a laboratory technique used for detecting and quantifying RNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction (RT-PCR) is a laboratory technique used to measure RNA levels, validating expression levels of enzymes involved in metabolism under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR is a laboratory technique used to amplify and analyze the expression of specific genes, in this case, the nifH gene in gut microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252</data>
    </node>
