      <data key="d2">chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOSTATISTICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to analyze differences among group means and their associated procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) is a statistical method used to identify differentially expressed genes (DEG) and analyze variance between groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-way analysis of variance, a statistical method used to test differences between means for statistical significance."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method used to analyze the variance among group means, applied in the experiment to compare plastic consumption data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Analysis of variance used to evaluate the differences in protein, sugar, and lipid content across samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) is a statistical method used to analyze differences among group means, utilized here to determine significance of experimental results."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or Analysis of Variance, is a statistical method used to compare differences between group means in an experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Analysis of Variance (ANOVA) is a statistical method used to analyze the differences among group means in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method used to determine the significant differences in various experimental measurements such as extraction rates and plastic removal efficiencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is used to evaluate the differences in survival indices among mealworm groups in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </node>
