    <node id="&quot;3-KETOACYL-COA THIOLASE (KAT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3-Ketoacyl-CoA Thiolase (KAT) is an enzyme involved in fatty acid metabolism, catalyzing the thiolytic cleavage of 3-ketoacyl-CoA."&lt;SEP&gt;"KAT (EC 2.3.1.16, 2.3.1.9) is an enzyme that catalyzes a key reaction in the β-oxidation of fatty acids, typically acting downstream in the metabolic pathway."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
