    <node id="&quot;BEESWAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-chain hydrocarbon that can be metabolized by Galleria mellonella independent of its microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a common component in hydrocarbon chains and was used as a feed in the study, affecting gene expression related to carboxylesterase and lipase families."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a long-chain hydrocarbon that Galleria mellonella can metabolize without microbial assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a product from beehives, used in studies to compare the effects on gene expression when fed to organisms alongside or instead of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A natural substance that certain insect larvae can digest and suggests potential for plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A natural lipid consisting of long-chain carbon atoms, which Achroia grisella larvae have evolved to digest, similar in chemical structure to polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a substance made by honey bees for raising larvae and storing honey and pollen, forming the structure of waxcomb."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is used to feed G. mellonella larvae as a control diet in experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798</data>
    </node>
