      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-Acetyltransferase (NAT) refers to enzymes involved in the transfer of an acetyl group to a substrate, playing an important role in drug metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"N-acetyltransferase (NAT, EC 2.3.1.5) is an enzyme that catalyzes the acetylation of aryl amines, playing a role in isoniazid metabolism."</data>
