    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCBI&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCBI provides access to genetic information, which can be utilized in Gene Ontology resources for biological data annotation."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI, or National Center for Biotechnology Information, provides bioinformatics tools and databases, utilized here for primer design and sequence analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is a repository where the study's datasets are made available."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is an organization that hosts a large database of nucleotide sequences and other genomic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) provides access to biomedical and genomic information, where the FASTA sequence was blasted against nucleotide sequences in GenBank."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCBI, or the National Center for Biotechnology Information, is a resource for data such as microbial diversity and metatranscriptomic sequences."</data>
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species of bacteria isolated from Tenebrio molitor's gut, capable of degrading polystyrene. Identified strains include NBRC 102593, ATCC 13182, and JCM 1665."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterial species that has been isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor and is studied for its potential to degrade polystyrene through the presence of the alkB gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterial strain involved in the degradation of plastics, particularly polystyrene, using it as a carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor that contains the alkB gene, contributing to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterial strain under study, with an ATCC 13182 variant that contains the alkB gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strains of this bacterium, such as ATCC 13182, JCM 1665, and NBRC 102593, are targeted for identification and analysis through PCR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca (9A) is another bacterial strain capable of plastic biodegradation, as indicated by clear zones in select media assays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium found in the gut of mealworms responsible for biodegrading plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium examined in microbiome studies with insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shows up to 12.97% biodegradation in PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is found in mealworms' intestines, known for digesting polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKB GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The AlkB gene is a gene found in various bacteria, used in research for phylogenetic analysis and evolutionary studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The AlkB gene is associated with the degradation of alkanes, and in this context, it is linked to the ability of Klebsiella oxytoca strains to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene encodes for alkane-1-monoxygenase, an enzyme involved in the oxidation of inactivated alkanes. It may be a marker for bacteria's ability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene is a specific gene sequence involved in the oxidation of alkanes, which was amplified in Klebsiella oxytoca strains using specific primers in PCR testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkane-1-monooxygenase gene, involved in the degradation of alkanes, detected in Klebsiella oxytoca strains through specific primer amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The alkB gene is identified as important in alkane biodegradation during polyethylene breakdown in Pseudomonas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKANE-1-MONOXYGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkane-1-monoxygenase is an enzyme found in higher abundance in polypropylene-fed larvae, with potential functions in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkane-1-monoxygenase is an enzyme involved in the oxidation of inactivated alkanes, potentially responsible for polystyrene degradation, and encoded by the alkB gene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RIBOSOMAL RNA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene commonly used as a molecular marker in microbiology, utilized here to identify different strains of Klebsiella oxytoca through PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gene used to confirm the identity of Klebsiella oxytoca strains, critical for bacterial phylogenetic studies due to its highly conserved nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific gene sequence targeted for amplification to identify bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is used in the identification and phylogenetic analysis of bacteria, confirming the presence of Klebsiella oxytoca among the isolated strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequencing was used to identify the bacterial strains within T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequencing is used in the study to identify bacterial isolates in the gut of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANGER SEQUENCING TECHNIQUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sanger sequencing technique is a method used to determine the sequence of nucleotides in DNA, applied here to sequence the alkB gene from Klebsiella oxytoca."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (PCR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A molecular biology technique used to amplify DNA sequences, utilized in this study for the identification of bacterial isolates in mealworm guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technique used to amplify 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequences to identify specific strains of Klebsiella oxytoca."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a molecular technique used to amplify DNA sequences, employed in this study to confirm the presence of Klebsiella oxytoca by targeting the 16S ribosomal RNA gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technique used to amplify DNA sequences, in this case, the 16S rRNA regions for subsequent analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a method used for amplifying DNA segments, including those of the gut microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a technique used to amplify segments of DNA, allowing for the identification of microorganisms through their genetic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is utilized to amplify the DNA of the lesser waxworms for sequencing and further genetic analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALINE WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sterile solution used to suspend gut contents for microbial analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline water, used in this study, helps to cleanse alcohol from mealworms and causes osmosis-induced death by its salt content, preparing samples for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
