      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERRATIA MARCESCENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium identified among gut microorganisms aiding in polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a strain associated with hydrocarbon degradation and found in PS-degrading mealworm gut microbiomes, though incapable of PS degradation when isolated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is one of the bacterial species isolated from the intestines of T. molitor, shown to be effective in biodegrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens (6A) is a bacterial strain studied for its plastic biodegradation abilities, as demonstrated through media assays showing clear zones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterium for microbiome study in context of PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterium studied for its role in breaking down plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is a bacterium associated with PS biodegradation in insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is an identified strain in mealworms, used for EPS degradation tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia marcescens is one of the species capable of degrading polystyrene in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041</data>
    </node>
