      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific strain of Klebsiella oxytoca identified using JCM-specific primers through PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca JCM 1665 is a particular strain identified and isolated in the study from the gut of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca JCM 1665 is a bacterial strain identified from isolate number 4 in Tenebrio molitor's gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca JCM 1665 is another strain of gram-negative bacterium present in Tenebrio molitor's gut, contributing to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca JCM 1665 is another strain of the bacterium closely related to K. pneumoniae and present in the mealworm's gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA ATCC 13182&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A strain of Klebsiella oxytoca identified using ATCC-specific primers during PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is a strain of Klebsiella oxytoca isolated from T. molitor, potentially involved in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is a strain of bacterium with a specific nucleotide sequence identified and studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is a gram-negative bacterium isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, potentially responsible for the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is a specific strain of the gram-negative bacterium identified in the mealworm's gut with polystyrene-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is one of the bacterial strains isolated from T. molitor gut, capable of biodegrading polystyrene."</data>
