      <data key="d2">chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC TREE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 16S RNA gene-based neighbor-joining phylogenetic tree is constructed to visualize the genetic relationships of strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"A branching diagram or tree showing the inferred evolutionary relationships among various biological species based on their genetic characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A diagram representing the evolutionary relationships among various bacterial strains derived from mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree constructed using the maximum likelihood method and Tamura-Nei model to analyze relationships between genetic sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree is constructed in the study to depict the evolutionary relationships of the alkB gene among different bacterial species."&lt;SEP&gt;"A diagram used to illustrate evolutionary relationships among various biological species based on similarities and differences in their genetic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree is used to illustrate the evolutionary relationships among various biological species or entities, including the isolates from the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree is a branching diagram showing evolutionary relationships, here used to depict the lineage of the Lac640 protein."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Phylogenetic Tree is a diagram showing the evolutionary relationships among various biological species based on their genetic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic Tree is a representation of evolutionary relationships constructed using sequence data from bacterial strains to visualize genetic similarities and differences."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree is constructed to determine the taxonomic relationships of bacterial strains based on 16S rRNA sequencing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A diagram representing evolutionary relationships among species, used in the classification and study of Achroia grisella."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phylogenetic tree is used in the study to show the evolutionary relationships between the different strains of bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1</data>
    </node>
