    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to study the evolutionary relationships among the nitrogen-fixing bacteria based on genetic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scientific procedure to study the evolutionary relationships between organisms using genetic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic Analysis examines the evolutionary relationships between the alkB genes from Klebsiella oxytoca and other bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic Analysis is a scientific process used to infer the evolutionary relationships between different organisms or genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis involves studying the evolutionary relationships between species using molecular sequencing data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic Analysis is a scientific approach used to evaluate evolutionary relationships among species or groups, such as non-symbiotic endophytic fungi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis involves sequencing and comparing 16S rRNA genes for determining bacterial relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis involves the study of the evolutionary relationships among biological entities using sequence data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is a process used to determine evolutionary relationships among the bacterial cells using 16S rRNA sequences in the context of polystyrene degradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is used to determine the evolutionary relationships of the isolated bacteria using 16S rRNA sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8f385513fcff2125529486530ad5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450</data>
    </node>
