      <data key="d1">"AlkB is a gene from various bacteria used for phylogenetic analysis. It is involved in determining evolutionary relationships using nucleotide sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is a hydroxylating enzyme involved in the initial hydroxylation of polyethylene during its biodegradation process."</data>
