    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF ZIMBABWE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Zimbabwe provided resources and acknowledgment support for the study on plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation Process refers to the natural process by which organic substances are broken down by living organisms, in this context by mealworms breaking down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process involves the breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms such as Klebsiella oxytoca and T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process involves the breakdown of plastic materials by mealworms and their gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown of plastics and polystyrene by biological means, explored through the use of mealworms under controlled conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which mealworms, particularly T. molitor, degrade polystyrene into simpler substances, aided by the bacterial community in their guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process discussed involves bacterial action on PS films, leading to mass loss, surface erosion, and chemical modifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process involves the breakdown of plastics by microbial action, including both fungi and bacteria in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of biodegradation involves breaking down plastics like PP through depolymerization, oxidation, and mineralization, challenging due to PP's hydrophobic hydrocarbons and methyl groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation process refers to the breakdown of organic and inorganic substances by microorganisms, crucial for understanding environmental degradation mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation process studied is the breakdown of plastics like PS and LDPE by mealworms, facilitated by digestive biofragmentation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b</data>
    </node>
