    <node id="&quot;HYDROCARBONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrocarbons are organic compounds consisting entirely of hydrogen and carbon, commonly found as components of fossil fuels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are organic compounds consisting entirely of hydrogen and carbon, utilized by certain microorganisms in various processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are organic compounds made entirely of hydrogen and carbon, and are the primary components of fossil fuels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are organic compounds that were identified in connection with the presence of polystyrene and its degradation through mealworm activity, indicating a chemical change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are organic compounds made exclusively of carbon and hydrogen, often serving as substrates for microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic compounds consisting entirely of hydrogen and carbon, often targeted in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons with longer carbon chains are identified in the study, indicating chemical transformations occurring during the biodegradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons in polyethylene are subject to biodegradation processes, leading to their breakdown and integration into waxworm biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA POLYMORPHISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA polymorphism refers to the variation in DNA sequences among individuals within a population, which can be used for studying genetic diversity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGHER PLANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Higher plants, also known as vascular plants, possess specialized tissue (xylem and phloem) for transporting water and nutrients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC SIGNAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phylogenetic signal refers to the tendency of related species to resemble each other more than they resemble species drawn at random from a phylogenetic tree."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRAL EVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Viral evolution describes the genetic changes in viruses over time, often characterized by high rates of mutation and rapid adaptation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOST PHENOTYPIC EVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Host phenotypic evolution refers to changes in the observable traits of a host organism in response to environmental pressures, including interaction with pathogens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEQUENCE BLASTING&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
      <data key="d1">"The FASTA sequence was blasted against nucleotide sequences in NCBI's GenBank to identify similarities and gather genetic information."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA STRAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCR was applied to identify multiple Klebsiella oxytoca strains using different specific primers targeting genetic markers."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein is a key nutrient identified as influencing the growth and development of larvae in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein is a macronutrient essential for the human body, which can be sourced from various insects like Tenebrio molitor, Alphitobius diaperinus, and Hermetia illucens, studied for their high protein levels."&lt;SEP&gt;PROTEIN is a critical macronutrient essential for body functions, consisting of large biomolecules formed by long chains of amino acid residues. It plays a vital role in various biological processes, including cellular growth, repair, and enzymatic functions, as well as the structure, function, and regulation of the body's tissues. Within the context of Tenebrio molitor, or yellow mealworms, PROTEIN accounts for a significant portion of their nutritional composition, specifically 65.41% in TMlp, and is recognized as a high-content, sustainable alternative protein source.

Studies have measured PROTEIN content in insect biomass, particularly in yellow mealworms, under different diet conditions to assess their nutritional value and potential as food sources. The Kjeldahl method and protein-dye binding techniques are used to determine PROTEIN content, offering a measure of nutritional adequacy. Changes in dietary intake, such as the consumption of polystyrene and Styrofoam, affect PROTEIN levels, often altering the nutritional composition of the larvae. Mealworms fed a Styrofoam diet are noted for higher PROTEIN content compared to a conventional diet, although PROTEIN content might decrease due to possible stress or metabolic changes when polystyrene is consumed, indicating the impact of plastic-only diets. Despite these changes, the high PROTEIN content in mealworms, along with their economic potential, reinforces their suitability as a novel and sustainable nutrition source.&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein is a vital nutritional component synthesized from fixed nitrogen in mealworms, illustrating the conversion of atmospheric nitrogen into biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein levels in larvae were measured in the study, using the Bradford method to assess the biochemical changes from plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins in mealworms' tissues are essential for their metabolism and building bodily structures, varying in content depending on diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are crucial for body functioning and can be used as an energy source during starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINO ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amino acids are metabolites observed as new peaks in NMR spectra, indicating biochemical transformations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are organic compounds found in yeast, necessary for mealworm protein synthesis and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are organic compounds that combine to form proteins, essential for various bodily functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are organic compounds that combine to form proteins. Tenebrio molitor contains abundant essential amino acids, such as threonine, valine, histidine, and lysine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids produced by fungi may contribute to nutrition under stringent conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are vital components needed for protein synthesis and overall development, which are not provided by PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids like isobutyric and isovaleric acid are products of SCGB1 metabolism, highlighting nutritional components in microbial processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are organic compounds that appear as residues or by-products in frass samples, indicating protein presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are organic compounds that combine to form proteins and may be involved in the physiological processes of the mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNSATURATED FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unsaturated fatty acids are a type of fat that can influence bacterial communication systems, including inhibiting motility and biofilm formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unsaturated fatty acids are a type of healthy fat found in various food sources, important for heart health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unsaturated fatty acids are beneficial fats for human health, present abundantly in Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unsaturated fatty acids are fatty acids with at least one double bond, beneficial for heart health and found in various foods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Essential inorganic substances not efficiently provided by PET, necessary for the long-term growth and development of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals are inorganic elements needed for numerous bodily processes, including building bones and producing hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals are inorganic nutrients required for various bodily functions. Tenebrio molitor is rich in minerals such as calcium and magnesium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMLP W/ EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMlp W/ eps refers to Tenebrio molitor larvae powder prepared with expanded polystyrene, used in studies to evaluate its safety and application as an alternative protein source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMLP W/O EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMlp W/o eps refers to Tenebrio molitor larvae powder prepared without expanded polystyrene, used as a comparison in studies assessing the product's effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPRAGUE-DAWLEY RATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A strain of laboratory rats used in scientific research to study effects on organ systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sprague-Dawley Rats are a breed of rats commonly used in laboratory studies. They were used in vivo to assess the toxicity of Tenebrio molitor larvae powder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN-DEPENDENT MCF-7 CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCF-7 Cells are a breast cancer cell line sensitive to estrogen, used to investigate the estrogen response to Tenebrio molitor larvae powder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BROILER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANIMAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Broilers are chickens raised specifically for meat production. They are one of the animal species that can benefit from Tenebrio molitor as an alternative protein source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANIMAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pigs are commonly raised livestock, and Tenebrio molitor is considered a viable alternative protein source for pig feed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOYBEAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLANT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soybean is a plant source of protein, traditionally used in animal feed. Tenebrio molitor provides more essential amino acids than soybean, making it a superior alternative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EUROPEAN FOOD SAFETY AUTHORITY (EFSA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The EFSA is responsible for assessing food safety in Europe. They validated mealworms, including Tenebrio molitor, as safe to consume as edible insects in 2021."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DROUGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drought refers to a prolonged period of deficient rainfall, challenging environmental conditions which Tenebrio molitor is adapted to withstand."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE VARIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature variation, including both high and low extremes, is a challenging environmental condition that Tenebrio molitor can adapt to."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estrogen response involves the reaction of cells to the hormone estrogen. It is studied in Tenebrio molitor larvae powder to assess potential hormonal activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOXYLIN AND EOSIN STAINING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematoxylin and Eosin staining is a common technique in histology to reveal tissue structure. It was used in studies with Sprague-Dawley Rats to assess organ tissues after TMlp administration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODY WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body weight here refers to the changes in weight observed in the larvae depending on the diet—starvation, PVC, or bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body weight is a measure of an organism's health and was monitored in Sprague-Dawley Rats as part of the toxicological assessment of TMlp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body weight is a primary measure used to assess health and growth in experimental animals during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body weight refers to the mass of the body, examined as a potential response to dietary administration, showing no significant difference between groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN WEIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ weights are measured post-study to determine the physical and metabolic impact of dietary interventions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ weights refer to the absolute and relative measurements of various organs to assess physiological changes resulting from dietary administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ weights refer to the measurement of organ masses, which were used as a health indicator in Sprague-Dawley Rats during the TMlp study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The absolute and relative weights of various organs (liver, kidney, adrenal gland, heart, thymus, testes, lung, spleen) were measured to assess the physical impact of TMlp in rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THREONINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Threonine is an essential amino acid important for protein synthesis and metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VALINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Valine is a branched-chain essential amino acid involved in muscle metabolism and tissue repair."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valine is an amino acid involved in metabolism pathways enriched in mealworms consuming PVC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTIDINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Histidine is an essential amino acid important for growth and tissue repair, and is a precursor for histamine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYSINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lysine is an essential amino acid crucial for growth and muscle turnover, and aids in calcium absorption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALCIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical element which was quantified using standards in the ion analysis procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is a mineral crucial for bone health, nerve transmission, and muscle function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is one of the minerals measured in mealworm frass to evaluate changes due to polystyrene consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGNESIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical element that was assessed and quantified during the analytical process for cations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnesium is a mineral involved in various biochemical processes, measured in the frass of polystyrene-fed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnesium is essential for many biochemical reactions, including energy production and muscle contractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR L. POWDER (TMLP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMlp is a powder form of the yellow mealworm and has potential as a safe food ingredient."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPRAGUE DAWLEY (SD) RATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sprague Dawley rats are a commonly used laboratory rat strain for in vivo experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN UTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein utilization refers to the body's ability to digest and use dietary protein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE MONOMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrene Monomer is a chemical unit used to produce polystyrene in EPS, impacting the structure and properties of the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene monomer is the raw material used in the production of polystyrene through polymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene monomer is a chemical used in graft modifications to improve the degradability of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a14229bceb339a4ca1baf0772b47ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIOXINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dioxins are a group of chemically related compounds that are persistent environmental pollutants and can be harmful to health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dioxins are carcinogenic substances potentially released during the burning of PVC and other plastic wastes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dioxins are harmful compounds released into the environment during the disposal of EPS through traditional methods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estrogen is a hormone involved in the regulation of the female reproductive system and secondary sexual characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED FLOUR BEETLE (TRIBOLIUM CASTANEUM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A kind of beetle reported to degrade Styrofoam as part of plastic waste management research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red flour beetle is an insect species investigated for its potential to biodegrade plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERWORM (ZOPHOBAS MORIO L.)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superworm is a larval stage insect explored for its ability to biodegrade synthetic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DARK MEALWORM (TENEBRIO OBSCURUS L.)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dark mealworm is known for potential applications in biodegradation and sustainable protein sources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW MEALWORM (TENEBRIO MOLITOR L.)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow mealworm is recognized for its applications in sustainable protein supply and biodegrading plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excrement of mealworms used in experiments to analyze biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Frass is the waste product generated by mealworms, used to assess the extent of mask degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm Frass is a byproduct of mealworms that has potential uses as a biofertilizer and can improve crop growth and soil properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass has a lower proportion of rooting and loss in height and is less effective at retaining moisture compared to superworm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass is a by-product of insect farming that can be used as a fertilizer, impacting crop growth and soil properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass is the waste material excreted by mealworms containing broken-down material."&lt;SEP&gt;"The excrement produced by mealworm larvae, processed to extract plastic remnants for analysis after the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass is the waste produced by mealworms, analyzed for its effects on the growth and rooting of cacti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass is the byproduct of mealworms, containing nitrogen and organic material, potentially useful as a fertilizer in sustainable agricultural practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass is the waste product of mealworms, which has potential use as a fertilizer affecting crop growth and soil properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VIVO TOXICOLOGICAL SAFETY EVALUATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In Vivo Toxicological Safety Evaluations assess the safety of substances within living organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCF-7 CANCER CELL LINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCF-7 is a breast cancer cell line used for scientific research and studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KONGJU NATIONAL UNIVERSITY INSTITUTIONAL ANIMAL CARE AND USE COMMITTEE (KNU-IACUC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KNU-IACUC is responsible for ensuring ethical approval and overseeing the experimental procedures involving animals."&lt;SEP&gt;"KNU-IACUC provides guidelines and oversight for animal experiments at Kongju National University."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCRINE-DISRUPTING CHEMICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endocrine-disrupting chemicals are substances that can cause developmental effects in humans and wildlife by interfering with hormonal functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine-disrupting chemicals are substances that can interfere with the endocrine (hormonal) systems, potentially causing developmental, reproductive, and immune problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VIVO EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In vivo experiments involve the testing of substances on living organisms to assess their effects and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"In vivo experiments refer to tests conducted on living rats to evaluate the toxicological safety of mealworm powder when combined with EPS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VITRO TOXICOLOGICAL SAFETY EVALUATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In vitro toxicological safety evaluations are laboratory-based tests conducted to assess the safety and effects of substances on isolated cells or tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FETAL BOVINE SERUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fetal bovine serum is a common supplement used in cell culture media to provide essential nutrients for cell growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RPMI 1640&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RPMI 1640 is a culture medium used for growing cells, providing essential nutrients required for cell growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"RPMI 1640 is a type of cell culture medium used to grow various types of cells under laboratory conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOREAN CELL LINE BANK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Korean Cell Line Bank is an organization that provides cell lines, such as the MCF-7 breast cancer cell line, for research purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Korean Cell Line Bank is the source from which the MCF-7 breast cancer cell line was purchased for use in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION AND MINERALIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation and mineralization describe the breakdown of organic substances into simpler forms and their conversion into inorganic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation and mineralization refer to the biological processes by which organic substances are broken down and incorporated into mineral forms within the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD SAFETY EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food safety evaluation involves testing food products to ensure they are safe for consumption, focusing on toxicological and nutritional factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN SOURCE IN LIVESTOCK FEED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Using insects like Tenebrio molitor L. as a protein source in livestock feed offers an economical and sustainable alternative to traditional feed sources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTION AND DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproduction and development processes are critical for the continuation and growth of living organisms, influenced by hormonal and environmental factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCF-7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELL LINE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCF-7 is a breast cancer cell line used in the experiment, cultured under specific conditions to maintain viable and proliferating cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FETAL BOVINE SERUM (FBS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FBS is a component of cell culture medium that provides growth factors and nutrients to support cell proliferation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STREPTOMYCIN/PENICILLIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Streptomycin/penicillin is used in cell culture medium to prevent bacterial contamination during cell growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHATE-BUFFERED SALINE (PBS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PBS is used to wash cells during cell culture and is a buffer solution that maintains a constant pH."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBS is utilized during cell culture for washing cell cultures and maintaining pH balance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRYPSIN-EDTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trypsin-EDTA is used to detach adherent cells from the culture flask surface for passaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;17-Β ESTRADIOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"17-β estradiol is a form of estrogen used to study its effects on cell proliferation during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3-(4,5-DIMETHYLTHIAZOL-2-YL)-2,5-DIPHENYLTETRAZOLIUM BROMIDE (MTT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MTT is used in assays to assess cell viability by measuring metabolic activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR L.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species of mealworm known for eating plastic and hosting a nitrogen-fixing community of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio Molitor L., belonging to the Tenebrionidae family, is commonly known as the mealworm beetle, a species often used in biological studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L. refers to the species of mealworm that potentially biodegrades expanded polystyrene due to actions of intestinal microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L., also known as mealworm, is used in experiments as a dietary supplement without adverse effects on growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L., commonly known as yellow mealworm, is an insect species rich in protein and capable of biodegrading expanded polystyrene (EPS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor, known as the yellow mealworm, is used to prepare larvae powder for experimental purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L., commonly known as the mealworm, is an insect used in experiments to study the effects of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L., also known as the yellow mealworm, is an insect species used in studies for its ability to degrade PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L., commonly known as the mealworm beetle, is often used in scientific research for studying various biological processes, including plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L. are plastic-eating mealworms involved in nitrogen fixation and the diazotrophic community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L. is a mealworm known for its ability to consume and degrade plastic, aided by symbiotic gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor L., commonly known as the yellow mealworm, is proposed as a source of animal protein for humans in bioregenerative life support systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIMETHYL SULFOXIDE (DMSO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DMSO is a solvent used to dissolve formazan crystals for measurement purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"DMSO is a solvent used to dissolve the concentrated TMlp extract for further experimental application."&lt;SEP&gt;"DMSO is used as a solvent for the final TMlp extract before it is used in experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"DMSO is used as a solvent to dissolve formazan crystals in the MTT assay for cell viability measurement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL VIABILITY ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell viability analysis measures the health and proliferation rate of cells using the MTT assay."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WELGENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Welgene is the supplier of RPMI 1640, the culture medium used for growing MCF-7 cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIBCO BRL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gibco BRL manufactures the fetal bovine serum and antibiotics used in the cell culture medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOSESANG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biosesang supplies the phosphate-buffered saline used to wash the cell cultures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGMA-ALDRICH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sigma-Aldrich is the supplier of 17-β estradiol and MTT reagent used in the experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The supplier of Extract-N-Amp PCR ReadyMix, used in PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sigma-Aldrich supplied \(\alpha{ }^{13} \mathrm{C}\)- and \(\beta{ }^{13} \mathrm{C}\)-labeled PS samples for the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INC. MCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inc. MCE is the company supporting the preparation of Tenebrio molitor larvae powder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KEIL is the supplier from which Tenebrio molitor L. were purchased for the experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOMACHINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Komachine provides the high-pressure steam sterilizer and hot-air oven used in processing Tenebrio molitor larvae powder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEQUIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lequip produced the low-temperature compressor utilized for oil extraction from Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;75 CM² CELL CULTURE FLASK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 75 cm² cell culture flask is used for thawing and culturing the MCF-7 cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOT-AIR OVEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hot-air oven is used to dry the Tenebrio molitor larvae powder at 80-85°C for several hours."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROTARY VACUUM CONCENTRATOR (EYELA N-1000)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The rotary vacuum concentrator is used to concentrate the TMlp extract under reduced pressure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO2 INCUBATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A CO2 incubator is used to maintain cell cultures at 37°C with 5% CO2 for optimal growth conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HDPE BOXES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-density polyethylene (HDPE) boxes are used to house and breed Tenebrio molitor in controlled conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PULVERIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pulverizer is employed to pulverize the residue of Tenebrio molitor larvae into powder after oil extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic activity is assessed through the MTT assay to determine cell viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic activity refers to the biochemical processes that occur within organisms, particularly those related to the degradation of PS in T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL PROLIFERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell Proliferation is the process by which cells grow and divide, crucial in understanding cancer cell dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cell proliferation is stimulated or inhibited by the addition of 17-β estradiol and measured in cell culture experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FASTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fasting is applied to Tenebrio molitor before processing into powder to ensure the discharge of EPS from their intestines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPS FEED BLOCKS (FBS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EPS feed blocks serve as a dietary component in the experimental diet of Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MTT SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MTT solution is a chemical product used to measure cell viability in the experiment by producing formazan that is soluble in DMSO."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DMSO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used as a solvent to dissolve formazan produced by MTT solution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELISA READER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ELISA reader is an analytical device used to measure absorbance at 595 nm to quantify formazan production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SD RATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SD, or Sprague-Dawley, rats are used as the experimental animals to study oral dosage toxicity and related biological measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sprague-Dawley rats are a strain of albino rats used frequently in biomedical research, including this particular study assessing toxicological impacts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMLP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMlp refers to mealworm powder fed with expanded polystyrene evaluated for its effects on rats in an experimental study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KONGJU NATIONAL UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kongju National University is the location where the animal facility and experimental studies are conducted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NARA BIOTECH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nara Biotech is the company from which the Sprague-Dawley rats were purchased for experimental use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALANINE TRANSAMINASE (ALT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALT is an enzyme measured in serum biochemical analysis to evaluate liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPARTATE AMINOTRANSFERASE (AST)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AST is an enzyme found in various tissues, important for assessing liver damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"AST is an enzyme measured in serum biochemical analysis, important for assessing liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE (ALP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALP is an enzyme measured in serum biochemical analysis, indicative of liver, bone, or bile duct conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"ALP is an enzyme related to bile ducts, often measured to evaluate liver and bone conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAMMA GLUTAMYL TRANSPEPTIDASE (Γ-GTP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"γ-GTP is an enzyme measured in serum biochemical tests related to liver and bile duct function."&lt;SEP&gt;"γ-GTP is an enzyme measured in the study, often used as a biomarker for liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM POWDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm Powder refers to the powdered form of mealworms used in this study, particularly noting its effects on organisms when fed with or without expanded polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm Powder, derived from Tenebrio molitor L., is used as a dietary component in animal feed experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm powder is a product derived from Tenebrio molitor and used to enhance the nutritional quality of food products such as acorn mook and garaedduk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENTAL ANIMALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experimental animals, specifically SD rats, are used in this study to assess toxicological and physiological responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD CONSUMPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food consumption is monitored to assess dietary impact and overall health of the experimental animals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOLOGICAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
