      <data key="d1">"Polycarbonate bottles are used in the experiment to provide water to the rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOXYLIN AND EOSIN (H&amp;E)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"H&amp;E is a dye used for staining tissue sections for histopathological examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"H&amp;E staining is a method used for examining tissue sections to identify histological changes in larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE POWDER (TMLP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMlp is a powder derived from Tenebrio molitor larvae, used as a dietary supplement and alternative protein source."&lt;SEP&gt;"TMlp is a powder derived from expanded-polystyrene-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae, evaluated for its components such as proteins, fats, and minerals, and its potential as livestock feed."&lt;SEP&gt;"TMlp is a product derived from Tenebrio molitor larvae and is used to test its effects on organ weights and cell viability in rats."&lt;SEP&gt;"TMlp is derived from mealworms and used in the study to evaluate potential health effects and estrogen activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED-POLYSTYRENE-FED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method of feeding Tenebrio molitor larvae with expanded polystyrene to produce a specific type of larvae powder used for various analyses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRUDE FAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crude fat constitutes 19.92% of the TMlp composition, contributing to its caloric and nutritional value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude fat is a measure of total fat content in larvae, lower in plastic-only diets compared to bran-fed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude fat is used as a measure in the study to analyze nutritional changes in the larvae's biomass based on various diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude fat measurement illustrates the accumulation of fat in the larvae under various polyethylene diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCF-7 CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCF-7 cells are a line of human breast cancer cells used for in vitro experiments to study cell viability and estrogenic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"MCF-7 cells are an estrogen-dependent breast cancer cell line used to test the effects of TMlp extract on cell viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"MCF-7 is an estrogen-dependent cell line used in viability assays to test the effects of TMlp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E2 is an estrogen hormone used in experiments to determine its effects on MCF-7 cell line proliferation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MTT ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MTT Assay is a colorimetric assay for assessing cell metabolic activity and used in this study to determine cell viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"MTT assay is a test used to measure the viability of MCF-7 cells after TMlp exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MTT assay is utilized to assess the viability of MCF-7 cells treated with various concentrations of TMlp extract."&lt;SEP&gt;"MTT assay is a colorimetric assay for assessing cell metabolic activity and viability, used here to measure the impact of mealworm extracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"MTT assay measures cell metabolism by converting MTT to formazan, indicating cell viability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXIN PRESENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Assessment of toxic elements such as aflatoxins and heavy metals in TMlp, reported as either not detected or in minimal amounts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
