      <data key="d2">chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rats are used for in vivo testing to assess the effects of TMlp on organ weights and other biological responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The liver is a large organ responsible for detoxification, protein synthesis, and other vital functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The liver is one of the organs investigated in the study, showing no histopathological abnormalities under dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The liver is one of the organs whose weights were measured to determine the effects of TMlp on rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The kidney is included in organ weight measurements to assess the effects of TMlp in rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The adrenal gland is one of the organs whose weight was measured in the study to determine the effects of TMlp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The heart is an organ responsible for pumping blood throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The heart was one of the organs studied, with its weight measured to assess TMlp effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYMUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The thymus is an organ involved in the development of the immune system, particularly T-cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thymus organ weight was measured in the study to evaluate the impact of TMlp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The testes are reproductive organs that produce sperm and hormones, particularly testosterone."&lt;SEP&gt;"The testes were evaluated for weight differences in the study to assess TMlp's influence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lung is another organ whose weight was measured to observe the effects of TMlp."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lungs are organs responsible for gas exchange, specifically taking in oxygen and expelling carbon dioxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPLEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGAN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The spleen is an organ involved in filtering blood and managing blood cells as part of the immune system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen showed significant differences in both absolute and relative weight between the W/o eps and W/ eps groups, potentially linked to physiological factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen's weight was a focus in measuring relative and absolute changes under TMlp treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUTROPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neutrophils are a type of immune cell measured for changes in response to TMlp diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neutrophils are a type of white blood cell that increased in the W/ eps 10% group compared to W/o eps 10% group, indicating a possible immune response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neutrophils are a type of white blood cell, crucial for fighting infections and part of the body's innate immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphocytes are a subtype of white blood cells essential for the adaptive immune response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphocytes are another type of white blood cell that tended to decrease in the W/ eps 10% group compared with the W/o eps 10% group, showing immune variance due to dietary changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphocytes are immune cells measured to identify changes under various TMlp treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AST, ALT, ALP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These are common liver function indicators used to measure the biochemical impact of TMlp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN (E2)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estrogen (E2), specifically 17β-estradiol, is used in the study to treat MCF-7 cells and assess cell viability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROL GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Control group is a standard of comparison for checking or verifying the results of an experiment, in this case, larvae fed with a non-plastic diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control group consists of rats that did not receive the experimental diets, serving as a baseline for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Control Group is used as a standard for comparison, featuring optimal conditions for larval growth and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/O EPS 10% GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This group of rats is fed a diet without expanded polystyrene at 10% concentration for comparative analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/ EPS 10% GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This group of rats is fed a diet containing 10% expanded polystyrene to observe its physiological effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/ EPS 5% GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This group of rats is fed a diet containing 5% expanded polystyrene to analyze dose-dependent effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/ EPS 15% GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This group of rats is fed a diet containing 15% expanded polystyrene to assess higher dose effects on rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL VIABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell viability is the ability of cells to survive and is measured to assess the effects of E2 and TMlp on MCF-7 cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematology involves the study of blood, which in this study includes measuring neutrophils and lymphocytes in response to different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERUM BIOCHEMISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serum biochemistry involves analyzing the chemical substances in blood serum, relevant to health and metabolic studies in organisms like bighead carp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serum biochemistry tests analyze specific biochemical markers in blood to evaluate physiological changes in rats."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-BILI (TOTAL BILIRUBIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-Bili is a component of blood biochemistry analysis that indicates liver function when under the detection limit in some groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-Bili measures bilirubin levels in the blood, reported in milligrams per deciliter, indicating liver function and hemolysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE BLOOD CELLS (WBC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WBCs are cells of the immune system involved in protecting the body against infectious diseases and foreign invaders."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monocytes are a type of white blood cell involved in the immune response against pathogens and old cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EOSINOPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eosinophils are white blood cells involved in combating multicellular parasites and certain infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASOPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basophils are white blood cells that participate in allergic reactions and release histamine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED BLOOD CELLS (RBC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RBCs are cells that carry oxygen from the lungs to the body's tissues and return carbon dioxide from the tissues to the lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMOGLOBIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hemoglobin is a biochemical parameter measured in grams per deciliter, used to assess blood components and oxygen transport capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemoglobin is the protein in red blood cells responsible for transporting oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOCRIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematocrit is a percentage that represents the volume fraction of red blood cells in blood, important for evaluating blood health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematocrit represents the ratio of the volume of red blood cells to the total volume of blood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRUDE PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crude Protein is a nutritional component in yellow mealworm larvae, enhanced by the degradation of small amounts of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude protein content is a key nutritional indicator in yellow mealworms, affected by the type of plastic consumed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude protein is the total protein content in a substance, including both digestible and indigestible proteins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude protein refers to the total protein content, assessed to understand the impact of different diets on larvae biomass nutrient contents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude protein content is used to evaluate the nutritional alterations in the larvae biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude protein is the amount of protein content determined by the Kjeldahl method after calculating nitrogen content in samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Crude protein refers to the total amount of protein in a substance, measured here in larvae and excrement to assess nutritional values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTOPATHOLOGICAL ABNORMALITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Histopathological abnormalities refer to unusual or abnormal tissue changes that can be detected via microscopic examination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidneys are the organs examined in the study for potential structural abnormalities, where no issues were found in the dietary groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"The kidneys are organs that filter blood, remove waste, and balance fluids and electrolytes in the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCV (MEAN CORPUSCULAR VOLUME)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCV measures the average volume of a red blood cell, reported in femtoliters, used in red blood cell characterization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCH (MEAN CORPUSCULAR HEMOGLOBIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCH is the average amount of hemoglobin per red blood cell, expressed in picograms, reflecting individual cell hemoglobin content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCHC (MEAN CELL HEMOGLOBIN CONCENTRATION)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MCHC denotes the concentration of hemoglobin in a given volume of packed red blood cells, reported in grams per deciliter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATELET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Platelet count, measured in thousands per microliter, evaluates platelets responsible for blood clotting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RDW (RED CELL DISTRIBUTION WIDTH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RDW is a percentage that indicates the variability in red blood cell size, important in diagnosing various anemia types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MPV (MEAN PLATELET VOLUME)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MPV is a measure of the average size of platelets, reported as a percentage, indicative of platelet production and function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMLP (TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE POWDER)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMLp is a product administered to rats as part of a dietary study, used in evaluating effects on various biochemical markers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/O EPS (WITHOUT EXPANDED-POLYSTYRENE-FED)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"W/o eps refers to a dietary condition where subjects are not fed expanded polystyrene, used as a control in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W/ EPS (EXPANDED-POLYSTYRENE-FED)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"W/ eps refers to a dietary condition where subjects are fed expanded polystyrene, included to evaluate its effects compared to controls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WBC (WHITE BLOOD CELL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White Blood Cell count is an indicator of immune system activity, involved in defending against infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RBC (RED BLOOD CELL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red Blood Cell count is a measure of the number of red blood cells, important in oxygen transport efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TP (TOTAL PROTEIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TP is the total concentration of all proteins in the blood, measured in grams per deciliter, reflecting nutritional and health status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALBUMIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Albumin is a major plasma protein, measured in grams per deciliter, important for maintaining osmotic pressure and transporting substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A simple sugar used as a positive control in experiments to compare microbial metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a simple sugar used as a positive control to determine if the increased CO2 production is due to carbon source availability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose levels, measured in milligrams per deciliter, are crucial for evaluating metabolic and endocrine function, especially in diabetes screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a carbohydrate found in the hemolymph, crucial for organ functioning, especially in the nervous system of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a simple sugar and an essential energy source derived from the catabolism of mannose during glycans biosynthesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a simple sugar, produced from cellulose degradation, that serves as an energy source in metabolic pathways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUN (BLOOD UREA NITROGEN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BUN is measured in milligrams per deciliter, representing the concentration of urea in the blood, used to assess renal function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREA (CREATININE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Creatinine is measured in milligrams per deciliter, used to evaluate kidney function and muscle metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AST (ASPARTATE AMINOTRANSFERASE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AST is an enzyme measured in units per liter, important for assessing liver function and cellular injury."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALT (ALANINE AMINOTRANSFERASE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALT is an enzyme measured in units per liter, often used as a marker for liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALP (ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALP is an enzyme measured in units per liter, indicative of liver, bone, and biliary duct health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Γ-GTP (GAMMA-GLUTAMYLTRANSFERASE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"γ-GTP is an enzyme measured in units per liter, important for liver function and bile duct injury assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBULIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Globulin is a group of proteins in the blood involved in immune responses and maintaining osmotic pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Globulin is a group of proteins in the blood, measured in grams per deciliter, involved in immune responses and transport."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAN CORPUSCULAR HEMOGLOBIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mean Corpuscular Hemoglobin (MCH) is a measurement of the average amount of hemoglobin in a single red blood cell, important for diagnosing anemia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAN CELL HEMOGLOBIN CONCENTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mean Cell Hemoglobin Concentration (MCHC) denotes the concentration of hemoglobin per unit volume of red cells, used to evaluate the average efficiency of hemoglobin cells in delivering oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATELET COUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Platelet Count is a measure of the number of platelets in the blood, which are vital for normal blood clotting and wound healing, measured in thousands per microliter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED CELL DISTRIBUTION WIDTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red Cell Distribution Width (RDW) measures the variability of red blood cell size, important for diagnosing and monitoring anemia and other blood disorders."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAN PLATELET VOLUME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mean Platelet Volume (MPV) is a laboratory measurement that reflects the average size of platelets in the blood, providing insight into platelet function and production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERUM BIOCHEMICAL PARAMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serum Biochemical Parameters provide insights into the metabolic, enzymatic, and physiological states of an organism, crucial for comprehensive health assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total Protein (TP) quantifies the total amount of protein in the blood, used to gauge nutritional status and various health conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total protein concentration in mealworms was measured to assess the impact of different polystyrene materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL BILIRUBIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total Bilirubin (T-Bili) is the amount of bilirubin in the blood, a breakdown product of hemoglobin, which is important for evaluating liver function and identifying hemolytic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD UREA NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood Urea Nitrogen (BUN) level indicates kidney function, as it measures the amount of nitrogen in the form of urea in the blood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREATININE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Creatinine is a waste product of muscle metabolism, its levels in the blood are indicative of kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPARTATE AMINOTRANSFERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspartate Aminotransferase (AST) is an enzyme found in high amounts in the liver and heart, used to assess liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALANINE AMINOTRANSFERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alanine Aminotransferase (ALT) is an enzyme found primarily in the liver, its levels are used as an indicator of liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAMMA-GLUTAMYLTRANSFERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gamma-Glutamyltransferase (γ-GTP) is an enzyme that helps transfer amino acids and peptides across the cellular membrane, typically tested for liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBULINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Globulins are a group of serum proteins that play roles in liver function, blood clotting, and fighting infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8bf6d17dfbab29bcb302ae97679bc903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM (NA+)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium is an essential electrolyte involved in maintaining fluid balance and nerve signal transmission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTASSIUM (K+)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potassium is an essential mineral that regulates heart and muscle function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLORIDE (CL-)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chloride is a key electrolyte that helps maintain fluid balance and acid-base balance in the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E2 (ESTRADIOL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estradiol (E2) is a form of estrogen involved in regulating reproductive and sexual functions, tested for its effect on breast cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTOPATHOLOGICAL TOXICITY ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scientific method used to assess tissue abnormalities for toxicity, particularly in liver and kidney tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN-INDUCED RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estrogen-induced response refers to the body’s reaction to the hormone estrogen, including changes in cell growth and differentiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL PROTEIN (TP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total Protein refers to the total amount of protein in the blood, used to assess nutritional status and kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL BILIRUBIN (T-BILI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total Bilirubin is a product of the normal breakdown of red blood cells, used as an indicator of liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD UREA NITROGEN (BUN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BUN is a measure of the amount of urea nitrogen found in blood, indicating kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREATININE (CREA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Creatinine is a waste product of muscle metabolism used as an indicator of kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALANINE AMINOTRANSFERASE (ALT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALT is an enzyme primarily found in the liver, used to assess liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The testis is an organ that showed a significant decrease in absolute weight, though not in relative weight, due to dietary administration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VITRO EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
