    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERMETIA ILLUCENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Also known as the black soldier fly, these larvae are studied for their microbiota and potential in organic waste-reduction processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hermetia illucens, commonly known as the Black Soldier Fly, is used for studies concerning organic material upcycling and plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hermetia illucens, known as black soldier fly, a promising species for entomoremediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hermetia illucens, known as the Black Soldier Fly, is another insect examined for its protein conversion efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hermetia illucens, known as the black soldier fly, whose larvae are evaluated for their nutritional value in broiler chicken diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hermetia illucens, commonly known as the black soldier fly, is an insect species known for its nutritional content and environmental applications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd</data>
    </node>
