    <node id="&quot;DYNAMIC ENERGY BUDGET (DEB) MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DEB model is a mathematical model used to describe the life cycles of organisms, helpful in analyzing the effects of polystyrene diet on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model is a theoretical framework used to analyze how energy is allocated in organisms, such as in studies examining the growth of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model is used in studies to analyze the energy budget related to growth, development, and survival of organisms such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dynamic Energy Budget model describes the energy and mass fluxes in organisms, helping to assess changes in physiological processes such as maintenance, growth, development, and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
