    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrient refers to a substance that provides nourishment essential for growth and the maintenance of life, used here as polystyrene for bacterial growth assay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrients are evaluated for their digestibility in mealworm larvae compared to traditional animal protein sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrients here refer to supplementary substances that enhance mealworm plastic waste degradation efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD SECURITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food security refers to the availability of food and individuals' access to it, which insects as a food source could potentially enhance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food security relates to the availability of safe and nutritious food, threatened by microplastic contamination in marine environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insects are considered as a sustainable food source that could play a significant role in future food security."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects were the subject of the development study, showing different growth dynamics and survival rates based on diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are studied for their potential to biodegrade plastic materials, showing promise in environmental remediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects are organisms that exhibit capabilities for plastic degradation and can be studied for their metabolic responses to plastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects have diverse gut microbiota with varied structures and functions, impacting their health and physiological processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
