      <data key="d2">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene's durable nature and resistance to biodegradation contribute significantly to environmental pollution, necessitating solutions for its disposal."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS MORIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of beetles, related to the yellow mealworm, whose larvae are studied for their diet on polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of superworm capable of consuming and breaking down Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is a genus of beetles whose larvae, known as superworms, have also been studied for their ability to metabolize polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio, also known as superworm, is another edible insect species examined for its consumption of polystyrene and nutrient composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio, known as the supermeal worm, is being studied for its anticancer peptides derived from its larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"An insect species known as the superworm whose gut bacteria aid in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio, a species used in biodegradation studies involving its gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio, also known as the superworm, is a species of beetle larva related to the mealworm, used in studies for its ability to decompose polyurethanes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles known for their feeding and degradation effect on plastic materials, contributing to waste reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is a genus of beetles whose larvae, known as superworms, are investigated for their potential in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is a species whose larvae are known as superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is another species of beetle often compared with Tenebrio, researched for its ecological and biological characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is a species of superworm larvae used in studies of nutritional composition and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species involved in the feeding and degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is the scientific name for superworms known to consume polystyrene, similar to mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASH CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ash content in mealworms increased after Styrofoam consumption compared to insects fed with a conventional diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ash content is a measure of mineral content, which increases in mealworms fed Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytotoxicity is the toxic effect on cells. The study investigates how emerging organic contaminants like tris(1,3-dichloro-2-propyl)phosphate and triphenyl phosphate impact this."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity refers to the potential toxic effects on cells, which was measured in insect cells after feeding them Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The quality of being toxic to cells, often assessed to understand the effects of substances like polystyrene on organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
