      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indicators of oxidative stress in organisms, used to assess cellular damage and response to diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress parameters were measured in insect cells to assess the impact of Styrofoam consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Various biomarkers indicating the level of oxidative damage in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. STRAIN YT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms capable of removing PS in a single culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial strain from mealworms, demonstrated significant polystyrene weight reduction over 60 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial strain reported to be involved in the conversion of polystyrene into CO2 and biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2, a bacterium in the digestive tract of mealworms, is responsible for their ability to consume Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 degrades polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor capable of degrading polystyrene as a sole carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"This strain is a PS-degrading bacterium isolated from the intestine of a mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm guts capable of degrading polystyrene by forming biofilm on its surface and creating physical changes such as pits and cavities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a plastic-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut of the plastic-eating mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is isolated from yellow mealworm, participates in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a microorganism found in the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor larvae, aiding in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polystyrene by forming biofilms and creating pits and holes in the plastic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONAL VALUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the beneficial qualities of food or feed in terms of ingredients and their contribution to diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritional value refers to the nutrient composition of insects, which was analyzed in this study post Styrofoam consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"The value of nutrients provided by organisms like Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas morio when grown on various diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritional value relates to the increased crude protein and phosphorus in yellow mealworm larvae post plastic degradation, influencing their growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nutritional value of yellow mealworms is primarily determined by their crude protein content, which is affected by their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nutritional value of natural fibers from plants like sugarcane and bamboo is higher than that of raw plastic polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VITRO CYTOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In vitro cytotoxicity measures the potential harmful effects of a substance on cultured cells, assessed in this study for insects fed Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"In vitro cytotoxicity pertains to the study of harmful effects of substances on cultured cells, often used to predict potential toxic effects in living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laboratory-based assessment of the toxic effects of substances on cultured cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOACTIVE PEPTIDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioactive peptides are beneficial compounds that can act as antioxidants, potentially present in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTOMOPHAGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Entomophagy is the consumption of insects as food, promoted for their nutritional benefits and environmental sustainability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The practice of consuming insects as food, which the text discusses in relation to insects fed on Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREENHOUSE GASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greenhouse gases are emissions that contribute to climate change; insect farming produces less compared to livestock farming."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE (EPS 80)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EPS 80 is a form of expanded polystyrene used in the study to feed insects, analyzing its impact on their nutrition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT FARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect farming is the practice of breeding insects for food, noted for its low environmental impact compared to traditional livestock farming."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH STATUS OF GUT CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The health status of gut cells was monitored to determine any adverse effects from Styrofoam ingestion in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN REPLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein replacement from Styrofoam was evaluated to see if it altered the cytotoxic nature of insect diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER ASBURIAE YTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial species known for its ability to degrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE) when combined with other bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial strain found in the gut of waxworms that contributes to polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAXWORMS (PLODIA INTERPUNCTELLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larvae of Plodia interpunctella, known for consuming and degrading plastic materials like polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERWORM (ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of larva with confirmed ability to digest Styrofoam, aiding in waste reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The superworm is a type of beetle larva that hosts microorganisms capable of degrading PS in its gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superworms are larvae known for feeding on Styrofoam and capable of biodegrading and mineralizing it, with a consumption rate four times that of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The superworm, also known as Zophobas atratus, is an organism from which Pseudomonas aeruginosa DSM 50071 was isolated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DARK MEALWORMS (TENEBRIO OBSCURUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae known for their ability to degrade polystyrene and study their role in plastic waste management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATERPILLARS OF THE WAX MOTH (GALLERIA MELLONELLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wax moth larvae noted for their capacity to degrade plastics such as polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESSER WAXWORM (ACHROIA GRISSELA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waxworm larvae identified as participants in bioconversion of plastic, particularly polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUBBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elastic material derived from latex, found to be degradable to some extent by certain insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rubber is an additive in rigid MPS which may influence the preference for functional group modifications during mealworm digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYLACTIDE (PLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biodegradable thermoplastic derived from renewable resources, subject to research on insect-facilitated degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PLA is a type of bioplastic made from renewable resources and capable of degrading naturally."&lt;SEP&gt;"PLA is a biodegradable thermoplastic, known for being derived from renewable resources like corn starch, which larvae consumed in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTATO WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste product from potato processing, used to breed mealworms due to its nutritional value."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CABBAGE WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste product from cabbage, used for breeding mealworms as part of their diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARROT WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste from carrot processing utilized for feeding mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLE WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A byproduct of apple processing, serving as a nutrient source for breeding mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental pollution involves the contamination of ecosystems by pollutants such as nanoplastics, which pose substantial ecological risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution, including that caused by plastic waste, is a major concern driving research into biodegradation and plastic waste solutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The introduction of harmful substances or products into the environment, such as plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a significant concern with Styrofoam waste, affecting wildlife and ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The introduction of contaminants into the environment causing adverse changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the introduction of harmful substances or products into the environment, which can be mitigated by biodegradation and other processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE WILDLIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sea organisms that are affected by environmental pollution, particularly plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The variety of life forms in an area, which can be impacted by plastic pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Human health can be affected by various environmental pollutants, such as microplastics, which may have indirect impacts through ecosystem changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human health is directly impacted by the exposure to microplastics in the environment, affecting well-being and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"The overall state of health in humans, which can be adversely affected by environmental pollutants like plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human health refers to the overall condition of a human's body and mind, significantly threatened by plastic pollution and microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC WASTE MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Practices and research in reducing, reusing, and recycling plastics including the role of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strategies and activities directed towards reducing plastic waste and its impact on the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strategies and processes for handling plastic waste in an environmentally sustainable manner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strategies and processes designed to handle plastic waste effectively, reducing environmental impact through recycling and degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fat acts as a basic source of energy for insects and is accumulated in the insect fat body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat content is reduced in mealworms fed Styrofoam compared to those on a conventional diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat percentage in the insects was calculated via Soxhlet extraction, essential for assessing their nutritional makeup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a macronutrient measured in the study to assess the nutritional composition of larvae fed various diets, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat refers to lipid content in larvae, significantly reduced in plastic-only diets, indicating malnutrition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOISTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moisture affects the growth rate and development of insects such as Tenebrio molitor L., impacting biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content in the insect samples was determined using a moisture analyzer, indicating the water content of the insect tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture is a key factor affecting the rate of biodegradation in mealworms, with increased moisture leading to more effective degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ash content in the samples was measured by using a muffle oven, providing data on the mineral content in the insects' bodies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOHYDRATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbohydrate levels in larvae were determined using the anthrone method, part of assessing the biochemical composition after plastic ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are organic compounds found in the biomass of larvae, and their concentration was determined as part of the study to assess nutrient levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates in mealworms decreased when fed on polystyrenes; they are important for maintaining organ function, especially the nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates were calculated by difference, giving a complete picture of the nutritional components present in the insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates provide essential energy during insect life, with varying contents depending on mealworms' diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are critical for insect haemolymph and support the nervous system and organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOTHELIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endothelial cells are targeted in cytotoxicity assays to evaluate the impact of insect homogenates on cellular growth and viability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HECA10 LINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The HECa10 line refers to a specific lineage of endothelial cells used for in vitro cytotoxicity tests in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTOTOXICITY ASSAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytotoxicity assays assess the impact of insect homogenates on the viability of HECa10 endothelial cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROLIFERATION ASSAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proliferation assays measure the growth rate of endothelial cells following treatment with insect extract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM EPS 80&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrofoam EPS 80 is a specific type of expanded polystyrene used in the study to feed insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWISSPOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Swisspor is the brand of Styrofoam EPS 80 used in the insect feeding trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KUPIEC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kupiec is the brand of wheat bran used as a control diet for the insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N CONVERSION FACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N conversion factor is used in the Kjeldahl method to calculate protein content from nitrogen values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEXANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hexane is used as a solvent in Soxhlet extraction to isolate fats from the insect samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIOPHILIZED INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lyophilized insects are freeze-dried to create homogenates for cytotoxicity assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYOPHILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lyophilization is a freeze-drying process used to preserve insects by removing moisture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lyophilization is a process used to dry mealworms by freezing and reducing surrounding pressure to allow frozen water to sublimate, facilitating lipid extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PASSAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Passage refers to the sub-culturing process of cells to maintain continuous growth for experimental purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;0.25% TRYPSIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"0.25% trypsin is an enzyme used to detach and harvest cells for proliferation and cytotoxicity assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DMEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DMEM, or Dulbecco’s Modified Eagle Medium, is a culture medium used to support the growth of endothelial cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FBS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FBS, or fetal bovine serum, is used in cell culture media to provide nutrients and growth factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PBS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PBS (Phosphate Buffered Saline) is a buffer solution used to maintain a constant pH and is used to dilute bacterial suspensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBS, or phosphate-buffered saline, is used in biological research for washing cells during assays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polybutylene succinate (PBS) is another bioplastic type tested for degradation by identified bacterial strains."</data>
