    <node id="&quot;PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a type of plastic polymer that is extensively used in packaging and textiles. It is known for its strong molecular structure, which makes it resistant to environmental degradation. PET is a polyester resin powder that has been the subject of numerous biodegradation studies, particularly focusing on its interaction with insect larvae such as T. molitor (mealworms) and BSF larvae. These studies explore the ability of larvae to ingest and biodegrade PET, potentially using it as an energy source and for larval biomass production.

The biodegradation process of PET involves depolymerization, which is characterized by isotopic enrichment and is influenced by gut microbial activity and the larvae's metabolic processes. The high-purity plastic can be partially degraded by the larvae, who use gut mechanisms and certain enzymes and microorganisms for this purpose. The biodegradation of PET is also influenced by its physical and chemical structure, which affects how effectively it can be broken down. These studies aim to better understand the metabolic interaction between PET and larvae, contributing valuable insights into potential waste management solutions and materials science.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
