    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON SOURCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A carbon source is a substance that provides carbon for organisms to produce energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon obtained from digested plastics like PET that contributes to larval biomass and energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The role of plastics as a carbon source for yellow mealworms, providing energy but not significantly influencing weight change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene film is used as a carbon source in the experiments to cultivate and assess the biodegradation potential of microorganisms such as strains LG3 and SCGB1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon source refers to a substance that provides carbon for the nutritional requirements of bacteria, as seen in the use of polystyrene as the sole carbon source in degradation tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
