    <node id="&quot;DYSGONOMONADACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A family of bacteria detected in the gut microbiota of insects, associated with decomposition processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIROPLASMA SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus strongly associated with the biodegradation of LDPE in the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dominant bacterial genus observed to be related to PET biodegradation in the gut microbiota of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of bacteria within the gut of T. molitor, involved in plastic degradation, especially LDPE and PLA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Often found in the gut microbiota of insects, actively involved in plastic degradation processes like LDPE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma sp. is a genus of bacteria involved in the degradation process of different molecular weights of polypropylene and lignocellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma sp. was among the dominant genera in the control group, not directly implicated in PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma sp. is a bacterium commonly present in the gut microbiome of mealworms and other insects, involved in maintaining microbiome structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium genus enriched in the gut of PP-M-fed T. molitor larvae, associated with LDPE and PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of bacteria frequently found in diverse environments and sometimes involved in degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a bacterium involved in the degradation of medium molecular weight polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a bacterium associated with PS degradation and isolated from insect larvae guts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROCOCCUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria involved in the biodegradation of LDPE in gut microbiome studies of T. obscurus and T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of plastic-degrading bacteria enriched in environments contaminated by plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus sp. is a genus of bacteria identified as a key microorganism in the degradation of PP and lignocellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus species are bacteria involved in microbiome studies with a range of hosts, including insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus sp. is part of the mealworm gut microbiome, contributing to digestive and microbiome balance in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENTAMICIN SULFATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A form of the antibiotic gentamicin used to suppress gut microorganisms in biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A product used in the experiment, likely as part of the growth medium or sampling process, purchased from Aladdin, Shanghai."&lt;SEP&gt;"An aminoglycoside antibiotic used in the study for gut microbial inhibition."&lt;SEP&gt;"An antibiotic used in the suppression test to inhibit gut microbes during PET degradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to test its effects on polymer biodegradation/depolymerization in larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress the gut microbiome activity in mealworm studies, helping to determine the role of gut bacteria in degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is used to suppress gut microbiota to study its effect on PP depolymerization and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress microbial activity, specifically targeting gut bacteria during depolymerization studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </node>
