      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A \(\beta\)-lactam antibiotic included in the mixture for gut bacteria suppression."&lt;SEP&gt;"A common antibiotic used to inhibit the growth of bacteria in biodegradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ampicillin is used in the study to show a strong inhibition on the gut flora of mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ampicillin is another antibiotic that can suppress gut microbiota, impacting their role in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An antibiotic previously tested for its ability to inhibit gut microorganisms in T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KANAMYCIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An aminoglycoside antibiotic used for inhibiting gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"An aminoglycoside antibiotic used to suppress bacterial growth related to the degradation of PET."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARCHAEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A group of microorganisms with low abundance in the gut microbiota, not considered significant in PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of microorganism targeted by prokaryotic universal primers for genomic analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Archaea are a group of unicellular microorganisms that play a role in the microbiome, influenced by dietary and environmental factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EUKARYOTE&quot;">
