    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diet containing polyethylene terephthalate (PET) that affects the gut microbial communities of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A group of enzymes, including monooxygenases and dioxygenases, over-expressed in PET-fed larvae, contributing to oxidation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes that participate in the PET degradation process by oxidizing polymer intermediates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidases are a type of enzyme in the larval gut that aids in the oxidative degradation of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
