      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A compound formed from the metabolism of terephthalic acid by dioxygenases during PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A metabolite formed during aerobic decomposition, linked to the degradation process of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protocatechuic Acid is another metabolite resulting from PET degradation, further degradable via catechol."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protocatechuic acid is a metabolite that increases in abundance in PET-fed samples, indicating its involvement in PET degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
    </node>
