    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROFLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microflora encompasses the community of microorganisms living in the digestive tracts of larvae, which aid in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microflora refers to the community of microbes residing in the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor, aiding in the biodegradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdf2753a9a78b282c1ca2c0539e3203d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYURETHANE (PUR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of polymer with unique chemical properties needing further research for its biodegradation by invertebrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUR is a polymer composed of organic units joined by carbamate links, used in foams, elastomers, and other applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a plastic material known for its resistance and environmental persistence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a widely used plastic polymer that is part of the study on biodegradation processes by insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a thermoplastic comprising 7.4% of plastic products and is among plastics considered hazardous."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a versatile plastic material used in foams and coatings, contributing to synthetic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a synthetic plastic that is resistant to biodegradation, although certain invertebrates have shown potential to degrade it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a versatile plastic used in foam products, insulation, and coatings, known for its resilience and flexibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer composed of organic units joined by urethane links, known for its flexibility and strength in foam and solid forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a polymer used in foam seating, insulation panels, and other applications due to its flexibility and durability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLESIOPHTHALMUS DAVIDIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A beetle species within Tenebrionidae, known for its capability to biodegrade plastics like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis belongs to the darkling beetle family and contributes to the biodegradation process of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is one of the darkling beetles involved in the natural process of plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis larvae contain gut microbial flora capable of polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis larvae have a gut microbial flora that facilitates the rapid biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species investigated for its potential biodegradation capabilities, although not yet broadly applied."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERMEDIATE FORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intermediate formation is part of the biodegradation process where oxidized intermediates are produced from plastic polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbes are important in the degradation of plastics by insects like Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes are involved in the process of biodegrading plastics in creatures like mealworms, contributing to depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes are microorganisms in mealworm digestive systems that facilitate the breakdown of polyethylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes are microorganisms present in the intestines that influence the biodegradation of specific plastics like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes refer to the microbial community residing in the digestive systems of organisms, involved in digestion and biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes within T. molitor are crucial for plastic degradation, varying their community composition depending on diet and showing gut microbe dependence for certain plastic types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms residing in the gastrointestinal tract, often involved in digestion and other bodily processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes in T. molitor larvae are part of a system that may contribute to plastic biodegradation, their role studied through antibiotic suppression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes are the collective microorganisms found in the digestive tract, involved in the enrichment and isolation of bacterial strains, such as YT2, capable of polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes refer to the diverse community of microorganisms living in the digestive systems of superworms and mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes are the diverse microbial communities found in the digestive systems of larvae, playing a role in the digestion and biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes play a role in the degradation of PP polymers, with their reduction affecting the process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms present in the guts of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae, potentially involved in the depolymerization and biodegradation of PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes are microorganisms residing in guts, enhancing but not essential for the depolymerization of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbes refer to the microorganisms residing in the larvae's digestive system, including bacteria, that are potentially involved in polymer depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbes found in the digestive system of organisms like the darkling beetle larvae, aiding in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms inhabiting the gut of insects, playing a crucial role in biological processes such as digestion and biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer degradation encompasses various chemical reactions that lead to the breakdown of large polymer molecules into simpler units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer degradation refers to the breakdown of polymer materials, influenced by chemical structure and conditions such as microbial activity and environmental variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which polymer chains break down through chemical reactions, leading to changes in material properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic activities in T. molitor larvae contribute to plastic degradation and energy acquisition from the diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE (LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A thermoplastic made from the monomer ethylene, food and beverage containers, and is also subject to metabolic processes in some larval species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another plastic polymer associated with microbial degradation in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a plastic material that shows less dependence on gut microbes for degradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a type of polymer whose decomposition is studied by extracting it from frass using specific solvents."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a type of polymer that was metabolized by mealworms, leading to a change in its crystalline structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE, or low-density polyethylene, is a type of polymer examined for transformations in its crystalline structure after being metabolized by mealworms from Tai'an and Shenzhen."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a thermoplastic made from the polymerization of ethylene, known for its flexibility and resistance to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a variant of polyethylene used in multiple forms, whose biodegradation is less dependent on gut microbes compared to other forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is another type of polymer feedstock used in biodegradation experiments to study its breakdown by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE) is a subset of polyethylene characterized by its lower density and branching, often used in films and bags."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of polyethylene with a significant amount of long chain and short chain branching, leading to lower crystallinity and density."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is another plastic type tested in the study, known for its elasticity, to assess its degradation by mealworm consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density Polyethylene, consumed by mealworms, has one of the lowest consumption rates in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a type of plastic material that T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae have attempted to biodegrade in earlier studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is another plastic polymer used in comparative studies with other plastics like polypropylene to assess degradation capabilities by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a type of polyethylene with a linear carbon backbone, used in commercial products and resistant to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a specific type of Polyethylene plastic tested to evaluate its degradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENTAMICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An antibiotic used in feedstocks for suppressing gut bacteria in larval studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"An antibiotic used in the study to test its effect on gut microorganisms within the larvae of T. molitor regarding plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin is an antibiotic used during the experiment to assess its impact on the biodegradation process of LDPE by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin is an antibiotic used in the study to inhibit gut bacteria in larvae, providing a controlled environment to assess the role of gut microbes in polymer depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin is an antibiotic used to suppress gut microbes, highlighting the role of microbes in polyethylene depolymerization studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin is an antibiotic used to suppress gut microbes, thereby inhibiting microbial depolymerization activities in T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin is an aminoglycoside antibiotic known for its ability to irreversibly bind to the 30S subunit of the bacterial ribosome, thereby disrupting protein synthesis and inhibiting bacterial growth. In experimental settings, particularly in studies involving mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) and superworms, Gentamicin has been extensively used to explore the microbial dynamics within the gut flora. It is primarily utilized to suppress gut bacteria, which significantly inhibits their activity and adversely affects the depolymerization of polystyrene (PS) without impacting the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene (LDPE). Additionally, Gentamicin is employed in researching the biodiversity and roles of gut microbial communities in degrading various plastic materials, highlighting its specific inhibitory effects on polystyrene degradation.

In these experiments, Gentamicin is used to depress microbial activity in larvae, notably impacting the biodegradation processes of plastics like polystyrene and polypropylene. This suppression illustrates the critical role of gut microbes in the degradation of these substances. Moreover, studies using Gentamicin have shown that it effectively inhibits microbes such as Exiguobacterium sp. YT2, emphasizing the dependence of polystyrene biodegradation on the innate microbial community within larvae. This makes Gentamicin a vital tool in scientific research focused on understanding how microbial pathways influence plastic degradation processes, by altering or reducing the active bacterial populations in larvae.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANFORD UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A leading academic institution involved in supporting environmental research, including studies on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stanford University is an institution where part of the research on mealworms' polystyrene degradation was conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stanford University is an institution where research on the biodegradation of plastics by T. molitor larvae is conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stanford University is one of the institutions involved in conducting research and analysis on polystyrene biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Educational institution where significant research was conducted on biodegradation and microbiome roles in it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stanford University is the research institution where the mealworm experiments are conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stanford University is the research institution where the mealworm experiments on plastic degradation are conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stanford University is the institution providing support and funding for the study under the Woods Institute for the Environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLA (POLYLACTIC ACID)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PLA is a biodegradable plastic that has been observed to be consumed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PLA is a biodegradable plastic that has been tested for degradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PLA is a biodegradable polymer whose content in frass provides insights into organic waste processing efficiencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"PLA is a biodegradable polyester used in experiments with larvae for testing their ability to process it as a food source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A parameter monitored during the biodegradation process, significant in influencing the activity of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature affects the survival and plastic consumption rate of T. molitor larvae, with different regional tolerances observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The temperature was maintained at 28°C ± 1°C during the experiment to provide optimal conditions for mealworm growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature settings, such as 30 °C and 230 °C, are crucial for various stages of the extraction and analysis processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a physical condition influencing the rate of biodegradation in mealworms, with higher temperatures enhancing breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature affects the biodegradation rate of polystyrene in mealworms, with optimal conditions at 25°C."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature affects the rate of polystyrene degradation by mealworms, with an optimal range reported between 25-28°C for mealworm physiology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a key variable affecting the survival rate and PS consumption of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a variable in the study, with effects on the degradation rate of PS by mealworms at 20°C, 25°C, and 30°C."&lt;SEP&gt;"The temperature of the experiment was consistently maintained at 37 °C."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a physical property that can affect the rate and efficiency of biodegradation of plastics in soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMIDITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A monitored environmental parameter that affects the biodegradation efficiency by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is maintained at 60–80% to support optimal conditions for T. molitor larvae during plastic degradation tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is maintained at 70% in the incubators to support optimal conditions for larval experimentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity levels were carefully controlled at 78-80% during the mealworm breeding experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity levels are controlled during experiments to ensure consistency in microbial activity and material degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is derived using a gravimetric method and refers to the moisture content, measured at 57.8%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity or moisture content is noted as a characteristic measured in the context of insects' biomass and frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"The humidity level during the experiment ranged from 30% to 40%."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC SUPPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic suppression involves inhibiting gut microbes with substances like gentamicin to study their role in the polymer degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to using antibiotics to inhibit gut microbiota, demonstrating its essential role in polystyrene degradation by superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic suppression refers to the use of antibiotics to suppress gut microbes in T. molitor larvae to study their role in PET biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test designed to inhibit gut microbiota to evaluate their contribution to PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic suppression is used to test how the removal of gut microorganisms affects mealworm's ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIETARY CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dietary changes in T. molitor larvae can influence the composition and functionality of their gut microbiome, affecting plastic degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genera are taxonomic categories used to classify groups of closely related species that play a role in plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Species are specific groups within genera that contribute to the biodegradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER SP. STRAIN NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A PE-degrading bacterium isolated from the intestine of yellow mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial strain capable of biodegrading polyethylene mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterium capable of degrading LDPE, known to grow in co-culture on such substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450, part of a co-culture with Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451, degrades LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of PE-feeding Tenebrio molitor larvae, which is involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene mulching films in co-culture with another bacterium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterium involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene mulching films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP. STRAIN NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain involved in the co-culture biodegradation process of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451 can degrade LDPE and grows in a co-culture environment on this type of plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451 is part of a co-culture that degrades LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of PE-feeding Tenebrio molitor larvae, which acts in concert with Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 to degrade polyethylene films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another PE-degrading bacterium from the intestine of yellow mealworm larvae, which shows synergy with Acinetobacter sp. NyZ450."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451 is a bacterial strain used in conjunction with Acinetobacter strain for biodegrading polyethylene films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451 is a bacterium that works in coordination with Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 to degrade polyethylene mulching films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTERIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacterium sp. is associated with plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA GENE AMPLICON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing is used to study microbial communities and involves gene regions of ribosomal RNA for phylogenetic identification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAVIMETRICAL ANALYSIS (TGA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TGA assesses the thermal stability of polymers, where degradation indicates reduced stability due to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a method used to determine the thermal stability of materials by measuring changes in their mass with temperature under a controlled atmosphere."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHATE BUFFERED WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phosphate buffered water is a solution with a pH of 7.0 used for rinsing extracted gut tissue to collect gut microflora for DNA extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA EXTRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA extraction is a biological process used to isolate genetic material from the larvae for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA extraction is a method used to isolate genetic material from T. molitor larvae samples for further molecular analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA extraction is performed on preserved larvae samples to analyze the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA extraction is the process used for obtaining and purifying DNA from biological samples for analysis of microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of isolating DNA from samples using mechanical and chemical methods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILLUMINA MISEQ PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOOL/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sequencing platform used for paired-end sequencing of DNA amplicons."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sequencing technology platform used to perform paired-end sequencing on DNA samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sequencing technology used to perform paired-end sequencing of microbial DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Illumina MiSeq platform is a technology recommended for 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing, used in microbial community studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Illumina MiSeq platform is a sequencing technology used for high-throughput DNA sequencing, particularly for analyzing microbial communities based on 16S rRNA gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PACBIO PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PacBio platform is used for full-length 16S rRNA gene sequencing, providing comprehensive data on microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANOPORE PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NanoPore platform is a sequencing technology used for full-length 16S rRNA genes, offering deep insights into microbial structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISEQ PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The HiSeq platform is recommended for shot-gun metagenome sequencing, providing high-throughput sequencing data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEXTSEQ PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NextSeq platform is used for shot-gun metagenome sequencing, enabling detailed analysis of microbial genomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOVASEQ PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NovaSeq platform offers advanced shot-gun metagenome sequencing capabilities for comprehensive genome analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM DODECYL SULFATE (SDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A detergent used to remove biofilms from the surface of PS film sheets for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"SDS is a detergent used to treat samples, aiding in cleaning by removing residual biomass or biofilm."&lt;SEP&gt;"SDS is a surfactant used for cleaning the plastic surface before analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium dodecyl sulfate is a detergent used for cleaning purposes, often used to remove biofilms and other organic attachments."&lt;SEP&gt;"SDS is used at a concentration of 2% as a solution for removing biofilms from the PS film surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"SDS is used in the study to prepare PE films by washing them as part of weight measurement processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A detergent used to wash PS films during biodegradation assays."&lt;SEP&gt;"SDS is employed to observe changes caused by bacteria in polystyrene films during experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTON NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE (1H NMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1H NMR is a method used to analyze the structural characteristics of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"1H NMR is used in NMR spectroscopy focused on hydrogen-1 nuclei to determine molecular structures and observe chemical modifications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIAL SCANNING CALORIMETRIC (DSC) ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DSC is a technique used to study the thermal properties and transitions of materials, such as polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPY (SEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SEM is a method used for detailed observation of surfaces, including microbial colonization and structural changes on materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a type of electron microscopy that produces images of a sample by scanning it with a focused beam of electrons."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is a technique that provides detailed images of the biofilm formation on the surface of PE films, aiding in morphological characterization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) is a technology used to observe the surface of HDPE film, revealing pits and cracks after incubation with Bacillus sp. PELW2042."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) is a technology used to observe physical changes in polystyrene surfaces caused by the microbial activity in Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning Electron Microscopy is a technique used to observe the detailed physical changes like cracks and holes in polystyrene induced by microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is used for obtaining high-resolution images of sample surfaces, employed for investigating micro-morphological features of feedstocks and frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM is employed to determine the surface structure and characteristics of NPS before and after treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) is a technique used to analyze surface alterations in PS film due to microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) is a technology used to investigate the physical and chemical changes in degraded PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f102938f307d7404d3f31b7200d93768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER CONTACT ANGLE (WCA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of surface hydrophobicity, affected by the polymer's structural changes during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A measure used to assess changes in surface hydrophobicity of PS film sheets."&lt;SEP&gt;"The water contact angle is a measure of surface hydrophobicity, used to evaluate changes in the PS film after biofilm formation by strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA measures changes in the hydrophobicity of surfaces, indicating activity related to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water Contact Angle (WCA) is used to determine the change in hydrophobicity of the PS Film Sheet surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle (WCA) is a physical property measured to assess changes in surface hydrophobicity of PS films during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA is a measure of the wettability of a surface, with lower angles indicating higher wettability. It is used to analyze the surface properties of PE powder and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle is a measure of the hydrophobicity of a surface, which decreases after polyethylene microplastics are processed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water Contact Angle indicates the degree of surface hydrophobicity of polymers, with changes implying surface roughness and biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOTOPIC LABELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique using isotopes to trace and analyze biological or chemical processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;14C LABELED ISOTOPIC POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymers labeled with carbon-14 isotopes used in experiments to track biodegradation by monitoring 14CO2 production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic materials that persist after partial degradation or research processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A carbohydrate consisting largely of glucose units, used as a nutrient or thickening agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is a carbohydrate polymer used in studies of polystyrene biodegradation when grafted onto polystyrene to enhance degradation rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starch is a carbohydrate component used in the feed to enhance larval growth and reduce overall development time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT DIGESTIVE ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes located in the gut that play a role in breaking down complex molecules into simpler ones during digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut digestive enzymes are biochemical catalysts present in the digestive system of insects like Zophobas aratus, involved in breaking down polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut digestive enzymes are proteins that facilitate the breakdown of food into nutrients within the digestive system, important in the study of plastic degradation by insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;14CO2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A carbon dioxide molecule that contains the radioactive isotope carbon-14, used in experiments to trace carbon flow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;14CH4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A methane molecule that contains the radioactive isotope carbon-14, indicating microbial activity in anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL COLONIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process by which microorganisms establish a community on a surface, such as a polymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADABLE ADDITIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Substances added to products to promote biodegradation, which also serve as nutrients for microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR TESTING AND MATERIALS (ASTM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An international standards organization that develops and publishes consensus technical standards for materials and products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL STANDARDS ORGANIZATION (ISO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An international standard-setting body composed of representatives from various national standards organizations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic polymers like polystyrene, polyethylene, and others are manufactured materials designed for various applications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C CP/MAS NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"13C CP/MAS NMR is a nuclear magnetic resonance technique used to analyze the chemical composition of solid materials without separating their components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solid-state 13C cross-polarization/magic angle spinning nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) is used to identify newly appearing functional groups in solid samples amid plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-DEGRADING BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic-degrading bacteria are microbial organisms capable of breaking down plastics, found in mealworm gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-degrading bacteria are specific microbes that can break down plastic materials into simpler substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are bacteria isolated from environments or organisms that can break down plastic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;H NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proton nuclear magnetic resonance (H NMR) is used to determine the purity of a sample and the structure of its molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WCA, or Water Contact Angle, measures the wettability of the PS film surface before and after treatment with bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water Contact Angle (WCA) measures changes in the hydrophilicity of the PS film's surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water contact angle (WCA) measurement is a method used to understand the hydrophilicity or hydrophobicity of surfaces in gut microbial degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,2 DICHLOROBENZENE (DCB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,2 Dichlorobenzene is used for the gel permeation chromatography (GPC) analysis of low density polyethylene (LDPE) and polypropylene (PP)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DICHLOROMETHANE (DCM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DCM is a solvent used for the extraction of LDPE, PP, and PLA, aiding in the analysis of plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS MPs (polystyrene microplastics) can be used as feedstock, often utilized in experimental diets with bran for larval growth tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS MPs refers to Polystyrene Microplastics, which are the subject of the study in terms of consumption and biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS MPs, short for polystyrene microplastics, are used in the study to evaluate their consumption and biodegradation by mealworms under varying dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene microplastics (PS MPs) are plastic particles under investigation for their biodegradation patterns in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JELLY POWDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jelly powder is used as an adhesive component to create PS-bran mixed diets for larval growth experimentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic foam is a material being studied for degradation by insect larvae and their associated microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic foam is targeted as a feedstock in incubator setups to study its consumption and biodegradation by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weights refer to the mass of a molecule and are determined through GPC analysis to understand the composition of foam additives."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION (MWD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A description of the distribution of individual molecular masses within a given sample, important in polymer characterization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Describes the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample, shifting during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD highlights the range and distribution of molecular weights in a polymer, affecting degradation rates when processed by T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD is a measure of the distribution of molecular masses in a given sample and is assessed via GPC analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD is the distribution of molecular weights in a given polymer sample, used to assess changes in PS after digestion by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution is a measure of the spread of molecular weights in a sample, analyzed by GPC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD) refers to the spread of various molecular weights within a polymer sample, crucial for analyzing depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is the molecular weights' range and frequency within a polymer sample, impacting processing and performance properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution reflects the variety of molecular weights within a polystyrene sample and changes as a result of microbial degradation by strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution represents the variation in the weight of different polymer molecules within a sample, affected by mealworm digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a critical property of polymers, including plastics, that affects their physical properties and degradation behavior, analyzed using GPC."&lt;SEP&gt;"An indicator used in characterizing the depolymerization of plastics, including PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD addresses the variation in sizes of polymer molecules, indicating the extent of degradation achieved by larval digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular Weight Distribution is an analysis metric to compare the size of LDPE polymers before and after the biodegradation by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution describes the distribution of molecular masses in a given polymer sample, crucial for understanding polymer properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOILED DEIONIZED WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boiled deionized water is used to dissolve jelly powder in the preparation of PS-bran mixed diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALUMINUM PAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An aluminum pan is used to air-dry the PS-bran mixture before it is used as a diet for the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AIR-DRYING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Air-drying is the process used to remove moisture from the PS-bran mixture prior to feeding it to larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCUBATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A controlled environment device used to maintain mealworms in optimal conditions when natural conditions deviate."&lt;SEP&gt;"An incubator is set up to create controlled conditions for larvae, featuring specific temperature and humidity settings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Incubators are used to house mealworms during experiments to control feeding conditions and environmental parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"An incubator is a controlled environment used for rearing mealworms at specific temperatures and humidity levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS Foam is a lightweight, expanded form of polystyrene used in applications such as packaging, undergoing decomposition in larvae studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is used as an initial feedstock in incubators targeting the biodegradation of plastics by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam refers to polystyrene foam, a type of plastic that is ingested and partially digested by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam, or polystyrene foam, used as a material in the study for degradation experiments with mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam, a form of polystyrene, is used as a diet in studies examining plastic degradation by insects and microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam, or polystyrene foam, is mentioned as another type of plastic that is compared to PET in the context of biodegradation and microbial functionality."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS Foam stands for polystyrene foam, which undergoes chemical structure changes when ingested by superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS Foam, or polystyrene foam, is used in studies of biodegradation using mealworms, though it does not support high productivity compared to standard diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene foam (PS foam) is used in the feeding experiments, evaluated for its effects on mealworm growth and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam refers to polystyrene foam, another material used in the study to observe biodegradation effects in its virgin and aged forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam stands for polystyrene foam, often used in packaging and insulation. It is also consumed by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic that T. obscurus larvae can biodegrade through gut microbe-dependent mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam, or polystyrene foam, is a type of plastic material ingested by mealworms to study its biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam refers to polystyrene material in a foam form, subjected to digestion by various organisms like mealworms and Achatina fulica."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHANOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A volatile, flammable, and colorless liquid used in the washing process to sterilize materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethanol is used for preserving larvae samples in a glass vial as part of microbiome analysis background control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethanol is used for sterilizing PE mulching films before treatment with bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethanol is used to kill mealworms to avoid contamination of products during preparation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethanol is used for surface sterilization of PS film and as a solvent in the Crystal Violet Staining Method for biofilm analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethanol is used as a disinfectant and solvent in laboratory processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a32ea55d79e87933e26b4165db47b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBAL RATE (CR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannibal Rate is a measure of the number of disappeared larvae in relation to the initial number, expressed as a percentage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibal Rate is the percentage of cannibalism occurring within the T. molitor larvae population under various diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibal Rate measures the occurrence of cannibalism among larvae in experimental settings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION RATE (PR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation Rate is a measure of the number of pupae compared to the initial number of larvae, expressed as a percentage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation Rate is calculated to assess the percentage of larvae that successfully transition to pupae stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rate refers to the percentage of larvae that successfully transition into pupae, indicating growth and development success."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRY WEIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dry weights refer to the mass of frass and other components after moisture removal, used to calculate residual PS content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual PS percentage is determined to assess the extent of polystyrene consumption and degradation by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Residual PS refers to leftover polystyrene that is extracted and analyzed for studying its properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;15-20 LARVAE SAMPLING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sampling process involving the collection of 15-20 larvae for microbiome analysis, preserved in ethanol."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(-20^{\CIRC} \MATHRM{C}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A temperature at which frass samples are stored for GPC and other analyses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(-80^{\CIRC} \MATHRM{C}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A temperature used to preserve larvae samples in alcohol for subsequent DNA extraction and analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLASS BEAKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A glass beaker is used for preparing and mixing solutions in the experimental setup."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPRESSED AIR FLUSHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Compressed air flushing is used to cleanse larvae before collecting their frass for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER SOLUBLE FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water Soluble Fraction refers to the portion of frass that dissolves in water, containing soluble salts and dissolved organic products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHANOL EXTRACTABLE FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethanol Extractable Fraction refers to the portion of frass that is extracted with ethanol, potentially containing biodegraded intermediates and residues of co-diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THF EXTRACTABLE FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"THF Extractable Fraction is the portion of frass extracted using tetrahydrofuran, assessing the residual polymer content."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF extractable fraction refers to the portion of PS that can be extracted using tetrahydrofuran as a solvent."&lt;SEP&gt;"The THF extractable fraction is measured as an indicator of polystyrene digestion in the larvae's frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"The THF extractable fraction is a measure used to indicate the extent of PVC degradation within the larvae gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PS CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual PS Content refers to the percentage of polystyrene remaining in the frass after consumption by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEIONIZED WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deionized Water is used in various extraction processes as a solvent to remove water-soluble components of frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deionized water is used to rinse plastic samples, providing a controlled environment free of ions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deionized water is used in preparing various experimental media to ensure purity and control conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLY(ETHER SULFONE) (PES) MEMBRANE FILTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of filter used to separate the THF solution during polymer extraction processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PES membrane filter is used for filtering water solutions to separate solids during frass analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBER GLASS FILTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fiber Glass Filter is an alternative filtering material used instead of PES for analyzing frass components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEFLON COATED SEPTUM COVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Teflon Coated Septum Cover is used to seal glass vials during solvent storage in extraction processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRASONIC TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ultrasonic Treatment is applied to frass samples to aid in the extraction of water-soluble fractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shaker is used to mix frass samples with solvents at controlled speeds for thorough extraction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VACUUM DRYING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vacuum Drying is employed to remove solvents from residues, aiding in measuring the mass of extracted fractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLASS VIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Glass Vial is used as a container for sample extraction processes during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glass Vial is used for storing extracted solutions from frass for further analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THF (TETRAHYDROFURAN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"THF is a solvent used in the extraction process of polymers from EPS and frass samples in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to dissolve residual polystyrene from frass in the extraction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is used as a solvent in the extraction of polystyrene and PVC from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to extract residual plastic from frass for evaluating the extent of polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to extract residual PS polymers from frass, indicating polymer presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is used as a solvent in GPC analysis for assessing PS degradation in mealworm frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,2 DCB (1,2-DICHLOROBENZENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,2 DCB is used in the extraction process to isolate LDPE and PP from frass samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DCM (DICHLOROMETHANE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DCM is a solvent used for extracting components such as PLA, LDPE, and PP from frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1H NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1H NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) is a technique used to observe the signals of hydrogen atoms within compounds, utilized here to assess the distribution of PS-derived oligomers."&lt;SEP&gt;"1H NMR, or Proton Nuclear Magnetic Resonance, analysis is used to identify the incorporation of various functional groups into oxidized polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proton Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (1H NMR) is employed to study the changes in the end groups of the polymer after being processed by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proton nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy, used to analyze the chemical structure changes in biodegraded polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS LOSS OF PS FEEDSTOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The reduction in mass of PS feedstock as it is consumed by larvae, used to calculate the ratio or percentage of PS in the diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N_A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N_a represents the average number of larvae over a test period, used in calculating the specific polymer consumption rate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W_F&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"W_f represents the total weight of frass generated by larvae as a result of consuming PS feedstock."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OMNIC SOFTWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OMNIC software is used for analyzing FTIR spectroscopic data to identify functional groups in plastic samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Software used for identifying peaks in FTIR spectra to analyze chemical structure changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1H NMR ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1H NMR Analysis is used to identify transitions in chemical structure, demonstrating changes in PET after degradation by intestinal microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"1H NMR analysis is used to characterize changes in polymer end groups through nuclear magnetic resonance at ambient temperature."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLOROFORM-D&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solvent used in NMR analysis to prepare frass samples by dissolving polymers for detailed characterization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a deuterated solvent used in the extraction of residual polymers from egested frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a solvent used to extract residual polyethylene from egested frass for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is used as a solvent in NMR analysis with high purity, specifically from Cambridge Isotope Laboratories, Inc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-d is a deuterated solvent used in NMR spectroscopy to provide stable signal locking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a deuterated solvent used in NMR spectroscopy to dissolve samples for analysis, known for its characteristic peak used for chemical shift referencing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform-D is a deuterated solvent used for dissolving and resuspending polymers in chemical analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEUTERATED CHLOROFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deuterated chloroform is used as a reference in NMR spectral analysis, indicating its importance in chemical shift standards."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer in this context refers to the substance being analyzed for end group changes using NMR after extraction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a large molecule composed of repeated subunits, like those in PS, PVC, and LDPE, affecting the mealworms' digestion processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating structural units. In the context of the text, polystyrene is the specific polymer being studied for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are large molecules composed of repeating subunits, forming materials like plastics which are often resistant to degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymers are substances with molecular chain structures that constitute plastic foams like PS and PE, which were degraded in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0</data>
    </node>
