    <node id="&quot;SPCR&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPCR stands for Specific LDPE Consumption Rate, which measures how much LDPE is consumed by the larvae in specified conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"SPCR, or specific polymer consumption rate, quantifies the rate at which larvae consume PS over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"SPCR stands for Specific Plastic Consumption Rate, which measures the rate at which mealworms consume polystyrene microplastics per 100 larvae per day."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific Polystyrene Consumption Rate is a measure used to quantify the rate at which mealworms consume PS microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC SAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deionized water is used to rinse plastic samples before analysis, ensuring cleanliness and removal of ions."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotics are compounds used to supplement the diet of larvae, affecting the gut bacterial community and metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that inhibit the growth of or destroy microorganisms, investigated here for their residual effects on mealworm microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances used to inhibit the growth of or destroy bacteria and sometimes have adverse effects on the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substances like gentamicin used in mealworm studies to understand the role of gut bacteria in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substances used to suppress the gut microbiome to study its role in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substances used to treat living specimens of larvae, potentially affecting their polyethylene degradation behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substances that have an effect on microbial community, influencing the composition and activity of gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are used in suppression assays to determine the role of gut microbiota in the degradation of Styrofoam by superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are tested for their effect on gut bacterial growth, providing context for studies on microbial degraders like strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics mentioned include ampicillin, chloramphenicol, erythromycin, gentamicin, tetracycline, and vancomycin. They were used in a screening test to inhibit mealworm gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics such as ampicillin and tetracycline are used to suppress microbial activity, helping to demonstrate the role of specific microbes in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics, when used to suppress microbial communities in the gut of insects, disrupt the plastic degradation process, indicating the critical role of gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that inhibit the growth of or kill microorganisms; used in the study to impair gut microbiota, affecting nitrogen fixation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAN-SHAN YANG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shan-Shan Yang contributed to the study's conceptualization, methodology, supervision, validation, and writing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shan-Shan Yang is one of the authors who contributed to the study on polystyrene digestion in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shan-Shan Yang worked on data curation and formal analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEI-MIN WU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Wei-Min Wu is a Guest Professor at Tongji University mentioned for their contribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is one of the authors involved in the research on the biodegradation capabilities of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu was involved in data curation, formal analysis, and writing review and editing for the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu was involved in conceptualization, methodology, supervision, validation, drafting, and editing of the research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834</data>
    </node>
