      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PetCo Pet Store Chain is a provider of mealworms used in biodegradation studies, indicating its role in the supply chain for research purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PETSMART PET STORE CHAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PetSmart Pet Store Chain is another provider of mealworms for the biodegradation research, offering a separate source of specimens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIMBERLINE FISHERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Timberline Fisheries supplies mealworms to various pet stores, contributing to the availability of specimens for scientific studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\({ }^{13} \MATHRM{CH}_{4}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Labeled methane may be part of the mineralization process of polystyrene in mealworms, indicating a path of biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;W.-M. WU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"W.-M. Wu is a co-author affiliated with Stanford University, who organized a global survey on mealworm polystyrene consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED (FTIR) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to identify chemical modifications in polystyrene as a result of mealworm digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a method to visualize chemical changes in materials by measuring absorbance spectra."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is used alongside thermogravimetric analysis to characterize thermal degradation properties of fecula and Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technique used to identify primary functional groups in polyethylene microplastics during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is an analytical technique used to obtain an infrared spectrum of absorption, emission, or photoconductivity of a solid, liquid, or gas. It is used here to characterize chemical modifications in polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL ROLE OF GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut bacteria are crucial in the depolymerization and degradation of polystyrene in mealworms, demonstrating a significant role in the process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANFORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stanford is one of the locations where mealworms were incubated for studies on plastic consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTHERN IRELAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Northern Ireland is a location where mealworms were studied for their plastic consumption behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"China is one of the regions where mealworms were incubated and studied for plastic degradation activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"China is the location where the mealworms and plastic feedstocks were sourced, including companies in Shandong and Guangdong."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
