      <data key="d2">chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHATASES, ESTERASES, LEUCINE ARYLAMIDASE, Β-GALACTOSIDASE, Β-GLUCURONIDASE, Α-GLUCOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes involved in the biodegradation of plastics within the mealworms' gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"H2O, or water, is crucial for the hydration and metabolic processes in organisms, affecting PS biodegradation and microbe activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water (H2O) was shown to significantly improve the biodegradation process of polystyrene monomers and oligomers, aiding identification in frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"H2O, or water, is included in Diet 2 and impacts the biodegradation process and molecular weight reduction of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAN:PS DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diet composed of bran and polystyrene tested at different ratios (4:1 and 20:1) to study its effect on the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORMS' GUT MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut microbiome of mealworms, which contributes to the accelerated biodegradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-GLUCOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme involved in the degradation process of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"α-glucosidase is an enzyme that hydrolyzes alpha bonds of alpha-glucosides, releasing glucose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-MANNOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme that plays a role in the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"α-mannosidase is an enzyme involved in the breakdown of complex sugars, catalyzing the hydrolysis of terminal, non-reducing alpha-D-mannose residues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-FUCOSIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme engaged in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"α-fucosidase is an enzyme responsible for the hydrolysis of α-fucose residues in glycosides."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROCOCCUS SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species of bacteria found abundantly in the gut of T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROSPIRA DEFLUVII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium present in the gut microbiome aiding in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrospira defluvii is a bacterial species reported as abundant in mealworms in prior studies when fed with polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrospira defluvii is associated with polystyrene degradation in the PS-fed gut microbiome, playing a part in the aerobic degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROPIONIBACTERIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria found in the digestive systems of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propionibacterium is detected as the most abundant genus in some studies of the mealworm gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STREPTOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus contributing to the microbial community in mealworms' gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streptococcus is found in the digestive systems of mealworms as part of the bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streptococcus is a genus of bacteria identified in termites, known for aiding in lignin degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Streptococcus is one of the genera with high abundance in PS- and CS-fed larvae, associated with plastic and lignocellulose degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAEMOPHILUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria found in the microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAPHYLOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria with significant presence in the gut microbiome, affected by host diet and environmental parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus participating in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus forms part of the bacterial community in mealworms, contributing to the diversity noted in microbiome studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus is enriched in the gut microbiome of CS-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus representing part of the microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is identified within the mealworm microbiome according to research focused on bacterial community characterization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria whose presence was observed in the digestive system of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is another dominant genus found in the gut microbial communities of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria found in the digestive system and involved in the response to bran and polyethylene diet in mealworm gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria significantly associated with the PE + bran diet, suggesting a role in the gut microbiome's adaptation to varying diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is associated with the PE + bran diet, contributing to adjusting and maintaining the health of the mealworm gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a beneficial genus of gut microbiota in mealworms, aiding in digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSTRIDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial genus part of the gut microbiome composition, showing response to dietary changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus found in the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is an anaerobic bacterium stimulated by large amounts of indigestible nutrients and involves in producing short-chain fatty acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium, detected in mealworm studies, illustrates part of the bacterial diversity found within their digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found in the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor larvae, negatively correlated with PS diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of gram-positive bacteria known for their roles in fermentation and energy production, some of which are pathogenic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria known for its role in intestinal microbial functions and possibly involved in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus with varying levels of abundance in the mealworm gut microbiome due to dietary alterations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is an anaerobic bacterial genus from mealworms, potentially involved in foam biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of anaerobes found in the hindgut of mealworms and part of the diverse microbiota involved in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found in the guts of nitrogen-fixing insects, capable of participating in nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a well-known bacterial genus including species capable of nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria predominating in mealworm larvae fed with bran, affecting the gut microbiota composition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM (PS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of plastic consumed and biodegraded by the mealworm gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION OF PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation of PS describes the degradation of PS foam by Tenebrio molitor larvae, evidenced by a shift in molecular weight distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) is evaluated by observing its consumption and breakdown by T. molitor larvae under different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process involving biological agents breaking down Styrofoam or polystyrene into simpler molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605</data>
    </node>
