    <node id="&quot;PYROLYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical recycling process where plastics are decomposed under high temperatures in anaerobic conditions to produce biofuel."&lt;SEP&gt;"A thermochemical decomposition of materials at elevated temperatures, often used in the recycling of plastic wastes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermochemical decomposition of organic material at elevated temperatures in the absence of oxygen, crucial for breaking down plastics like LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is the thermal decomposition of materials at elevated temperatures in an inert atmosphere, utilized to study weight loss and chemical changes in polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermal decomposition process occurring at high temperatures, leading to mass loss and combustion in mealworm fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a process used to mitigate microplastics in sewage sludge, with the role of pyrolysis temperature being a key factor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a thermochemical decomposition process used to convert organic material, such as sewage sludge, into usable products in the absence of oxygen, studied for its role in mitigating microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
    </node>
