    <node id="&quot;BENZENE RING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A benzene ring is a common functional group in organic chemistry known for its stable symmetry and aromatic properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benzene rings are chemical structures observed in polymers, whose integrity is assessed before and after exposure to mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benzene Ring is a stable chemical structure within polystyrene that is broken down during the biodegradation process by certain insect larvae such as yellow mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"The benzene ring is a chemical structure in PS that is destroyed by the gut microbes of yellow mealworm, indicating strong depolymerization capability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The benzene ring is a fundamental component of aromatic compounds, involved in the bonding with the nitrogen element as indicated in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f102938f307d7404d3f31b7200d93768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
