    <node id="&quot;PU1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific type of polyurethane plastic that was part of the biodegradation experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of polyurethane used in experiments, noted for high concentrations of calcium and silicon."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU1 is a type of polyurethane foam with a smooth and flat surface, which becomes wrinkled after passing through the insect digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU1 refers to a polyurethane kitchen sponge characterized by high concentrations of Calcium, Aluminum, Silicon, and Chlorine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane variant 1 (PU1) is one of the types of plastics being consumed and reduced in mass by mealworms in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
    </node>
