      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of polyurethane with notable chlorine and phosphorus content, associated with flame retardant additives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another variant of polyurethane plastic involved in biodegradation trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU2 is another form of polyurethane foam that initially has more edges than PU1, which become smoother after insect digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU2 refers to a different polyurethane material from PU1, notable for high Chlorine and Phosphorus content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane variant 2 (PU2) is one of the types of plastics being consumed and reduced in mass by mealworms in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9</data>
