    <node id="&quot;PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Generally refers to materials such as PS, PU1, PU2, and PE, each with distinct elemental compositions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials made from polymers, such as polyethylene, known for their durability and resistance to environmental degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Materials subject to biodegradation in the study, with varying effectiveness depending on their micron size and chemical composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic polymers widely used globally, causing environmental concerns due to their persistence in the ecosystem when not properly managed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics refer to synthetic polymers such as polyethylene, polystyrene, and polyvinyl chloride, which are commonly used and pose environmental challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials made from polymers and are widely used in various applications. They can be challenging to biodegrade and constitute a significant environmental concern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials affecting environmental and metabolic processes, serving as potential resources in scientific exploration for biotransformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials used extensively in various industries, but their accumulation in landfills and oceans poses significant environmental challenges like pollution and toxicity."</data>
