    <node id="&quot;T. OBSCURUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">T. obscurus, commonly known as Dark mealworms, is a species of darkling beetle larvae recognized for its significant contributions to biodegradation studies, specifically targeting plastic waste management. This species has been extensively researched for its ability to depolymerize and biodegrade various plastics, including polystyrene (PS) foam and multiple forms of polyethylene (PE), such as low-density polyethylene (LDPE), linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE), and high-density polyethylene (HDPE). The larvae's plastic degradation capabilities are largely attributed to adaptations in their gut microbiome, which enhances the breakdown process. 

In comparative studies, T. obscurus has demonstrated greater efficiency in polystyrene biodegradation than its relative, T. molitor, yielding better results in consuming and degrading PS foam. Additionally, these beetle larvae are capable of consuming lignocellulosic materials, showcasing their versatility in diet and biodegradation potential. The consistent outcomes across studies have positioned T. obscurus as a valuable model organism in the field of ecological research, especially in understanding plastic depolymerization and the associated shifts in microbial communities.

Aside from ecological benefits, T. obscurus is also studied for its potential as a sustainable protein source, offering a dual advantage in environmental conservation and food supply. Across various research efforts conducted primarily in the United States, T. obscurus stands out as a robust entity contributing to innovative solutions in plastic waste reduction and sustainable waste management strategies, thereby helping mitigate global plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-109486cd939a227e73354d0478c59ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6</data>
    </node>
