    <node id="&quot;CORN FLOUR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nutritional component used as a normal diet for T. obscurus, providing sufficient nutrients and carbon for growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is added in experiments to improve the degradation of PS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Used as a dietary supplement for T. obscurus, impacting polystyrene consumption rates during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour was used as a component of the diet for a group of mealworms to compare the effects of different feeds on their ability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is added to the diet of larvae along with polystyrene to study its effect on the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corn flour is used as a co-feed for Tenebrio obscurus larvae to enhance their PS consumption rates."</data>
