    <node id="&quot;PU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU (Polyurethane) is a plastic material degraded by specific bacteria found in the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU stands for polyurethane, a polymer that was significantly consumed and degraded in the study by mealworms and associated microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PU), a polymer subject to degradation by microorganisms and extracellular enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane, often abbreviated as PU, is a type of plastic used for a variety of applications including kitchen sponges and insulation foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is presumably a product mentioned alongside PP and EVA, although no additional context is provided."</data>
