    <node id="&quot;CROP GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
      <data key="d1">"An increase in plant biomass and yield, which can be influenced by fertilizers such as mealworm frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm frass used as a fertilizer enhances crop growth, illustrating the agricultural application of insect by-products."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEWAGE SLUDGE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microplastics are found in sewage sludge, indicating environmental contamination and necessitating studies on pollution management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sewage sludge from wastewater treatment facilities can undergo fractionation and conversion processes to extract lipids for biodiesel production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Semi-solid waste generated in the treatment of wastewater, which serves as a medium for microplastics biodegradation using hyperthermophilic composting technology."</data>
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERWORMS (ZOPHOBAS MORIO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superworms are voracious agricultural insect pests that consume polystyrene at higher rates than mealworms, providing nutritional value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superworms, the larvae of the beetle Zophobas morio, can feed on plastics, contributing to their biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORM FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Worm frass is the nutrient-rich excrement of worms, capable of substituting traditional fertilizers, supporting plant growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worm frass refers to the waste material excreted by both superworms and mealworms, used as a plant growth medium in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
