    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUCROSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sucrose is a commonly used insect attractant added as a food additive in experiments to enhance the consumption of polystyrene (PS) by worms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a sugar additive used in the study to enhance PS consumption by superworms and mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a sugar found effective in increasing mealworms' PS consumption rates when used as an additive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a sugar used as a food additive in the study to increase polystyrene consumption by worms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sucrose is a sugar tested in bacteria for its ability to ferment into acid, indicating metabolic activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671dc96f9c648fdc6d21397c515d171d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN (N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen is a chemical compound found in EPS, with higher volumes present in white EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen is a chemical element essential for plant growth, found in worm frass as a nutrient alternative to traditional fertilizers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHITIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOPOLYMER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chitin is a biopolymer present in the skeletons of mealworms, affecting microbial diversity when digested."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component found in raw whole insects and is extracted and characterized for various uses, including its elicitor activity in plants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of worm frass that contributes to its potential as a natural fertilizer, replacing traditional chemical fertilizers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin, found in superworm frass, is reported to support rooting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a long-chain polymer found in the exoskeletons of arthropods, significant in biodegradation studies by organisms like mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of the insect cuticle, identified in the chemical composition of frass through resonance signals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a natural polymer found in the exoskeleton of insects, including mealworms, detected in the fecula post digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a long-chain polymer found in the exoskeletons of insects and crustaceans, and in the cell walls of fungi, important for structural integrity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a long-chain polymer that forms part of the exoskeleton of arthropods and is ingested by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK SOLDIER FLY FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Black Soldier Fly Frass is studied as a novel fertilizer for enhanced maize growth, yield, and nitrogen use efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black Soldier Fly frass is a type of insect excrement shown to support plant growth, demonstrating the potential of insect frass as fertilizer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </node>
