      <data key="d2">chunk-671dc96f9c648fdc6d21397c515d171d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERWORM FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superworm frass is the waste produced by superworms, studied for its impact on cacti growth and rooting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superworm frass supports superior rooting and growth compared to other media and is recommended over mealworm frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CACTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS,FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cacti are used in the study to test the effect of worm frass on plant growth and rooting efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;9-OLEAMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"9-Oleamide is a fatty acid primary amide detected in the frass from the worms fed on PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEA LEAVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tea leaves are used as a control medium for comparing the effects on cacti growth alongside worm frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DI WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DI (Deionized) Water is used to ensure adherence of additives to PS balls in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"DI Water, or deionized water, is used as a negative control in experiments to measure hydrophobicity of supernatant fractions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deionized water used as a control for testing supernatant hydrophobicity in contact angle analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deionized water used to prepare LB medium and in other experimental procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHORT CHAIN ALKANES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Short chain alkanes were detected in the frass of worms fed on PS, indicating chemical processes within the frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alcohols are among the chemical compounds detected in the frass of worms fed on PS, indicating metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic compounds featuring a hydroxyl group (-OH) bonded to carbon atoms, indicated by stretching vibration peaks during analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYCLOALKANES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
