      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZYL GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzyl groups were found in the PS balls used in the study, detected as part of the chemical analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE DECAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene decay is the process of breaking down polystyrene, a type of plastic, assisted by microbial and enzymatic activity of worms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC-MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC-MS (Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry) is utilized to detect metabolic intermediates during the degradation of feedstocks by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"GC-MS, or Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry, is used for analyzing chemical compositions, such as detecting changes in worm-fed plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry, a method used to identify intermediates in PS- and CS-fed larvae analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry (GC-MS) is a technology used for determining fatty acid content in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURIER-TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY (FTIR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An analytical technique used to obtain spectra of PP foam and frass samples for chemical characterization."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is a technique used to obtain an infrared spectrum of absorption or emission of a solid, liquid, or gas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy is an analytical technique used to obtain infrared spectrum absorption or emission of a solid, liquid, or gas sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is an analytical method used to verify the formation of oxidized functional groups in polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16</data>
