    <node id="&quot;MICROPLASTIC POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL ISSUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microplastic pollution consists of tiny plastic debris affecting various aquatic systems including large lakes, oceans, and marine ecosystems worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the contamination of environments, particularly oceans and seas, by microplastics, which have detrimental effects on marine life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the contamination of ecosystems, particularly due to the breakdown of plastic products like face masks into smaller particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution is a major environmental issue stemming from plastic waste that affects numerous ecosystems and organisms across the globe."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution is the accumulation of tiny plastic particles in the environment, and studies on Tenebrio larvae microbiome offer insights into potential remediation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de</data>
