      <data key="d1">"Microorganisms residing in the gut of mealworms play a crucial role in the degradation of EPS. They potentially release extracellular oxidative enzymes that assist in this biological process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms residing in the gut that contribute to various metabolic processes, including the breakdown of ingested materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"These microorganisms reside in the guts of larval insects and contribute to the biodegradation of microplastics."</data>
