    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. YT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the intestine of yellow mealworms that achieves significant degradation over a 60-day incubation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium isolated from the mealworm gut microbiome, known for its PS-degrading capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is the first identified microorganism capable of degrading EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Displays high biodegradation ability at 28.6%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the gut of mealworms, with a notable capacity to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the guts of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated in studies aimed at understanding polystyrene degradation."</data>
