      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental stresses refer to factors or conditions in the environment that can influence an organism’s ability to survive and reproduce."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOST-SPECIFIC METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Host-specific metabolism is the specialized metabolic processes that occur within organisms coexisting with hosts, optimizing for conditions provided by the host."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOOKMIN UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
