      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R&amp;D PROGRAM FOR FOREST SCIENCE TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R&amp;D Program for Forest Science Technology is a project supporting forest-related scientific and technological research in Korea."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOREMEDIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An environmental process aimed at using biological organisms such as identified bacteria to degrade pollutants like nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a process that uses microorganisms or biological agents to break down or neutralize hazardous substances or contaminants in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a strategy using biological entities to detoxify and break down hazardous substances from plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is an ecological process used to treat and remediate contaminated agricultural soils, specifically those affected by petroleum crude."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using microorganisms to remove pollutants from the environment, such as plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"The use of microorganisms or other biological agents to remove or neutralize contaminants from a polluted area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation refers to the process of using organisms, often microbes, to detoxify and restore polluted and contaminated environments including soils and water sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation uses living organisms to naturally degrade environmental pollutants, in this context, plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a process that uses microorganisms to degrade environmental pollutants like PS, offering solutions for waste management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043ac4479b542b2eb2620db8d408349b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAGENOMIC SEQUENCE ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metagenomic Sequence Analysis is a process that involves the study and clustering of genetic material from environmental samples to understand microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87</data>
    </node>
