      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TGA Curves refers to Thermogravimetric Analysis, a method of thermal analysis in which changes in physical and chemical properties of materials are measured as a function of increasing temperature, indicating changes before and after biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DSC CURVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DSC Curves, or Differential Scanning Calorimetry, is a thermo-analytical technique used to study thermal transitions of polystyrene, showing changes before and after biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XRD PATTERNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"XRD Patterns refer to X-ray diffraction patterns used to identify crystalline materials and analyze the structure of polystyrene before and after biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAMAN SPECTRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Raman Spectra refers to a spectroscopic technique used to observe vibrational, rotational, and other low-frequency modes in a system, analyzing polystyrene before and after biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UV-VIS SPECTRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"UV-Vis Spectra refers to Ultraviolet-visible spectroscopy, a method used to determine the absorption or reflectance in the ultraviolet-visible spectral region, applied to polystyrene before and after biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR SPECTRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR Spectra provide data indicating the different chemical components of evolved gaseous compounds produced during the thermal decomposition of fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR Spectra refers to Nuclear Magnetic Resonance spectroscopy, a technique to observe the magnetic properties of certain nuclei, examining polystyrene before and after biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055</data>
    </node>
