      <data key="d2">chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mz refers to the z average molecular weight of polymers, analyzed during the gel permeation chromatography process in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mz represents the size-average molecular weight, indicating the highest molecular weight portion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mz stands for the z-average molecular weight of a polymer, indicating changes in polymer structure after exposure to larvae digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z-average molecular weight (Mz) is used to describe the molecular weight distribution of PS residues after being processed by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP (POLYPROPYLENE) CONTAINERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
