      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUANTIFLUOR TM-ST BLUE FLUORESCENCE QUANTIFICATION SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The QuantiFluor system is used for quantifying DNA samples using fluorescence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UCHIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOOL/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tool used to identify and remove chimeric sequences from genetic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"UCHIME is a bioinformatics tool that improves the sensitivity and speed of chimera detection in sequence data analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"UCHIME is a software tool for identifying and removing chimeric sequences in DNA sequencing data."&lt;SEP&gt;"UCHIME is a tool used to identify and remove chimeric sequences in sequence data analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"UCHIME is a process used to identify and remove chimeric sequences during DNA sequence analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RDP CLASSIFIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RDP Classifier is a tool for taxonomic classification of 16S rRNA gene sequences against a database."&lt;SEP&gt;"RDP classifier is a software tool used to classify 16 S rRNA gene sequences against the Silva database."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ribosomal Database Project (RDP) classifier is a tool for assigning taxonomy to 16S rRNA gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVA 16 S RRNA DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Silva 16 S rRNA database is a reference database used for classifying microbial gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLWEGENE CLOUD PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Allwegene Cloud platform is an online platform used for analyzing microbial community data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBALIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannibalization is observed in T. molitor larvae as a survival strategy under nutrient-limited conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-1 is a sample of polyethylene used in the study to evaluate its depolymerization in the presence of gentamicin."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-1 is a specific variant of LDPE whose depolymerization pattern was observed to be similar to that of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-1 is a type of LDPE foam used in biodegradation experiments with T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-1 is a specific variant of polyethylene used in the study to measure the extent of depolymerization under different conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-1 refers to one type of low-density polyethylene foam used in the study to assess larval consumption and degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-2 is another form of polyethylene assessed for its depolymerization during antibiotic treatment on different days."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is another variant of LDPE foam studied for its impact on survival and cannibal rates in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is another variant of LDPE foam with unique depolymerization characteristics compared to PE-1."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is another variant of polyethylene used to assess depolymerization in larvae, providing comparative data against PE-1."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 refers to another type of low-density polyethylene foam utilized in this research for similar purposes as PE-1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSSTART FASTPFU DNA POLYMERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TransStart Fastpfu DNA Polymerase is an enzyme used in PCR to amplify DNA sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXYPREP DNA GEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AxyPrep DNA gel is used to recover PCR products after electrophoresis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTROPHORESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used for separating DNA fragments based on size during analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electrophoresis is a technique used to separate DNA fragments by size for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electrophoresis is a laboratory technique used for separating molecules, which can be used to analyze changes in biological samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electrophoresis is a method used to separate DNA, RNA, or proteins based on size and is used here for analyzing PCR products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHIMERIC SEQUENCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chimeric sequences are artificial DNA sequences formed from combined fragments, identified and removed in analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sequences formed by combining two or more different genetic sequences, removed during analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIERARCHICAL CLUSTER ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hierarchical cluster analysis is a statistical method used in the study to understand the microbial community composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis is used to group gut bacterial communities based on the diet of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis is used to group similar microbial communities based on genetic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERNARY ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ternary analysis is a statistical method for analyzing composition data, used in microbial community studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ternary analysis is used to explore compositional data of microbial communities in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"During starvation, insects utilize endogenous proteins as a source of energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation in this context describes the physiological response of organisms, like larvae, to insufficient food availability, affecting metabolic rates and energy distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a condition where an organism experiences a deficit in energy intake, influencing metabolic and structural changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is one of the eight feeding conditions in the experiment where mealworms are not fed any additional sustenance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation occurs in mealworms when they are unable to access adequate nutrients from polystyrene materials like PS and PSr, leading to the breakdown of stored energy sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to the condition of T. molitor larvae when deprived of essential nutrients, affecting development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation triggers significant metabolic adaptations in mealworms, affecting nutrient levels and energy reserves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation refers to a diet condition where T. molitor is deprived of sufficient nutrients, affecting its growth and pupation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBAL RATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannibal Rates indicate the frequency of cannibalistic behavior among the larvae under different diet conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION RATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation Rates are the percentage of larvae that successfully transition to the pupal stage under different diet conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rates refer to the percentage of larvae transitioning to pupae, measured to evaluate the effects of different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION OF LDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation of LDPE involves the breakdown of LDPE foam by Tenebrio molitor larvae, as indicated by changes in molecular weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE (25°C)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature (25°C) is the condition under which the tests on the larvae's consumption and biodegradation were conducted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC FOAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic Foams encompass EPS, LDPE, and PS materials tested for larval consumption and depolymerization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIGURE 1D&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESEARCH ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Figure 1D illustrates the accumulated consumption of PS and PE-1 by the larvae over a 60-day period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CFU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colony Forming Units (CFUs) are used to quantify viable bacterial or fungal cells in the microbial community analysis of the T. molitor larvae gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Forming Units, used as a measure for counting viable gut microorganisms per gut in the biodegradation study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONMETRIC MULTIDIMENSIONAL SCALING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used in this study to analyze the variation in microbial communities based on weighted UniFrac metrics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-biodegradation is the process of breaking down polyethylene (PE) by environmental or biological means, including microbial activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL DIGESTIVE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larval digestive system is a biological structure aiding in digestion and potentially influencing biodegradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO GENUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrio is a genus of beetles known for their ability to degrade plastic polymers such as polystyrene (PS) and low-density polyethylene (LDPE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tenebrio genus includes insects like T. molitor and T. obscurus, both of which show potential for plastic biodegradation with gut microbe dependence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tenebrio genus includes mealworms that have shown capability in biodegrading plastics such as polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species of invertebrates being considered for study in microplastic-induced oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae known for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene and low-density polyethylene, with studies showing the involvement of gut microbiota and microbial functional enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae, also known as superworms, are capable of biodegrading plastics such as EPS and LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae of the Zophobas atratus beetle, also known as superworms, which are capable of biodegrading certain plastics like polystyrene and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae, known as superworms, have been studied for their ability to depolymerize LDPE foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae contribute to degrading polystyrene (PS) through the combined effect of reactive oxygen species and extracellular oxidase produced by their gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae of a species of beetle investigated for their potential to degrade plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae are known for biodegrading polystyrene and low-density polyethylene into microplastics, also affecting their gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae, a species known to degrade plastics, are mentioned as candidates for further study on microplastic-induced oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as superworms, these larvae are used for the biodegradation of polystyrene and polyethylene, affecting gut microbiota and microbial enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COPROCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coprococcus is a genus of anaerobic gut cocci that show significant abundance changes in the gut flora of larvae fed on different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORGANELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morganella is a bacterium whose relative abundance increased in the gut microbial community of yellow mealworms after ingesting masks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a genus of bacteria whose increased abundance is noted in the inner-fed group of mealworms, strongly correlating with the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a genus of gut microbes found to decrease in abundance in larvae fed with PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a genus of Gram-negative bacteria, some species of which are involved in human urinary tract infections. Its abundance in genus level is analyzed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain isolated from mealworm gut, capable of biodegrading high-density polyethylene (HDPE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. increased in T. molitor larvae fed with polystyrene, indicating a potential role in PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a genus of bacteria found at low levels in all diet-fed larvae, known for their diverse metabolic capacities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterial genus involved in the growth kinetics and biodeterioration of polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genus of bacteria enriched in the gut of PP-L-fed T. molitor larvae, potentially involved in PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterium associated with the metabolism of low molecular weight polypropylene in Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a genus of bacteria observed in larvae during the degradation of different molecular weights of PP and also plays a role in lignocellulose degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus is a genus of bacteria present in the guts of lignocellulose-feeding insects, involved in degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus species are bacteria involved in microbiome studies, particularly with Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacteria indigenous to the Niger Delta mangrove swamp, capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterium species isolated from mangrove sediment, known for its ability to contribute to the biodeterioration of polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterium that has shown ability to biodegrade polypropylene under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. refers to a genus of bacteria that are gram-positive, rod-shaped, and capable of producing endospores, often involved in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus is a genus of bacteria identified in the intestines of mealworms with the capability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMDS ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
