    <node id="&quot;LUMBRICUS TERRESTRIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species within the Lumbricidae family affected by microplastics in terrestrial ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbricus terrestris, commonly known as earthworms, whose gut bacteria are capable of degrading microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbricus terrestris, known as the common earthworm, can incorporate microplastics into its burrows, indicating environmental interaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbricus terrestris, also known as the common earthworm, is capable of fragmenting and depolymerizing various types of microplastics in its digestive tract."</data>
