    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A degradation process involving the reaction of a material with oxygen, leading to the breakdown of polymer chains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative degradation refers to the breakdown of materials through reactions involving oxygen, often leading to changes in the molecular weight and properties of substrates like LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"A process in which oxygen interacts with other substances to produce various degradative effects, particularly in plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative degradation is a chemical reaction where substances are broken down due to the interaction with oxygen, often leading to changes in physical and chemical properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc</data>
    </node>
