    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM GUT MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mealworm gut microbiome consists of a diverse community of microorganisms capable of facilitating the degradation of plastic polymers, such as polystyrene (PS), in a gut environment enriched with secreted factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome consists of microorganisms capable of metabolizing specific carbon sources, like PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community within mealworm guts that may synergistically enhance plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community within mealworms' intestines, crucial for the biodegradation of plastics such as PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome consists of diverse microorganisms within the mealworms that contribute to the breakdown of polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome includes various bacteria that aid in digestion, with its diversity being influenced by diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms residing within the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor, influencing its ability to degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome is capable of degrading plastics such as PE and PS, highlighting its potential in biodegradation research."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome plays a critical role in the biodegradation of plastics like polyethylene and polystyrene, showcasing diverse microbial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut microbiome refers to the diverse community of microorganisms inhabiting the mealworm's digestive tract, influenced by diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba</data>
    </node>
