    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal Microbiome comprises the microorganisms residing in the gut of insect larvae, which alter in diversity and function when fed polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiome is the complex community of microorganisms residing in the intestines, playing a crucial role in digestion and nutrient absorption."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Intestinal Microbiome is a community of microorganisms in the intestines of organisms like Galleria mellonella, which play a critical role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The intestinal microbiome refers to the specific collection of microorganisms inhabiting the intestines, influencing various biological processes, including plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The collection of microorganisms within mealworms, affecting their ability to digest plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiome refers to the microorganisms, including bacteria, residing in the intestines, significant in analyzing the effects of plastic diet in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
