    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROCARBON DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrocarbon degradation is a process involving the breakdown of hydrocarbons by microorganisms like Brevibacterium sp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbon degradation refers to the chemical process of breaking down hydrocarbons, often through microbial activity, observed in LDPE biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown of hydrocarbons by microbial action, often enhanced by surfactants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbon degradation refers to the breakdown of hydrocarbons by microorganisms, often used in the context of bioremediation in environments contaminated with petroleum or other hydrocarbon pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"This process involves the breakdown of hydrocarbons by bacterial degraders, important in removing pollutants from environments such as petroleum-contaminated areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043ac4479b542b2eb2620db8d408349b</data>
    </node>
