    <node id="&quot;CO2&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO2 emission was a measure observed to assess the PS metabolic activity of bacterial strains and control."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2 is a gaseous metabolite produced as a result of the mineralization of Styrofoam in superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2, or carbon dioxide, is a byproduct of metabolism that is measured in studies of superworms consuming Styrofoam to analyze their metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide emissions are a consideration in the lifecycle assessment of plastic waste treatment and biodiesel production."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gas chromatograph measures CO2 concentration, providing data on microbial respiration and activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2 is a product of the mineralization and degradation of Styrofoam in the mealworm gut system."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2, carbon dioxide, is produced as a result of the mineralization of polystyrene within the mealworm gut, representing a waste product and energy source."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2 or carbon dioxide is produced as a result of Styrofoam degradation by mealworms, providing a traceable marker of metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2 is produced as a putative gas fraction from the biodegradation of ingested polyethylene by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2 is the final metabolite of PS degradation, whose concentration in the headspace increases as microbial activity progresses under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2, or carbon dioxide, is a byproduct of the metabolic processes involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene by LG3, with its concentration monitored during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide (CO2) is a gaseous metabolite produced through the biodegradation of LDPE by T. molitor and T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a gas released during the biodegradation process when organic materials are broken down."</data>
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
    </node>
