      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serratia is a bacterial genus identified in the mealworm microbiome with potential in bioplastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia is a genus of bacteria dominant in the gut microbiome of PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serratia is a bacterium associated with PE diets in the greater wax moth larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degradation in this context refers to the microbial process of breaking down polyethylene films into smaller molecular components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Degradation refers to the breakdown of complex molecules like polystyrene into simpler substances, a process explored in the microbiome of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Degradation is the process by which microorganisms, including the gut bacteria of T. molitor and other fungi and bacteria, break down plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which materials like polyurethane are broken down by natural means, such as through microbial action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Degradation refers to the breakdown of polyethylene microplastics by mealworm larvae observed in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9</data>
    </node>
