    <node id="&quot;BACTERIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteriome is a term describing the collective symbiotic bacteria residing within hosts like insects, often forming specialized organs to aid various biological functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bacteriome is a large symbiotic organ composed of aggregated microorganisms present in insects. It plays a crucial role in their digestive processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90</data>
    </node>
