    <node id="&quot;OATMEAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A control food used in the experiment for mealworms, used to compare against other polystyrene diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal was used as a control diet for one group of larvae to provide a comparison against those fed with polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal serves as a control diet in the experiment, providing a baseline for evaluating the effects of polymer diets on mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal was used as a control diet for mealworms to compare protein concentration against those fed polystyrene materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is used as a control diet for mealworms, providing a standard reference for measuring mass and nutrient changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is used as a control food in studies, providing a baseline for comparing lipid content in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is provided as a nutritional supplement every 10 days to some larvae groups in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is used as a dietary supplement in the experiment to influence the survival and development of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is used as a food component in the Control and PS + Oat. diet groups for T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
