    <node id="&quot;PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An essential nutrient that constitutes the main biochemical analysis focus, with levels measured in mealworms fed on different polystyrene species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are a major nutritional component high in yellow mealworms, contributing to their relevance as animal feed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins in mealworm larvae are affected by different diets, with the polystyrene diet showing higher protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are essential macromolecules studied in various organisms, including mealworms and bighead carp, for their dietary effects and biodegradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins in mealworms are not significantly affected by the food type, suggesting that protein synthesis remains stable even during deprivation, although there are indications that it could decrease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are macronutrients found in yeast, aiding the growth and development of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are essential nutrients included in feed to positively affect the growth and development of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macromolecules consisting of one or more long chains of amino acids, essential for various biological functions such as structuring tissues and catalyzing reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUGARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of nutrient measured in mealworms to assess the impact of different polystyrene diets on total sugar content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simple carbohydrates detectable in mosquitoes using rapid determination methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugars are important nutrients for sustaining organs, particularly the nervous system, and their levels decrease in mealworms fed with less digestible polystrene types like PS and PSr."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCESSED POLYSTYRENE (PSR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A recycled form of polystyrene whose dietary effect on mealworms was assessed, involving recycling processes affecting material properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Processed Polystyrene (PSr) refers to polystyrene that has undergone further processing for specific experiment conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Processed Polystyrene is polystyrene that has undergone extrusion, injection molding, and grinding, enhancing its form for various applications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PACKING POLYSTYRENE (PSP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A commercial type of polystyrene used for parcels, tested as a dietary component for mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECYCLING PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method involving the transformation of materials, highlighted in the context of polystyrene, notably affecting the MFR and properties of PSr."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELT FLOW RATIO (MFR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indicator of possible differences in molecular structure of materials, with low values obtained for PSp and higher for PSr and EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melt flow ratio is a parameter used to characterize the viscosity of polymers, aiding in understanding the processing characteristics of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS INCREASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Observed in control mealworms fed with oatmeal and imagines indicating normal development in absence of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONE-WAY ANOVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical method used to identify differences between groups, applied here to analyze biodegradation and larvae growth data."&lt;SEP&gt;"A statistical test applied to assess differences in protein, sugar, and lipid content among various feeding types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVED LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms deprived of food other than the assigned polystyrene type, resulting in specific metabolic responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starved larvae refers to larvae undergoing starvation, resulting in significant changes to their fat levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starved larvae are mealworms that were not fed and used in studies to compare the effects of starvation versus consuming certain materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSp is a type of packaging polystyrene material that is readily consumed by mealworms, leading to efficient biodegradation similar to EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSp is a type of plastic material characterized by its lower hardness and greater availability for mealworm consumption compared to other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSp is another form of polystyrene used in the study to understand its impact on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSp refers to a type of PolyStyrene used in food packaging, explored in the study for its mass loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSr indicates a type of raw polystyrene used in the study for feeding mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSr is a type of plastic material noted for its hardness and lower susceptibility to degradation by mealworm chewing and biting."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSr refers to a recycled variant of PolyStyrene, used in the study to assess mass loss and biochemical characteristics in different samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSr stands for processed raw polystyrene, a variant tested for biodegradation which shares similar consumption difficulties with raw PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADABLE ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradable activity is the process by which microorganisms break down plastics into simpler compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM FEEDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm feeding is the process of providing various plastic materials to mealworms to study their consumption and degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIGLYCERIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triglyceride is stored as fatty acids in mealworms and is used as a primary energy source during malnutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglyceride levels are linked with the duration of starvation in insects, indicating its role in energy storage and metabolism during periods of food scarcity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREHALOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUGAR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trehalose is a primary carbohydrate in insects that plays a crucial role in energy metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a sugar consisting of two glucose molecules, used by organisms as an energy source and stress protectant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a sugar synthesized in response to abiotic stresses in plants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCONEOGENESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gluconeogenesis is a metabolic pathway that results in the generation of glucose from certain non-carbohydrate substrates, such as hydrolyzed proteins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gluconeogenesis is the metabolic process where protein is converted to glucose, essential for mealworms' energy under certain diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIETARY POLYSTYRENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dietary Polystyrenes are used to feed mealworms to study their effects on the larvae's metabolism and microbial ecology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAENIBACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paenibacillus is a dominant bacterium in landfill sediment capable of decomposing micro-sized polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paenibacillus is a genus of bacteria that plays a role in the decomposition of micro-sized polyethylene (PE) in landfill sediments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paenibacillus is among the genera noted in the mealworm microbial communities, which vary among different studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL. (2015A, B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOURCE"</data>
