    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIONINI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrionini is a family of beetles to which the insect species Tenebrio molitor belongs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVERTEBRATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Invertebrates are organisms without a vertebral column that are affected by microplastic-induced stress responses and toxicity effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invertebrates such as mealworms are being studied for their potential role in degrading plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invertebrates, such as Tenebrio molitor, are animals without a backbone, some of which can consume and degrade synthetic materials like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invertebrates in aquatic and terrestrial environments exhibit oxidative stress and metabolic alterations due to plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMBIOTIC INTESTINAL MICROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Symbiotic Intestinal Microbes in insects like mealworms are crucial in the biodegradation of plastics such as PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are microorganisms residing in the intestines that have a symbiotic relationship with their host, contributing to the degradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS SPECTROMETRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass Spectrometry is an analytical technique used to identify the chemical alterations in the biodegradation products of PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass spectrometry is used to analyze the molecular composition of samples, with techniques like ESI and TOF-MS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL FLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal flora of yellow mealworms is influenced by the type of plastic they ingest, affecting their nutritional characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to bacterial strains isolated from yellow mealworms, capable of degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities in the gut of yellow mealworms that adapt toward those associated with LDPE biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to the community of microorganisms residing in the digestive tract, from which various PS-degrading bacteria were isolated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452</data>
