    <node id="&quot;GENOMIC DNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genomic DNA extraction and identification involve the isolation of genetic material from plastic-degrading strains for PCR amplification and sequence analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA is extracted from mealworm larval guts using enzymatic lysis, serving as a template for PCR amplification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA is extracted from mealworms to analyze gut microbiota and their role in biodegrading polystyrene, providing data on microbial species present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA refers to the total genetic material extracted from intestinal specimens for sequencing purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA from the larval guts is extracted for microbiome analysis to study the genetic material present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA is extracted from bacterial colonies for 16S rDNA amplification and identification of bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA was extracted from bacterial colonies to facilitate identification in the biodegradation study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The complete DNA sequence used for identifying and assessing the nitrogen-fixing capabilities of isolated bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic DNA refers to the complete set of DNA in a cell, used for comparison in identifying polystyrene degrading genes in bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </node>
