    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VEGAN PACKAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Vegan Package is a tool used within the R programming environment for visualizing taxonomic composition and abundance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vegan package is an R package used for ecological and community analyses, specifically applied for NMDS in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAMOND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DIAMOND is a sequence aligner for fast mapping genes against the KEGG database for functional profiling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEGG DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KEGG database is a resource for understanding high-level functions of biological systems from molecular-level information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The KEGG database provides a collection of pathways that helps understand high-level functions of biological systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S rRNA is a RNA sequence used in the phylogenetic analysis of bacteria to evaluate their evolutionary relationships and capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a component of the 16S rRNA gene sequence used to identify microbial compositions in the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a component of the 30S subunit of prokaryotic ribosomes and is used for bacterial sequencing."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S ribosomal RNA sequencing is employed to identify and differentiate bacterial species within microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a component of the ribosomal RNA gene sequence used to identify and compare different bacteria within various microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"A component of the 16S ribosomal RNA used as a marker for identifying and comparing bacteria within a community."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a component of the 30S subunit of prokaryotic ribosomes, used for phylogenetic analysis of bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is used for phylogenetic analysis to determine the taxonomic relationships of bacteria, such as WJ2020 and WJ2025."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a gene used as a marker to study bacterial communities and their changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a component of the 30S small subunit of prokaryotic ribosomes, used for phylogenetic studies and identifying bacterial species."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gene that is part of the ribosomal RNA, used to identify and classify bacteria in mealworms' gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a component of the 30S subunit of prokaryotic ribosomes and is commonly used for phylogenetic studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITS RRNA GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ITS rRNA genes refer to internal transcribed spacer regions used in fungal sequencing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMERS 343F AND 798R&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primers 343F and 798R are specific sequences used to amplify the 16S rRNA coding V3-V4 regions for bacterial analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a</data>
