      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACCASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme found to be enriched in T. molitor larvae, involved in the oxidative degradation of PP polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is a copper-binding enzyme involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, produced by the actinomycete Rhodococcus ruber."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is a lignin-degrading enzyme that has been reported to show minimal activity on polyethylene (PE) plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"An enzyme involved in oxidation reactions, capable of degrading complex polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme whose activity was measured using a spectrophotometric method."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme capable of oxidizing various substrates, including lignin, and is involved in bioremediation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme involved in the degradation of lignin and plastic, particularly important in metabolic pathways of PS- and CS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme that catalyzes the oxidation of phenolic substrates, used in lignin degradation and biotechnological applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme that facilitates the oxidation of lignin and aromatic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme that helps break down lignin and could contribute to the degradation of plastics with similar chemical structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an oxidative enzyme known to decompose polyethylene and aromatic compounds, aiding in the biodegradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"An enzyme that oxidizes phenols and is utilized in the degradation of synthetic textile dyes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laccase is an enzyme that catalyzes the oxidation of phenolic compounds, found in several bacterial isolates including Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 and Achromobacter xylosidans M9."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKANE HYDROXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme expressed in Pseudomonas sp. E4 and E. coli BL21, showing activity towards degrading low molecular weight polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UV PHOTOSENSITIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A component used to pre-treat plastic films, enhancing their susceptibility to degradation under UV light."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL CONSORTIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groups of different microorganisms working together synergistically to improve the breakdown of substances such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial consortia are groups of different microorganisms that can work together to enhance the degradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM GUTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm guts harbor a diverse and complex mixed microbial community, capable of performing nitrogen fixation and adapting to diets like Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive systems of mealworms, which host bacteria capable of degrading polyethylene films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL CONSORTIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial consortium is a group of different bacterial species working together to degrade complex substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"A consortium of bacteria utilized to improve the degradation of plastics such as polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Bacterial Consortium is a group of bacteria isolated from soil that is capable of degrading polyurethane, a plastic polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial consortium refers to a group of different bacterial species that work together to biodegrade polyvinyl chloride within the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE PARTICLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE particles are the substrate used for testing the growth and biofilm formation of bacterial strains NyZ450 and NyZ451 in incubation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene particles used as a carbon source in experiments to study degradation by isolated bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULCHING FILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mulching films made of polyethylene are used in agricultural applications for early vegetable production but present biodegradation challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pieces of polyethylene material used in the experiments as a carbon source for bacterial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SDS (Sodium dodecyl sulfate) is a detergent used to wash samples as part of preparation for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium dodecyl sulfate, used for washing PE particles and mulching films to prepare them for use in experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILE WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterile water is used to wash and rinse larvae to ensure no external contamination before analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water that is free of living microorganisms, used in the washing process of laboratory materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYSOGENY BROTH (LB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nutrient-rich medium used to culture bacteria aerobically."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON FREE BASAL MEDIUM (LCFBM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A growth medium devoid of carbon, used in experiments to emphasize the use of polyethylene as the sole carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain isolated for its potential to degrade PE and form biofilms when combined with NyZ451."&lt;SEP&gt;"An isolated bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene mulching films, identified from the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strain NyZ450 is a bacterium involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, primarily responsible for breaking down PE and utilizing it as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another isolated bacterial strain, similar to NyZ450, that can degrade polyethylene mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451 is a bacterial strain that plays a role in degrading PE when part of a consortium with strain NyZ450."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strain NyZ451 is a bacterium that plays an auxiliary role in the degradation of PE, assisting NyZ450 though with limited ability to break PE chemical bonds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-DEGRADING STRAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterial strains isolated and cultured for their ability to degrade polyethylene, emphasizing their role in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILIZED CLEAN BENCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A laboratory workspace designed to maintain a sterile environment for various experimental preparations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CFBAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CFBAM is the medium used on plates for growing bacterial strains, providing a base for interactions with PE films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon Free Basal Agar Medium used to prepare culture plates for bacterial isolation."&lt;SEP&gt;"CFBAM likely refers to a specific growth or surface medium in which biofilms are assessed, used in studying strain YT2's activities on PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cold Frosted Bio Agar Medium used to culture microorganisms during PS degradation experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
