      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to characterize and assess biofilm formation on polyethylene by the isolated bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scanning electron microscopy is a type of electron microscopy that produces images by scanning the surface with a focused beam of electrons, used to observe surface changes on polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE MULCHING FILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE mulching films are polyethylene films used in agriculture, and are the subject of biofilm formation and degradation studies using bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSORTIUM OF NYZ450 AND NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A combination of Strains NyZ450 and NyZ451, effective in significantly degrading PE mulching films by forming biofilms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The consortium consists of the collaboration between strains NyZ450 and NyZ451, essential for effective degradation of PE films."&lt;SEP&gt;"The consortium refers to the combination of strains NyZ450 and NyZ451 that, when grown together, significantly enhance the degradation of polyethylene mulching films compared to single strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
