      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ATR-FTIR is an analysis process used to identify chemical changes on PE surfaces, indicative of degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"ATR-FTIR is used to analyze surface chemical modifications of PE films treated with bacterial strains, identifying changes in chemical structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LB PLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LB Plates are used for culturing bacterial strains to count colonies and assess growth in experimental analyses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRON BEAM INTENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electron beam intensity is a parameter used in SEM, set at 5 kV for imaging biofilm formation on polyethylene surfaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE MULCHING FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE Mulching Film is a type of plastic film used in agriculture, which is being studied for its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain used in the biodegradation study of PE mulching films, showing growth and degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain NyZ451 is another bacterial strain involved in the study, contributing to the degradation of PE mulching films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECTROMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A spectrometer is used to measure OD600, indicating the growth of bacterial strains during the degradation study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SDS SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A SDS (sodium dodecyl sulfate) solution is used to clean polystyrene fragments, removing contaminants for accurate biodegradation assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"SDS solution is used to wash PE samples during preparation for ATR-FTIR analysis, ensuring removal of debris and contaminants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;-C=C- BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The presence of C=C bonds, revealed by ATR-FTIR, indicates chemical changes in the PE surface due to microbial oxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O-H BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"O-H bonds observed in ATR-FTIR analysis indicate surface oxidation of PE by microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-C BOND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A C-C bond is a chemical bond between two carbon atoms, involved in forming complex organic molecules and targeted in biodegradation processes like those of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbon-carbon (C-C) bond is a strong molecular bond in polyethylene that poses a significant challenge for biodegradation due to its inertness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical reaction crucial for activating the inert C-C bond in PP polymers, facilitating their breakdown into smaller molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydroxylation is a chemical reaction necessary for activating the inert C-C bonds in polyethylene, crucial for its biodegradation by bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A reaction important in the modification of PP polymers, aiding in their biodegradation by introducing carboxyl groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylation is a chemical reaction that involves the introduction of a carboxyl group and is mentioned as a method to activate the C-C bonds in PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROPHOBIC PE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrophobicity describes the property of PE that resists interaction with water, making it difficult for microorganisms to colonize and degrade it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRETREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pretreatment refers to methods like peroxidation and preheating that modify polyethylene's structure to improve its susceptibility to microbial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEROXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peroxidation is a chemical reaction that is used as a pretreatment method to make polyethylene more susceptible to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREHEATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Preheating is a process used as a method of pretreatment to alter the structure of polyethylene, enhancing its bioavailability for degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYVINYL ALCOHOL DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The degradation of polyvinyl alcohol is used as a reference for collaborative microbial interactions, similar to the cooperation observed for PE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH STIMULANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A growth stimulant is produced by one bacterium in a cooperative relationship that assists the other bacterium in the degradation process, enhancing microbial interaction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADABLE MULCHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradable Mulches are agricultural products used to cover soil, suppress weed growth, and retain moisture while being environmentally friendly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS LICHENIFORMIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus licheniformis is a bacterium capable of producing bio-surfactants that aid in the biodegradation process of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus licheniformis is a bacterium that produces biosurfactants aiding in the biodegradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYSINIBACILLUS FUSIFORMIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lysinibacillus fusiformis is a bacterium involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene by breaking down polymer chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS ATRATA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zophobas atrata, also known as superworms, are larvae capable of depolymerizing low-density polyethylene and polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIO-SURFACTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bio-surfactants are surface-active substances produced by microorganisms that help in the breakdown and solubilization of hydrophobic compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXO-BIODEGRADABLE PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxo-biodegradable plastics are designed to degrade through oxidation, eventually breaking down into water, carbon dioxide, and biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expanded Polyethylene is one of the plastic substrates tested for its impact on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Expanded polyethylene is a foam version of polyethylene used in packaging due to its cushioning properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical oxidation is a reaction where a substance loses electrons, often used in treatments to break down pollutants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYVINYL ALCOHOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyvinyl alcohol is a water-soluble synthetic polymer used in various industrial and commercial products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL STRAINS FROM WAXWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These bacterial strains are found in the guts of plastic-eating waxworms and have shown evidence of biodegrading polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKB CLONED RECOMBINANT CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AlkB cloned recombinant cell is a genetically modified cell used for the biodegradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOSURFACTANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biosurfactants are surface-active substances produced by microorganisms, contributing to bioremediation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL BACTERIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This refers to unspecified bacterial species found in the soil with the ability to biodegrade plastics like polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
      <data key="d1">"The biological breakdown of polyethylene by gut fungi in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The interaction among different bacterial strains can improve the biodegradation performance for polyethylene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which the lesser waxworm breaks down polyethylene through chewing and possible microbial activity in its digestive system."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL INTERACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interactions among microbes play a crucial role in the degradation of plastics like polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECALCITRANT PETROLEUM-BASED PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial enzymes are used for recycling recalcitrant petroleum-based plastics, facilitating their breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE AND POLYETHYLENE FOAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor degrade these foams, indicating its use in bioremediation efforts."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAE OF THE GREATER WAX MOTH (GALLERIA MELLONELLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae of Galleria mellonella, known as the greater wax moth, are macro-organisms reported to chew and potentially digest plastic, specifically polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYCAPROLACTONE (PCL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polycaprolactone is a fossil-based biodegradable polymer that needs specific conditions for degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC HYDROLYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic hydrolysis is a biochemical process where enzymes break down polymers like PLA into monomers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic hydrolysis is a dominant degradation mechanism involving enzymes breaking down materials like plastic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANDIDA TROPICALIS ATCC 20962&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Candida tropicalis ATCC 20962 is a type of fungus that has the ability to functionalize smaller, liquid alkyl chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON-CARBON BACKBONE SYNTHETIC POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These polymers, including PE, PP, PS, and PBD, are characterized by their resistance to enzymatic degradation due to the lack of functional groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERAL OXIDANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mineral oxidants are compounds used to treat polymers, enhancing their susceptibility to degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to plastic materials discarded improperly, contributing to environmental pollution and posing significant degradation challenges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL RECYCLING TECHNOLOGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical recycling technologies involve methods of breaking down complex materials into simpler chemicals that can be reused, often using biological organisms or enzymatic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are innovative methods developed to recycle plastics by breaking down and converting them into useful chemicals like ethylene glycol."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MACRO-ORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae of the greater wax moth (Galleria mellonella), studied for their ability to biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae are macro-organisms capable of chewing and potentially assisting in the biodegradation of plastics like polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae, particularly from Galleria mellonella, interact with LDPE and other substrates in the experiments to assess degradation impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae are insects known to biodegrade certain types of plastic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYBUTA-DIENE (PBD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polybuta-diene is an unsaturated polyolefin, similar to polystyrene, known for its structural stability and resistance to enzymatic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOLOGICAL MECHANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to the biological processes involving microorganisms that might contribute to the degradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECHNO-ECONOMIC ANALYSIS (TEA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TEA evaluates the costs and potential revenue of converting waste materials like mealworm remains into biodiesel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Techno-economic analysis evaluates the economic and technical aspects of recycling technologies for plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Techno-economic analysis evaluates the technical feasibility and economic viability of a technological process, including waste management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFE CYCLE ASSESSMENT (LCA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Life cycle assessment assesses the environmental impact of a process or product from its creation to disposal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle assessment is a methodology to evaluate the environmental impact associated with all stages of a product's life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE GLYCOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical compound not detected in samples, used for comparison in FTIR analysis to understand decomposition in polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene Glycol is a chemical compound that acts as an active ingredient in antifreeze formulations and has significant industrial value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene glycol is a chemical compound that polyethylene can be converted into, providing a valuable product from recycling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene glycol is a chemical potentially formed during biodegradation, its presence checked using FTIR without prior washing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene Glycol is a product of MHET metabolism in PET degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOMBELLI ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bombelli et al. refer to a group of researchers who conducted studies on the degradation of polyethylene by biological entities, although some of their results were deemed inconclusive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KUNDUNGAL ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kundungal et al. conducted studies on biodegradation, demonstrating capabilities of Achroia grisella larvae to degrade high-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a group of studies or authors who investigated the biodegradation process and chemical modifications of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEBER ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weber et al. are researchers who raised methodological issues regarding the findings of Bombelli et al. concerning the biodegradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASSONE ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cassone et al. explored changes in the intestinal microbiome of greater wax moth larvae influenced by diet on polyethylene and investigated the role of microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A product of the conversion from acetylene, used as an indicator of nitrogen-fixing activity in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is a hydrocarbon which is the simplest alkene and is used in the production of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLING FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cling film, made of LDPE, is a film used in the experiments to analyze the effect of larval and homogenate exposure on its degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR-ATR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR-ATR is a technology used to analyze chewed flakes produced by larvae interaction with substrates, aiding in the identification of material composition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMOGENATE PASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Homogenate paste is used in experiments, applied to LDPE substrates to study degradation over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homogenate paste refers to the physical mixture of homogenized larvae or mealworms used for treating plastic film substrates in degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEGWML_1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveGWML_1 is designed to study the degradation of loosely folded LDPE cling film after 17 hours of contact with Galleria mellonella larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEGWML_2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveGWML_2 investigates the degradation of loosely folded LDPE cling film over 89 hours with Galleria mellonella larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEGWML_3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveGWML_3 analyzes the degradation effect of layered LDPE cling film on Galleria mellonella larvae over a period of 96 hours."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEGWML_4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveGWML_4 examines the degradation of a black LDPE shopping bag by wax moth larvae over a span of 216 hours."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEMW_1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveMW_1 studies the interaction between mealworms and a large LDPE cling film sample over 38 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEMW_2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveMW_2 focuses on the effect of a thin LDPE grocery bag being acted on by mealworms for 38 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEMW_3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveMW_3 serves as a control with 100 mealworms kept without any substrate for 38 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT LIVEMW_4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment liveMW_4 is set up with mealworms and bran to observe any substrate interaction over 38 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT PASTEGWM_1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An experiment testing degradation of LDPE using homogenate paste under mechanical and microbial influences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experiment pasteGWM_1 investigates the effect of homogenate paste on LDPE cling film."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT PASTEGWM_PARAFFIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An experiment mixing greater wax moth larvae with liquid paraffin to analyze biological interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experiment pasteGWM_paraffin uses homogenate to interact with polystyrene powder in a high humidity environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT PASTEGWM_PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A study involving polystyrene powder mixed with homogenate paste to observe material interactions and degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experiment pasteGWM_PS involves the treatment of polystyrene powder with homogenate paste from larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT PASTEMW_PARAFFIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An experiment where mealworms were mixed with liquid paraffin to study long-term effects on substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experiment pasteMW_paraffin observes the degradation catalyzed by mealworm homogenate on polystyrene powder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT PASTEMW_PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experiment pasteMW_PS examines the effects of mealworm homogenate on polystyrene powder in a controlled setup."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial activity refers to the processes carried out by microorganisms, investigated here in the context of their interaction with LDPE substrate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLID STATE FERMENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solid state fermenter is a 150 mL jacketed vessel used to maintain constant O2 and relative humidity for experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACETONITRILE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acetonitrile is a solvent used in LC-MS applications due to its polar characteristics and miscibility with water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acetonitrile was used to wash substrate films after the experiment to prepare them for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIQUID PARAFFIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liquid paraffin is mixed with the homogenate paste in a 1:1 mass ratio for experiments with mealworms and greater wax moth larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE POWDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene powder is used in experiments to study its interaction when mixed with homogenate paste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM LIPIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm lipids are evaluated for their potential to be converted to biodiesel, considering environmental impact."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODIESEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biofuel derived from organic materials, including potentially from the lipids in larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is considered for production from mealworm lipids, analyzed for its greenhouse gas emissions offset potential."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel properties are derived from converted lipids, which serve as a renewable energy source and potential revenue stream."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GWP (GLOBAL WARMING POTENTIAL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GWP represents emissions account for greenhouse gases, and is considered in biodiesel production evaluation from mealworm lipids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MECHANICAL TEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
