    <node id="&quot;PUPA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupa indicates the developmental stage following the larval stage of Tenebrio molitor, analyzed for different feeding types in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pupa is a life stage of some insects undergoing transformation, following the larval stage and preceding the adult stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pupa is a life stage of the mealworm observed during experiments, which affects survival rates and mass measurements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pupal stage in mealworms is a transitional phase between the larva and imago, involving significant physiological transformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa is an intermediate stage in the development of mealworms before they become adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
