      <data key="d1">"A bacterial species involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene as studied in microbial research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is another bacterium present in the mealworm gut, playing a role in digesting and degrading plastic wastes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a soil bacterium known for its ability to help degrade polystyrene foam as part of waste management efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a bacterium that participates in the breakdown of polyethylene, contributing to its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a</data>
