      <data key="d2">chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL FLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial flora refers to the community of microorganisms in an environment, such as the gut of insects that decompose plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial flora refers to the diverse community of microorganisms in the gut of Plesiophthalmus davidis larvae, known for aiding in the biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOLYTE PS POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ecolyte PS Polystyrene is a type of polystyrene, a synthetic aromatic polymer made from the monomer styrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecolyte PS polystyrene is a type of polystyrene that has undergone tracer studies to understand its biooxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION OF POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation of Polystyrene is a process that involves breaking down polystyrene through biological means, such as the action of bacteria or other microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation of polystyrene refers to the breakdown of this synthetic polymer by organisms such as yellow mealworms, facilitated by their gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process involves the breakdown and decomposition of polystyrene by biological means, such as by microbes or enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which polystyrene wastes are broken down naturally, often involving biological organisms such as yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation of polystyrene refers to the breakdown of polystyrene, a common plastic, by microbial actions to reduce environmental waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"This process involves microbial breakdown, enhancing bioavailability and microbial degradation, which helps reduce its environmental footprint."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION OF LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (LDPE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process involving the breakdown and decomposition of low-density polyethylene by biological means such as Pseudomonas species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANGROVE SOIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mangrove soil refers to the soil found in mangrove forests, often characterized by high salinity and unique microbial communities capable of degrading certain plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARCH-POLYETHYLENE PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starch-polyethylene plastics are biodegradable blends that combine starch and polyethylene to enhance degradation in compost environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPOST ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A compost environment is a controlled microbial ecosystem that facilitates the decomposition of organic waste, often including biodegradable plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLY (METHYL METHACRYLATE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poly (methyl methacrylate) is a clear, strong, and lightweight plastic commonly used as a shatter-resistant alternative to glass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIAN MANGROVE SOIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indian mangrove soil refers to the soil found in mangrove ecosystems in India, notable for supporting unique microbial communities capable of degrading plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTH ATLANTIC SUBTROPICAL GYRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The North Atlantic Subtropical Gyre is a large system of rotating ocean currents where plastic waste accumulates substantially."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM (TENEBRIO MOLITOR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms are larvae known for their ability to degrade and mineralize Styrofoam efficiently through their gut system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERALIZATION OF POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mineralization of polystyrene involves converting the ingested Styrofoam carbon into CO2 during the digestion process in superworms over a 16-day period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The conversion of polystyrene into inorganic minerals through biological processes, reducing plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-EATING SUPERWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic-eating superworms refers to Zophobas atratus larvae, which are used to study the degradation of synthetic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to superworms capable of consuming polystyrene, indicating a potential application for bioremediation of plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPLASTIC DECOMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to the natural breakdown of bioplastics, here spotlighted by the ability of insect larvae like superworms as a biological solution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA BARCODE OF COI GENE (CYTOCHROME C OXIDASE SUBUNIT I)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to determine the genetic divergence between Zophobas atratus and Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLID-STATE $^{13}$C CROSS-POLARIZATION/MAGIC ANGLE SPINNING NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE (CP/MAS NMR) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sophisticated technique used to study the molecular changes of polystyrene in superworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAVIMETRIC INTERFACED WITH FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED (TG-FTIR) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An analytical method used to investigate the thermal degradation and composition of polystyrene in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut system refers to the digestive tract in superworms, potentially involved in the breakdown and mineralization of Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIAL SYMBIONT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbial symbionts are microorganisms residing in the gut of superworms, hypothesized to play a role in biodegradation of Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM-DEGRADING PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This process involves the consumption, breakdown, and mineralization of Styrofoam by superworms, potentially facilitated by their gut microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAVIMETRIC ANALYSIS - FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY (TG-FTIR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG-FTIR is a technique combining thermogravimetric analysis with infrared spectroscopy to characterize thermal degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESPIROMETRY TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Respirometry tests were conducted to evaluate the conversion efficiency of Styrofoam to CO2 by superworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAXING INSECT BREEDING PLANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Daxing Insect Breeding Plant is the supplier of superworms used throughout the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SINOPEC BEIJING YANSHAN COMPANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SINOPEC Beijing Yanshan Company is the source of the Styrofoam feedstock used for biodegradation testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"SINOPEC Beijing Yanshan Company is the supplier of Styrofoam used as feedstock in the investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The organization SINOPEC Beijing Yanshan Company provided the Styrofoam used in biodegradation tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"SINOPEC Beijing Yanshan Company provided the Styrofoam used in biodegradation tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT-AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mw is the average molecular weight of polymers based on the weight fraction, an important factor in assessing polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight-average molecular weight (\(M_w\)) is a measurement used to characterize the Styrofoam chemical properties, listed as 274,000."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight-average molecular weight is a measure of the average weight of molecules in a sample, significantly decreasing in PS MPs after digestion by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMBER-AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mn is the average molecular weight of polymers based on the number fraction, used to evaluate changes after polystyrene consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number-average molecular weight (\(M_n\)) is a measurement used to characterize the Styrofoam chemical properties, listed as 147,000."&lt;SEP&gt;"Number-average molecular weight is a measure indicating the total mass of polymer molecules divided by the number of molecules, used to characterize PS MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTOPERIOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photoperiod refers to the light/dark cycle maintained during the experiment, specifically 8:16 L:D for 28 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIMATIC CHAMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Climatic chamber is used to maintain controlled environmental conditions during the experiment with superworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(T\) TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(t\) test is a statistical test used to compare the survival rates of superworms fed with Styrofoam versus wheat bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIFAMPICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rifampicin is an antibiotic included in experimental diets to evaluate its impact on superworms' gut bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STREPTOMYCIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Streptomycin is an antibiotic administered to superworms to observe changes in gut bacteria populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELEMENTAL ANALYZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An instrument used to determine the carbon content of mealworm biomass and fecula in carbon balance experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Elemental Analyzer is a device used to determine the carbon content of Styrofoam and frass in the study of superworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPE (ESEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ESEM is used to observe the morphology of microorganisms on superworms' gut walls, offering insight into gut bacteria interactions with Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACO3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BaCO3, or barium carbonate, is formed from the reaction of CO2 with NaOH and BaCl2 during experimental analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAOH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NaOH is used as part of a solution to resuspend dried mealworm samples during the preparation of methylated derivatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"NaOH, or sodium hydroxide, is used in experiments to trap CO2 produced by superworms during Styrofoam digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"NaOH is used to stop the reaction during lipase activity measurement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium hydroxide is used to trap CO2 in biodegradation experiments, aiding in the analysis of carbon conversion rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACL2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BaCl2, or barium chloride, is used to precipitate BaCO3 from CO2 trapped in NaOH solutions during analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIAL THERMOGRAVIMETRIC (DTG) CURVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DTG curves represent the rate of weight loss as a function of temperature, used to analyze thermal decomposition of materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENYL DERIVATIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phenyl Derivatives are lower molecular weight products detected in frass, indicating degradation of Styrofoam during digestion by superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phenyl derivatives are aromatic compounds formed as smaller molecules during the depolymerization and oxidation of PS, identified in fecula."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;^13C CP/MAS NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANALYTICAL TECHNIQUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"^13C CP/MAS NMR is a solid-state Nuclear Magnetic Resonance technique used to identify chemical compositions of frass and Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TG-FTIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANALYTICAL TECHNIQUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG-FTIR (Thermogravimetric Analysis with Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy) is used to analyze the thermal decomposition and volatile compounds of samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON MONOXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon Monoxide is identified as a decomposition product of fecula, represented by strong absorbance peaks in FTIR spectra."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon monoxide is a gaseous compound released during the thermal decomposition of lower molecular weight degradation products of Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAGENOMICS SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metagenomics sequencing is a technique used to analyze the functional diversity of gut microbiota related to enzymatic activity for PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TG/DTG CURVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG/DTG curve is a thermal gravimetric analysis tool used to measure the weight loss of Styrofoam and frass during thermal decomposition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3D FTIR PROFILES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3D FTIR profiles are used to identify the evolved gaseous compounds during the thermal decomposition of Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON BALANCE BATCH EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon balance batch experiments are conducted to estimate conversion efficiencies of ingested Styrofoam into CO2 and frass residues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG ELITE SCIENTIST SPONSORSHIP PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Young Elite Scientist Sponsorship Program of the China Association of Science and Technology supports research like the study on Styrofoam degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL NATURAL SCIENCE FOUNDATION OF CHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A funding body supporting the research on PET biodegradation in Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"A funding organization supporting research, including the work on biodegradation in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization that provided financial support for the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Natural Science Foundation of China funds research, including the study of Styrofoam degradation by superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Natural Science Foundation of China is a government organization that provides funding for basic research and scientific advancement in China."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Natural Science Foundation of China is a funding body that supported the research work on Mixta tenebrionis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A funding organization that supported the research on mealworms, contributing to the study of nitrogen fixation and plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization that provides grants to support research in science and technology, including studies on biodegradable materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"This foundation provides financial support for scientific research, including studies on biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Natural Science Foundation of China is a government agency that provides funding for scientific research in China."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa27760a0a889fe7b58360dbb150cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEIJING INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY RESEARCH FUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Beijing Institute of Technology Research Fund supports young scholars in scientific research, including the study of plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE BIODEGRADING BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteria isolated from soil, capable of degrading polystyrene, showcasing their ability to process synthetic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHORIA GRISELLA F.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lesser wax moth that consumes polyethylene, highlighting its role in the biodegradation process of plastic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VULCANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical process used to harden rubber, making materials more durable and initially resistant to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS RUGIPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zophobas rugipes is a synonym for Zophobas atratus, as identified in taxonomic studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,3-DIPHENYLBUTANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,3-Diphenylbutane is a chemical compound investigated for microbial degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"1,3-diphenylbutane is an organic compound sometimes used in studies of microbial degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) is a technique used to analyze the molecular structure in extracts from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR provides insights into the chemical structure changes of Styrofoam during the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance used for the detailed characterization of PET degradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR, or Nuclear Magnetic Resonance, is an analytical technique used in the study to observe chemical modifications in plastics through the detection of hydrogen bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) spectroscopy is used to identify chemical shifts and formation of new peaks in degraded polymer samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) is a technique used to observe the local magnetic fields around atomic nuclei."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTICS (GENTAMICIN, RIFAMPICIN, STREPTOMYCIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotics are used to suppress gut bacteria in superworms to study their role in Styrofoam digestion and measure their adaptive functions."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP. PELW2042&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus sp. PELW2042 is a strain isolated from the gut contents of Tenebrio molitor larvae, known for its high ability to degrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE) film, causing changes in the film's molecular structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Identified as a member of the Bacillus genus, Bacillus sp. PELW2042 can degrade HDPE, forming biofilms on its surface and causing structural changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL GROUP (-C=O)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Carbonyl Group (-C=O) is a functional group formed during the degradation process of HDPE by Bacillus sp. PELW2042, as indicated by FT-IR spectroscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURIER TRANSFORM-INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY (FT-IR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fourier Transform-Infrared Spectroscopy (FT-IR) detects absorption peaks, indicating the formation of new functional groups during the biodegradation of HDPE by Bacillus sp. PELW2042."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS BACTERIOPHAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas bacteriophage is a bacterium genus involved in biodegradation research, capable of affecting microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas bacteriophage is a genus of PE-degrading bacteria isolated from environments like landfills, known to degrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL GROUPS (-C=O)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbonyl Groups (-C=O) are functional groups formed as a result of the biodegradation of PE by various bacteria, including Bacillus sp. PELW2042."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC CONTAMINANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organic Contaminants can be absorbed by microplastics, leading to their transfer through the food web and posing potential risks to wildlife and humans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (HDPE) FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
