      <data key="d2">chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS STRAIN YP1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus strain YP1, extracted from Waxworms, can degrade polyethylene (PE) and contributes to biodegradation by reducing PE mass over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surfactant is secreted by Strain PELW2042 and may contribute to the biodegradation of HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surfactants secreted by bacteria like Bacillus can lower the surface tension of plastics, aiding in bacterial adhesion and enhancing the degradation of PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LB MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A growth medium composed primarily of lysogeny broth, used here to culture bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"LB medium is used as a growth medium for culturing bacteria, providing necessary nutrients for strain PELW2042."&lt;SEP&gt;"LB medium is a nutrient-rich growth medium used to culture bacteria, observing specific characteristics under defined conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A growth medium prepared with bacteriological tryptone, yeast extract, NaCl, and agar used for cultivating bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"LB Medium is a nutrient-rich media used for bacterial growth, containing sodium chloride."&lt;SEP&gt;"LB Medium is a nutrient-rich media used for growing microorganisms during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"LB medium is a nutrient-rich bacterial growth medium used for culturing the isolated strains in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"LB medium is a nutrient-rich medium used for the growth of bacteria in laboratory settings, facilitating the measurement of doubling times for various strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALMODULIN (CAM) GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Calmodulin gene sequence analysis was used to identify strain PELW2042 as belonging to the Bacillus genus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEIGHBOR-JOINING METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used for constructing phylogenetic trees based on genetic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neighbor-joining method is a statistical method used to construct phylogenetic trees based on genetic sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Neighbor-Joining method is a clustering method used to create phylogenetic trees, aiding in identifying the evolutionary relationships of Bacillus sp. PELW2042."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neighbor-joining method is a clustering method used to construct phylogenetic trees, based on genetic distances among organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PP microplastics (Polypropylene microplastics) are small plastic particles that can be degraded by certain Bacillus strains, indicating their biodegradation potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN PELW2042&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific strain with a high capacity to biodegrade polyethylene, performing better than other known strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strain PELW2042 is a microorganism used to biodegrade HDPE, altering its molecular structure and weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHER GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ether groups (-C-O-C-) are functional groups that appear in HDPE during its biodegradation by microbial action."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYLATING ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxylating enzymes such as AlkB and P450 initiate the hydroxylation at the PE terminal, aiding its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY ALCOHOL DEHYDROGENASE (ADH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adh facilitates the conversion of primary alcohols into ketones during the biodegradation process of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XRD (X-RAY DIFFRACTION)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"XRD is used to characterize material properties and analyze the crystallinity of HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P450 is another type of hydroxylating enzyme that participates in the breakdown of polyethylene, facilitating biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMORPHOUS REGIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amorphous regions in polymers like HDPE are more easily attacked by microorganisms, playing a role in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-DEGRADING MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
