      <data key="d1">"Rawal Lake in Pakistan has shown the first evidence of environmental exposure to microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARINE FOOD WEB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The marine food web consists of interconnected food chains in marine environments, affected by microplastic and contaminant trophic transfer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEXTILE FIBERS INCLUDING MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Textile fibers, often contributing to microplastic pollution, are found in indoor and outdoor environments, impacting environmental health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTAMINANT TRANSPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contaminant transport refers to the movement of pollutants like microplastics through environments, impacting ecosystems and health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD SAFETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food safety involves reducing risks from contaminants like microplastics in food sources, crucial for protecting public health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOURCE-PATHWAY-RECEPTOR MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This model explains the movement of pollutants like microplastics from a source, through a pathway, to a receptor, like organisms or ecosystems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC FALLOUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atmospheric fallout is the settling of particles from the atmosphere, which can include microplastics, impacting land and water environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGING, MIGRATION, AND CO-TRANSPORT OF CONTAMINANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These processes describe how microplastics age, migrate, and transport contaminants through different environments, affecting their properties and impacts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE FILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These are types of plastics that can degrade in the environment, sometimes enhanced by specific biodegradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREATER WAXMOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greater waxmoth is a species associated with the enhanced biodegradation and mineralization of low-density polyethylene films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STENOTROPHOMONAS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stenotrophomonas sp. is a bacterial genus that biodegrades unpretreated low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stenotrophomonas sp. refers to species within the genus Stenotrophomonas, which are Gram-negative bacteria known for their diverse metabolic capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
