      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique employed to analyze the isotopic composition of carbon, particularly in the context of 13C-labeled experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID EXTRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process of extracting lipids from mealworm bodies after degradation experiments with Styrofoam to study metabolite profiles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FECULA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecula is a significant byproduct of the mealworm digestion process of EPS, analyzed for changes in molecular weight compared to the original feedstock."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a substance whose chemical components and native compositions evolve during thermal decomposition, as indicated by FTIR spectra and NMR analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is the material excreted by mealworms after digesting Styrofoam, used to study chemical changes in ingested materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is the residue of Styrofoam egested through the gut of mealworms, analyzed for changes in chemical composition and structure post digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is the waste material excreted by mealworms, containing residual Styrofoam fragments and gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the waste material produced by mealworms after ingesting Styrofoam, collected for further analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is the waste product from mealworms post-consumption of polystyrene, containing biodegradation byproducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the residual matter derived from mealworms processing Styrofoam, which is analyzed for changes in molecular weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13CO2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"13CO2 is the carbon dioxide generated with a carbon-13 isotopic label, used to trace carbon conversion in experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUBBER STOPPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rubber stoppers are used to seal incubators in mealworm experiments to prevent contamination and maintain controlled conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLOROFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organic compound used as a solvent in laboratory settings including phase separation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform is used as a solvent for lipid extraction from mealworm bodies after experimental feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chloroform is used as a solvent to extract lipids from mealworm bodies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
    </node>
