      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEOH/NAOH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MeOH/NaOH is a mixture used to resuspend and react dried mealworm samples in the analysis process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYL ETHER-BORON TRIFLUORIDE (MEBT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEBT is a reagent mixture used in the methylation of fatty acids for their analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-HEXANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n-Hexane is used to extract methylated derivatives of fatty acids after the methylation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOXHLET EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Soxhlet Extractor is a piece of laboratory apparatus used to extract crude fat from mealworm larvae using petroleum ether."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Soxhlet extractor is a device used to achieve the continuous extraction of lipids from mealworms using chloroform."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD) is a polydispersity measure indicating the range of molecular sizes in a polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution refers to the variation of molecular weights within a sample, analyzed to study changes in polystyrene after decomposition by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RETENTION TIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Retention time refers to the duration plastic particles remain within an organism's digestive system during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Retention time refers to the duration that Styrofoam remains in the gut of mealworms before egestion, indicating its processing speed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEETLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beetles are the adult form of mealworms, which emerge after the larvae stage following Styrofoam consumption and metamorphosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles refer to the final stage of development for Tenebrio molitor after pupation in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles consume much less EPS compared to mealworms but may assist mealworm consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are the adult form of the mealworms and play a role in the reproduction process after pupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are the adult stage of mealworms and result from pupae transformation, completing the mealworm life cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process conducted to analyze thermal properties of PP foam and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal analysis is a method used to study the changes in material properties as they are heated, involving thermogravimetric analysis and differential scanning calorimetry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal analysis is used to examine the decomposition process of fecula, highlighting differences between evolved gaseous compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TG SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG Spectroscopy, or Thermogravimetric spectroscopy, is used alongside FTIR to study weight loss patterns and evolved gases during heating."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON DIOXIDE (CO₂)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon Dioxide is a decomposition product detected in FTIR spectra and recovered in significant amounts during the conversion of PS (polystyrene) by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR SPECTRA AT 233, 327, AND 431 \({ }^{\CIRC} \MATHRM{C}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR Spectra at these specific temperatures reveal strong absorbance peaks indicating decomposition products like carbon monoxide and carbon dioxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECOMPOSITION PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Decomposition products such as carbon monoxide and carbon dioxide result from thermal decomposition of fecula and are observed in the FTIR spectra."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INITIAL CARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial Carbon refers to the starting amount of carbon present in materials like Styrofoam before the experimental incubation period begins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINAL CARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Final Carbon indicates the remaining amount of carbon in materials like Styrofoam after the incubation period, used to determine carbon conversion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCUBATION TIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Incubation Time refers to the duration over which mealworms are allowed to consume PS, affecting the amount of CO₂ and biomass produced."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON BALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon Balance is calculated to estimate the carbon recovery from PS into CO₂, biomass, and fecula residues over the incubation period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAS (FATTY ACIDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acids serve as biomarkers for determining carbon assimilation in mealworms, showing higher δ13C values when fed PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON ISOTOPIC TECHNIQUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The technique uses carbon isotopes in fatty acids to measure carbon assimilation in mealworms fed with labeled PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNLABELED BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unlabeled bran is used as a control diet in the experiment, providing a baseline comparison for mealworm growth alongside PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO2 (CARBON DIOXIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO2 is a byproduct of PS mineralization in mealworms, providing an energy source for their biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2, or carbon dioxide, is a gas released during respiration, decomposition, and the breakdown of some microplastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"CO2 is a product resulting from the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene by larvae, indicating breakdown into simpler components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOREACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larval gut is described as a bioreactor, facilitating microbial and enzymatic degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut functions as a bioreactor, facilitating the physical and biochemical treatment required for PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Essential nutrients such as calcium, potassium, nitrogen, and phosphorus are needed for growth and development of lesser waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrients including calcium, potassium, nitrogen, and phosphorus are essential for the growth and development of organisms, facilitating processes like enzyme synthesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins, phosphorus, vitamins, and minerals are essential nutrients missing in Styrofoam that affect mealworm growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrients are components that provide nourishment essential for growth and the maintenance of life, discussed in the context of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERALIZATION OF INGESTED STYROFOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This refers to the conversion of ingested Styrofoam to CO2 within the mealworm gut, contributing to energy production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes secreted by organisms to break down external materials, such as polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular Enzymes are proteins secreted by gut microbes in mealworms that assist in the catalysis of depolymerization of Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are enzymes secreted by microorganisms in the mealworm gut that facilitate the breakdown of polyurethane bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular Enzymes are enzymes secreted by bacteria and evaluated for their activity in breaking down substrates, contributing to plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular enzymes are crucial for biodegradation processes, particularly in the degradation of polyurethane plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTIONAL MICROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Functional Microbes refer to the specific types of microorganisms in the mealworm gut responsible for catalyzing the degradation of Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13C STABLE CARBON ISOTOPE TRACER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 13C Stable Carbon Isotope Tracer is used in experiments to track the carbon flow and fate during the degradation process in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TGA-FTIR THERMOGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TGA-FTIR Thermograms are used to analyze the thermal and chemical changes of the Styrofoam material during the degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATCH STYROFOAM-FEEDING TRIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Batch Styrofoam-feeding Trials are experimental setups used to study the degradation activity and outcomes in mealworms feeding on Styrofoam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMETHYL METHACRYLATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymethyl methacrylate is a transparent thermoplastic often used as a lightweight or shatter-resistant alternative to glass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOLYTE PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ecolyte PS is a type of polystyrene designed to be more susceptible to biooxidation and microbial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOOXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biooxidation is a chemical process involving the oxidation of organic compounds by living organisms, often used in biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biooxidation is the process by which organisms use oxygen to break down organic compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON ASSIMILATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon assimilation is the process by which organisms convert inorganic carbon (CO2) into organic matter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLOMBOLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collombola, also known as springtails, are soil-dwelling microarthropods that play a role in the decomposition process in soil ecosystems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPHESIA CAUTELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ephesia cautella is a species of moth larva known for its ability to penetrate packaging films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ephesia cautella is a species of moth whose larvae are known to penetrate packaging films, causing damage to stored products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC-TOF-MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC-TOF-MS (Gas Chromatography-Time of Flight Mass Spectrometry) is a technique used for metabolic profiling in research on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"GC-TOF-MS, or Gas Chromatography-Time of Flight Mass Spectrometry, is an analytical technique utilized in metabolic profiling to study biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gas Chromatography Time-of-Flight Mass Spectrometry is a technique used to analyze volatile compounds in frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gas Chromatography-Time of Flight Mass Spectrometry (GC-TOF-MS) is a technology used to analyze the metabolic profiling of larvae gut intestine tissue and frass in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2,4 DI-TERT BUTYLPHENOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2,4 di-tert butylphenol is a compound identified in both frass and tissue, coming from the PS polymer, indicating the presence of non-intentionally added substances (NIAS)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AARHUS UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aarhus University is an institution where multiple departments are involved in the research of biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aarhus University is the location where Tenebrio molitor larvae were reared for the purpose of the biodegradation experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIFOOD, CENTRE FOR INNOVATIVE FOOD RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CIFOOD is part of Aarhus University and plays a key role in research and innovation in food science, involved in this biodegradation study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CBIO, CENTRE FOR CIRCULAR BIOECONOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CBIO is an Aarhus University center focused on circular bioeconomy, participating in research efforts related to sustainability, such as this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIO-RECYCLING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bio-recycling involves the use of biological processes, often involving microorganisms, to decompose and recycle waste materials naturally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bio-recycling refers to the process of using biological means to recycle materials like polystyrene, which is the focus of increasing research interest."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVA GUT INTESTINE TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut intestine tissue of the mealworm larvae, which is analyzed to understand the metabolic processes involved in polystyrene biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC RESIDUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organic residues generated from polymer degradation, analyzed to detect changes in chemical structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC PACKAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic packaging made from polystyrene, discussed in the context of its environmental impact and biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL LIFE SCIENCES INSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The International Life Sciences Institute is referenced in relation to the importance and recycling of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIMERS, TRIMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These are forms of PS oligomers identified in the metabolic analysis, indicating partial breakdown of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-INTENTIONALLY ADDED SUBSTANCES (NIAS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These are chemicals like 2,4 di-tert butylphenol that unintentionally form during polymer processing or degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC-BASED METABOLOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANALYTICAL METHOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gas chromatography-based metabolomics is a technique used to analyze small molecules in biological samples, applied here to study the metabolic changes in larval frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGMA ALDRICH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sigma Aldrich is a company that supplies various chemicals such as methoxime hydrochloride, chloroform, and others used in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUJIFILM WAKO CHEMICALS EUROPE GMBH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
