    <node id="&quot;OLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fatty acid identified in the frass or intestinal samples of PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a fatty acid that accounted for about 50% of the fatty acid content in the PE and CEL groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a monounsaturated omega-9 fatty acid observed to increase in the frass of PS-fed mealworms due to lipid metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is one of the long-chain fatty acids identified as a product of the PS biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e</data>
