      <data key="d2">chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The wax moth, particularly its larvae, is known to harbor bacteria capable of degrading polyethylene, playing a role in biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax Moth larvae are utilized as a model organism and exhibit elevated Vitamin B6 metabolism when exposed to specific plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths, particularly in their larval stage, have been researched for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene plastic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT FAT BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The insect fat body is an organ responsible for energy storage and metabolism regulation, impacted by the dietary inclusion of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACID AMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acid amides are signaling molecules involved in various physiological processes, potentially disrupted by plastic consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic biodegradation refers to the breakdown of materials like plastics through enzyme action, as studied in environmental microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic biodegradation refers to the process of breaking down complex substrates into simpler molecules using enzymatic activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic biodegradation uses enzymes to accelerate the breakdown of polymers such as polystyrene, providing a more efficient degradation pathway."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
