    <node id="&quot;LIFE CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
      <data key="d1">"A life cycle is the series of stages through which a living organism passes from the beginning of its life until its death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Figure 6 depicts the completion of Tenebrio molitor's life cycle with the transition from pupae to beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the stages of development and growth, such as in polystyrene-fed larvae attempting to complete their natural life processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life Cycle refers to the complete series of stages in the life of superworms and yellow mealworms, including egg, larva, pupa, and adult stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the stages of development of Tenebrio molitor from larvae through to adult beetle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the complete series of stages (development, growth, maturation, reproduction) that organisms undergo from birth to the natural end of its life, as described by the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
