    <node id="&quot;RAPD PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd</data>
      <data key="d1">"RAPD PCR is used to explore genetic relationships and differences among bacterial isolates."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYLOGENETIC TREE CONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEGAX is utilized for constructing phylogenetic trees using specified algorithms."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEASURING EVOLUTIONARY DISTANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 16S rRNA sequences are used to compute evolutionary distances using the Maximum Composite Likelihood method."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDY RECOGNITION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Research Board is acknowledged for supporting the research study conducted at the University."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDY ASSAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
      <data key="d1">"OM was responsible for performing all assays in the study, resulting in data collection and interpretation."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT BACTERIA OF T. MOLITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut bacteria isolated from T. molitor are evaluated for their ability to grow on PS as the sole carbon source and are characterized biochemically and molecularly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut bacteria of Tenebrio molitor are capable of degrading polystyrene and have been shown to form biofilms on PS sheets, exploiting it as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biofilms are communities of microorganisms that attach to surfaces and contribute to the biodegradation of substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilms are structured communities of microorganisms that adhere to surfaces, facilitating processes like degradation of various substances, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilms are structures formed by microbial colonies, such as Exiguobacterium sp., that contribute to plastic degradation by facilitating microbial activity on the surface of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilms are structures formed by microorganisms, including the gut bacteria of T. molitor, on polystyrene surfaces, contributing to its physical degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilms refer to the structured community of microbial cells that adhere to surfaces, such as PS films, through extracellular polymeric substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collections of microorganisms that can form on various surfaces and influence the interaction of microplastics with antibiotics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL ADAPTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental adaptation refers to the procedure of acclimating T. molitor larvae to the environmental conditions for studies on polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOMBIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colombia is the geographical area from where the mealworm larvae were collected and studied for polystrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOGOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bogota is the city where the experiments with T. molitor larvae are conducted, located at an altitude of 2630 m.a.s.l."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINIMAL SALT MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Minimal salt medium provides the basic nutrients needed for the growth of T. molitor gut bacteria, excluding carbon sources like PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACCLIMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acclimation refers to the process by which T. molitor larvae adjust to the laboratory's environmental conditions in Bogota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT T. MOLITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adult T. molitor are used to evaluate their capacity to ingest PS, similar to the experiments conducted on larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NILO, CUNDINAMARCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nilo is a locality in the department of Cundinamarca, Colombia, where T. molitor larvae were initially collected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACCLIMATION CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acclimation conditions include the environmental factors like temperature and light that the mealworms were exposed to, ensuring their adaptation in Bogota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTOPHOBIC BEHAVIOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photophobic behavior is the mealworms' tendency to avoid light, influencing the conditions their experiments were conducted under."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANALYTICAL BALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An analytical balance is used to accurately measure the changes in mass of control and treatment larvae, as well as the PS plates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILE CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterile conditions refer to a contamination-free environment maintained for the excision and identification of gut bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGAR MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agar medium is used as a cultivation platform for bacteria in the experiments, facilitating growth assessment under aerobic and anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STENOTROPHOMONAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stenotrophomonas is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of T. molitor larvae, characterized by its facultative, fermenting nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stenotrophomonas is a genus of bacteria with differing relative abundances observed under varying mealworm diet conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL., (2018)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yang et al., (2018) conducted a study observing T. molitor larvae feeding on PS with an 85% survival rate after 32 days of incubation, indicating their capability to consume PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL., (2015B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yang et al., (2015b) identified bacteria in the digestive tract of T. molitor, contributing to the understanding of microbial impact on PS consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAW STRUCTURE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jaw structure changes in T. molitor from larvae to adult may prevent adults from consuming and ingesting polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL MICROBIOTA COMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in intestinal microbiota composition, particularly through T. molitor's life stages, can influence dietary capabilities and PS processing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHEAT FLOUR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wheat flour is used as a comparative diet to PS for feeding T. molitor larvae, providing necessary carbohydrates and proteins for growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREASE TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The urease test is used to determine the presence of urease enzyme activity in bacterial isolates from T. molitor guts, which returned negative results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATALÁN ET AL., 2011&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catalán et al., 2011 provided information on nutritional requirements for larval growth, suggesting PS lacks necessary organic nutrients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS ANTHRACIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus anthracis is a bacterium that can form tunnels, cracks, and cellular aggregates on polystyrene (PS) sheets, contributing to bacterial-driven transformations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus anthracis is a species of bacteria within the genus Bacillus and is known as the causative agent of anthrax. It is a Gram-positive bacterium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA PERSICINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwinia persicina is a species of bacteria within the genus Erwinia, likely involved in plant association, characterized by its rod shape."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia persicina is a species of bacterium included in the LMG 11254 group, associated with HQ accession numbers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exiguobacterium is a genus of bacteria distinguished by its ability to degrade a range of substances, including polyethylene terephthalate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL CHARACTERISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical Characteristics refer to the chemical processes and compounds that define the metabolic and physiological functions of organisms, crucial for identifying bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORPHOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morphological Characteristics describe the form, structure, and configuration of cells, important for distinguishing bacterial species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATALASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catalase is an enzyme present in Mixta tenebrionis, responsible for degrading hydrogen peroxide to water and oxygen, indicating the bacterium's ability to detoxify reactive oxygen species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that catalyzes the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen, commonly found in aerobic bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that catalyzes the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide to water and oxygen, showing activity in several isolates including M7 and M8."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrate, commonly present in the citric acid cycle, serves as an indicator of certain bacterial metabolic activities, such as the ability to utilize citrate as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VP TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Voges-Proskauer (VP) Test identifies bacterial species that produce acetoin during glucose metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLARY MORPHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillary morphology describes the rod-shaped appearance of certain bacterial cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAS PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gas production in bacteria is a result of metabolic processes, often indicated by changes in culture media during biochemical tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isolates refer to the specific bacterial strains that are separated from other microorganisms for detailed study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus sp is a bacterium involved in the transformation of PS sheets through physical changes such as forming tunnels and cracks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STENOTROPHOMONAS SP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stenotrophomonas sp is a bacterium that participates in causing changes on PS sheets, such as forming tunnels and cracks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILM GENERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biofilm generation is the initial step in the transformation of materials like PS by microorganisms, facilitating material deterioration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE CONVERSION TO PHENYLACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The conversion of styrene to phenylacetate via the citric acid cycle is a chemical reaction common among different microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T. MOLITOR ADULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T. molitor adults have bacteria like Bacillus in their digestive tract, but structural changes in jaws may prevent the ingestion of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNIBALISTIC BEHAVIORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannibalistic behaviors in T. molitor larvae occur when they are fed exclusively on PS, indicating nutritional deficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS SHEETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS sheets refer to polystyrene sheets that undergo transformation and degradation by microorganisms such as Bacillus anthracis, Bacillus sp, and Stenotrophomonas sp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLA/PBAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PLA/PBAT refers to a blend of polylactic acid (PLA) and polybutylene adipate terephthalate (PBAT) used in creating flexible films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS SP. STRAIN Y2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas sp. Strain Y2 is a bacterial strain notable for its genetic and functional traits enabling it to catabolize styrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. strain Y2 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading styrene through its styrene catabolic cluster."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECABROMODIPHENYL OXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A brominated flame retardant often added to plastics, which poses challenges for biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Decabromodiphenyl oxide is a flame retardant commonly used in electronics and plastics that poses environmental and health concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Decabromodiphenyl oxide is a brominated flame retardant used in combination with other chemicals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56425bd62513be46b9165bfd84f0dd0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIONID BEETLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrionid beetles, part of the family Tenebrionidae, are diverse species noted for varied environmental adaptations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL APPROACH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial approach refers to the use of microorganisms to degrade or transform substances, often used in bioremediation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COCKROACH GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cockroach gut bacteria are microorganisms residing in a cockroach's digestive system contributing to digestion and other functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E-PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E-plastic is a term commonly referring to electronic plastics, often containing hazardous additives like flame retardants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIA OF THE DIGESTIVE TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The bacteria isolated from the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor are capable of degrading polystyrene, forming biofilms on PS surfaces, and causing observable physical changes in the material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTÉRIAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bactérias isolated from the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor, capable of forming biofilms on polystyrene surfaces, indicating potential use of polystyrene as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLIESTIRENO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poliestireno, or polystyrene, is the material on which bacteria from Tenebrio molitor's digestive tract can form biofilms, causing surface changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPELÍCULAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopelículas, or biofilms, are formed by bacteria on the polystyrene surfaces, leading to changes such as grooves and holes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPIA ELETRÔNICA DE VARREDURA (SEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microscopia Eletrônica de Varredura, or Scanning Electron Microscopy, is the technique used to observe changes on polystyrene surfaces caused by bacterial biofilms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAULA M. PEÑA-PASCAGAZA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental engineer with expertise in bioprocesses, microbiology, and environmental monitoring, involved in environmental research and guideline development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATHALIA A. LÓPEZ-RAMÍREZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental engineer specializing in Health, Safety, and Environment (HSE), experienced in waste management and continuous improvement process for multinational companies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIGUEL A. BALLEN-SEGURA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Professor and researcher with a focus on fundamental and applied ecology, working on projects involving microorganisms as remediation tools."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of beetles, specifically studied for differences in species-specificity affecting gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus of beetles, in this context referring to species whose larvae were used to study gut microbiome shifts when fed different polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is the genus of beetles from which the species Tenebrio molitor is derived, relevant to the study of bacteria in the digestive tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus of beetles within the family Tenebrionidae, commonly known as darkling beetles, which includes species such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio is a genus of beetles, including T. obscurus and T. molitor, noted for their roles in biodegrading plastics like PS due to gut microbiome activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRATO DIGESTIVO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trato Digestivo, or digestive tract, is the system from which bacteria are isolated in Tenebrio molitor and potentially used for biofilm formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAMINAS DE PS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laminas de PS refers to polystyrene sheets on which biofilm formation by isolated bacteria is observed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RANHURAS E BURACOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ranhuras e Buracos are grooves and holes observed on polystyrene surfaces as a result of biofilm activity by bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING&quot;">
