    <node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION AND DEMOLITION WASTE (CWD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Construction and Demolition Waste refers to debris generated during construction and demolition activities, comprising materials such as bricks, mortar, and insulation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3f0582a5d7e55961a1ce4d971d3e4a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE FRAMEWORK DIRECTIVE 2008/98/EC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLICY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Waste Framework Directive 2008/98/EC is a European directive that regulates the management and recycling of waste, including construction and demolition debris."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3f0582a5d7e55961a1ce4d971d3e4a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZERO WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHILOSOPHICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zero Waste is a concept based on the circular economy that aims to minimize waste production and maximize resource recovery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3f0582a5d7e55961a1ce4d971d3e4a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMBIOTIC MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microorganisms residing in mealworms' guts that aid in the digestion of hard-to-degrade plastics and contribute to their ability to consume synthetic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Symbiotic microbiota in the gut of Tenebrio molitor assists in the digestion of plastics, playing an essential role in breaking down hard-to-degrade materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
