      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREY EPS WITH GRAPHITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grey EPS with graphite is a specialized construction material with higher thermal properties than ordinary white EPS, used in building energy-efficient structures. It has an apparent density of 19.66 kg/m³."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOUR LIFE STAGES OF TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrio molitor goes through four life stages: egg, larva, pupa, and adult, with distinct physical characteristics during each stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIET OF MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms can consume various materials, including durable plastics like polyethylene and polystyrene, due to their strong mandibles and supportive gut microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WARD'S METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ward's method is a statistical technique used in cluster analysis for constructing a dendrogram as part of agglomerative hierarchical clustering in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ward's method is a type of hierarchical clustering used to create a dendrogram, identifying clusters in data as part of statistical analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEETLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beetles are adult forms of mealworms and are used in experiments to understand EPS consumption and life stage effects on feeding habits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are part of the co-culture experimental setup, studied for EPS consumption alongside mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles belong to the class Insecta and are holometabolic insects, which undergo complete metamorphosis including distinct life stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles, specifically adult Tenebrio molitor, primarily consume the hard outer layer of EPS but contribute little to overall EPS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLOMETABOLIC INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Holometabolic insects undergo complete metamorphosis with four distinct life stages: egg, larva, pupa, and adult."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCESSED CELLULOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
