      <data key="d2">chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White EPS is a variant of Expanded Polystyrene characterized by a pH of 7.95 when processed, producing a different frass texture and larvae mortality effect compared to grey EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"White EPS is a variant of expanded polystyrene with larger material density and contains higher volumes of carbon (C) and nitrogen (N)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREY EPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grey EPS is a variant of expanded polystyrene containing graphite, thought to have a composition beneficial for larvae life processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grey EPS is another variant of Expanded Polystyrene characterized by a pH of 7.74 and a higher phosphorus content in the resulting frass, having a distinct chemical and physical interaction with Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEMENT MORTAR&quot;">
