      <data key="d2">chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOME DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiome diversity refers to the variety of microbial species found in a given environment, such as the gut of Tenebrio molitor during plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome diversity refers to the variety of microbial species in organisms like Tenebrio molitor, which aids in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome diversity refers to the variety of microbial species present in Tenebrio molitor, especially when fed with different diets such as polystyrene waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROCARBON-BASED PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrocarbon-based plastics are synthetic polymers derived from petrochemicals, which are resistant to environmental degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics composed of hydrocarbons, studied for consumption and biodegradation by insect larvae, including Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMETRIC EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process of assessing biological conditions, such as those of wheat seedlings fertilized by mealworm larvae meal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGNOCELLULOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complex of lignin, cellulose, and hemicellulose found in plant cell walls, practically devoid of nitrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose degradation mechanisms are studied across the Tree of Life for their biochemical processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose is a natural polymer, part of the diet tested for mealworm larvae, and is considered less beneficial for their development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose is a complex biomass consisting of cellulose, hemicellulose, and lignin, present in plants and the focus of degradation studies in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose is a complex natural polymer consisting of cellulose, hemicellulose, and lignin, forming the structural component of plants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose is a complex plant material found in cell walls, requiring pre-treatment for conversion into high-value chemicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose is a natural polymer resistant to degradation, similar in structure to some synthetic plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A complex of lignin, cellulose, and hemicellulose, typically found in plant materials and part of the natural diet of gut microbes in T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lignocellulose is a structural component of plants, composed of lignin, cellulose, and hemicellulose, often decomposed by bacteria and fungi."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
