    <node id="&quot;IMAGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imago is the adult stage of T. molitor beetles that emerge from pupae, and whose characteristics were measured in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imago refers to the final stage of T. molitor life cycle, characterized as an adult beetle, with productivity affected by nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imago represents the adult stage of Tenebrio molitor, with varying proportions observed based on diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Imago is the final stage of insect development where the insect reaches maturity and is capable of reproduction."</data>
