    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEL DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CEL diet is a specific nutritional regimen that shows unique associations with physiological and structural changes in microbiome related to insect development."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEL diet refers to the cardboard-based diet, which showed high numbers of adults after 45 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CEL diet includes cardboard as a substrate and resulted in lower development rates in the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CEL diet involves a specific dietary intervention that includes cellulose, aimed at studying its effects on microbiome structure and health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-OXO DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-oxo diet refers to the oxo-degradable polyethylene-based diet, associated with low metamorphosis rates and high mortality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PE-oxo diet consists of oxo-degradable polyethylene, correlated with adverse growth impacts on larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PE-oxo diet involves a specific dietary variant examined for its influence on microbiome abundance and metabolic measures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-REG DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-reg diet refers to the polyethylene regranulate-based diet, showing similar development patterns to OAT and high adult numbers despite high mortality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PE-reg diet is a regular dietary variation observed for its impact on microbiome composition and metabolic traits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PE-reg diet uses polyethylene regranulate, demonstrating favorable development conditions despite high cannibalism rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A polystyrene-based diet studied for its effects on protein levels and microbiota composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS diet refers to the polystyrene-based diet, characterized by high protein content in larvae and high mortality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PS diet consists of polystyrene, showing unique metabolic and microbiological impacts on Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PS diet is a specific dietary regimen used in research to analyze its effects on microbiome composition and metabolic responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PS diet consists of polystyrene, a persistent plastic consumed by Tenebrio obscurus, linked to changes in gut microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS diet refers to a diet composed of polystyrene materials, affecting T. molitor larvae by providing insufficient food supply and potential toxic effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAMORPHOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metamorphosis is the developmental transition in larvae influenced by diet, particularly the natural life cycle in oatmeal diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metamorphosis is the transformation process that insects undergo from larvae to adults, varying across different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process by which lesser waxworms develop from larval stages to pupae and eventually moths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINOLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Linoleic acid content was higher in larvae fed with diets other than OAT, showing significant dietary impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linoleic acid is associated with consumption in the PS diet and correlated with specific bacterial presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linoleic acid is a polyunsaturated omega-6 fatty acid reported to be in varying percentages according to different authors, ranked third after palmitic acid in certain studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALMITIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palmitic acid is a saturated long-chain fatty acid used in soap and detergent industries, and identified as a chemical involved in the biodegradation context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palmitic acid showed a higher percentage in the OAT diet group compared to other diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palmitic acid, also known as hexadecanoic acid (C16:0), is a saturated fatty acid with percentage content varying from 12.1% to 19.4% depending on the feed type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STREPTACIDIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Streptacidin refers to a genus of bacteria involved in the microbiome analyzed within the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGNOCELLULOSE GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Lignocellulose group is characterized by low consumption and activity leading to rapid metamorphosis possibly as a survival strategy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMETRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biometry refers to the statistical analysis of biological data, like the size and development measures among insect diet groups analyzed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE COUNTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
