      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L-ARABINOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sugar involved in unique uptake patterns shared between the PE and PS groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"L-arabinose is a nutrient connected to specific dietary patterns in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"L-arabinose is a sugar involved in the pentose phosphate pathway, utilized variably by larvae under different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"L-arabinose is a sugar utilized by Mixta tenebrionis to produce acids, reflecting its ability to metabolize this pentose sugar."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRYPTOPHAN DEAMINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tryptophan deaminase is an enzyme related to amino acid metabolism, with varying activity levels depending on the diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urease is an enzyme involved in urea metabolism, with activity levels varying among different dietary treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that helps in the hydrolysis of urea into ammonia and carbon dioxide, tested in bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
