      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sugar alcohol absorbed by the PE-oxo group, indicative of metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-Sorbitol is consumed in PE diets, highlighting metabolic diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"D-sorbitol is a sugar alcohol utilized differently by larvae according to their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"d-Sorbitol is a sugar alcohol tested to check if a bacterium can ferment it into acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACETOIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A compound produced by various microorganisms, noted for its role in metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acetoin is a metabolic compound, with CEL diet showing high production potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADIPIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adipic acid is a dicarboxylic acid utilized differently depending on the diet, with CEL being a notable outlier."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adipic acid is found in mealworm larvae with correlations to certain diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organic acid used in the study to observe metabolic changes in the microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
