    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fundamental process involving energy production, linked with inositol metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central metabolism refers to the metabolic pathways within a cell that provide precursor metabolites, reducing power, and metabolic energy essential for cell function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SELENOMONADALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An increase in this order was unique to the CEL-fed group, indicating dietary-specific microbial changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Selenomonadales is an order of bacteria known for their role in the anaerobic fermentation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RHODOBACTERALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order of bacteria found in different abundance across diet variants, significant in the PE-oxo and OAT groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodobacterales is an order of proteobacteria involved in carbon and sulfur cycles, often found in marine environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodobacterales is linked negatively with PS diet, impacting the microbial environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROSIRIPLAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrosiriplas is an order of bacteria involved in the oxidation of ammonia as part of the nitrogen cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANCTOMYCETALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An order part of the unique bacterial composition in PS diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planctomycetales correlated positively with the PS diet, influencing microbiological dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planctomycetales is an order known for their distinctive cell plan and their role in nitrogen cycling, particularly anaerobic ammonium oxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORIOBACTERIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coriobacteriales is an order of gram-positive bacteria present in the human gut, contributing to metabolic activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURKHOLDERIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burkholderiales is an order of proteobacteria that includes a variety of species, some of which are known pathogens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONADALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonadales is an order of bacteria known for diverse metabolic capabilities, often forming symbiotic relationships with insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadales is an order of diverse bacteria that includes many species found in soil and water, some of which are pathogenic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMOA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The amoA gene encodes for ammonia monooxygenase enzyme, critical for the conversion of ammonia to nitrite during nitrogen metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"The amoA gene is responsible for nitrogen metabolism, and its high load was observed in correlation with PS diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC ENERGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic energy refers to the energy derived from metabolic processes, which is used by cells to power various biological functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REDUCING POWER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reducing power is the ability of a molecule to donate electrons during biochemical reactions, which is crucial for energy generation and biosynthetic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECURSOR METABOLITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precursor metabolites are intermediate molecules in metabolic pathways that serve as substrates for the biosynthesis of macromolecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT DIGESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut digestion is the process by which food is broken down in the digestive tract, involving microbiome participation and metabolic activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVELOPMENT STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Development stages refer to the different phases of life cycle progression in organisms such as insects, evaluated during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"The growth cycle of lesser waxworms, including stages from larvae to adult moths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen metabolism encompasses the processes by which nitrogen is converted into various chemical forms as it circulates among atmospheric, terrestrial, and marine ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen metabolism encompasses the processes through which organisms assimilate, absorb, and utilize nitrogen for growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen metabolism encompasses the set of biochemical processes that manage the fate of nitrogen within biological systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen metabolism refers to the processes within organisms that convert nitrogen compounds, crucial for growing organisms, as influenced by genes like amoA, nifH, and nirS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen metabolism refers to biological pathways that involve the transformation and synthesis of nitrogen-containing compounds, including essential nutrients like amino acids and vitamins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen metabolism involves the larvae's utilization of nitrogen for cellular functions, influenced by PE ingestion and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen metabolism involves the processes organisms use to convert nitrogen into forms necessary for life, such as amino acids and nucleotides."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL TRAITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical traits represent specific chemical properties or activities expressed by microbial communities, such as those seen in larval microbiomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREC GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ureC gene, correlated with lignocellulose diet, is involved in urea metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIFH GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene encoding nitrogenase enzyme components, key to the nitrogen fixation process, identified in mealworms' gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gene used to further ascertain the nitrogen-fixing ability of bacterial isolates from Styrofoam-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene encodes a component of the nitrogenase enzyme complex necessary for nitrogen fixation, used to identify nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene encodes dinitrogen reductase, a key enzyme involved in the biological nitrogen fixation process, and is detected through molecular techniques."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is associated with nitrogen fixation and is used as a marker for assessing diazotrophic communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is associated with nitrogen fixation, encoding dinitrogenase reductase, a key enzyme in the nitrogen fixation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is involved in the fixation of nitrogen in soil and microorganisms, affecting nitrogen metabolism in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene, negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet, is involved in nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIRS GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nirS gene is involved in nitrogen metabolism and was negatively correlated with certain diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-LINOLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"α-Linoleic acid is abundant in the PS diet and linked to high abundance of specific bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"α-linoleic acid is a fatty acid observed to be positively correlated with the PS diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARGAROLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Margaroleic acid is a fatty acid positively correlated with lignocellulose diet in Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acet is a compound found in mealworm larvae, related to specific dietary correlations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUCIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AMINO ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leucin is an amino acid correlated with lignocellulose diet in the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGNOCELLULOSE DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lignocellulose diet consists of cellulose, hemicellulose, and lignin, having specific chemical and biological impacts on Tenebrio molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
