      <data key="d0">"ORDERS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These orders of bacteria are typically involved in nitrogen and other biochemical cycles within the microbial environment of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OATMEAL DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Oatmeal Diet is considered an optimal natural food for larvae, usually associated with their natural life cycle and lower mortality."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEREAL BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cereal Bran is used with polystyrene in larvae diets to improve survival rates and promote full growth of generations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL., 2018A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SCIENTIFIC REFERENCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A reference to a study that investigated the biodegradation process associated with T. molitor consuming PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Study by Yang et al. demonstrating that a cereal and polystyrene diet increases larvae survival and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reference to research that further explores polymer depolymerization processes, contributing to the understanding of microbial roles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. (2018a) is a reference to previous studies on larval growth and development, providing context for the current experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL ORDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Significant bacterial orders inhabiting the digestive system of larvae vary depending on the diet they are fed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACID SYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty Acid Synthesis is influenced by the type of diet, showing dysfunction in the Oatmeal diet and PS diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN SYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein Synthesis appears preserved in larvae even with nitrogen-deficient diets like PS, though influenced by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein synthesis is the process cells use to create proteins, heavily reliant on the availability of nitrogen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance used as an indicator of a biological state, often in reference to Phytane."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ratio of protein to fat in larvae can serve as a biomarker for physiological and cultural changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN CONVERSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
