    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDITERRANEAN FRUIT FLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species used as a comparative standard for evaluating nitrogen-fixing activity in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mediterranean fruit fly is a species whose microbiosa during ontogeny is influenced by phylogenetic, metabolic, and taxonomic diversities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH GALLERIA MELLONELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Caterpillars of the wax moth Galleria mellonella are noted for their capability to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The wax moth Galleria mellonella is noted for its larvae's capability to consume and reduce polyethylene, offering novel insights into plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076</data>
