    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN FIXATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process by which nitrogen in the Earth's atmosphere is converted into ammonia or other molecules available to living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biological nitrogen fixation in insects affects ecosystems and provides insights into nutrient cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the process by which nitrogen in the atmosphere is converted into ammonia, notably enhanced in PP-fed larvae's intestinal bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the process of converting atmospheric nitrogen into a form that plants and other organisms can assimilate, playing a crucial role in ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is a process by the gut flora which is lessened when larvae are fed with a PE diet, affecting the nutrient composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the conversion of nitrogen from the atmosphere into ammonia, a form usable by living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of converting atmospheric nitrogen into ammonia or related molecules in living organisms, important for the diazotrophic community in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is a process by which nitrogen in the air is converted into ammonia (NH3) or other molecules available to living organisms, studied in plastic-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is a process by which nitrogen in the Earth's atmosphere is converted into ammonia by living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is a process by which nitrogen in the atmosphere is converted into ammonia, an essential process for incorporating nitrogen into living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the process by which certain organisms convert atmospheric nitrogen into a form usable by plants and animals, here demonstrated in plastic-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the process by which nitrogen in the Earth's atmosphere is converted into ammonia or other molecules available to living organisms, often facilitated by symbiotic and free-living microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the process by which organisms convert atmospheric nitrogen into a usable form for biological processes, facilitated by gut bacteria in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the process of converting atmospheric nitrogen into bioavailable forms, critical for nitrogen-deficient environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation refers to the process through which nitrogen in the atmosphere is converted into ammonia, a form that can be assimilated by organisms. In this study, it is observed in Styrofoam-eating mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252</data>
    </node>
