    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PP (Polypropylene) depolymerization is a microbial-influenced process where polypropylene polymers are broken down, a capability seen in specific beetle larvae when gut microbes are present."&lt;SEP&gt;"The initial breakdown of nonhydrolyzable PP polymers by extracellular enzymes, leading to the formation of smaller particles and molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENITROGEN GAS FIXATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
