      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC) is a synthetic plastic polymer used in construction and pipes, notable for its durability and environmental impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) is a synthetic plastic polymer used in construction for pipes, electrical cable insulation, and signage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl chloride is a synthetic plastic polymer that can be degraded by specific bacteria found in insect larvae guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) is a synthetic thermoplastic polymer targeted for microbial degradation, particularly by bacteria isolated from insect guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) is a type of plastic that has been shown to be degradable by specific bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyvinyl chloride is a type of plastic that is subject to degradation by bacterial consortia enriched from insect gut microbiota."</data>
