    <node id="&quot;DIAZOTROPHIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A community of microorganisms capable of fixing nitrogen, identified within plastic-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen, potentially found in plastic-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diazotrophic community consists of microorganisms capable of fixing nitrogen, often playing a role in nitrogen cycling within ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophic communities are groups of microorganisms capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophic community refers to a group of microorganisms, including certain bacteria, capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen, present in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophic community consists of nitrogen-fixing bacteria in plastic-eating mealworms, playing a role in nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
