    <node id="&quot;LIPASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes that assist in breaking down specific chemical bonds within PU molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes involved in decomposing polyurethane by breaking down its chemical structure, aiding the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes that aid in the breakdown of lipids, facilitating both the synthesis and degradation of polymers, and have applications in biotechnology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes that hydrolyze fats and certain polymers, involved in the breakdown of plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes involved in the breakdown of lipids and, in this study, related to degradation processes of polymeric substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes assessed for their function against bacteria on NPS emulsion using Tween 80 as the substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes produced by Achromobacter, important for degrading fats and oils."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are extracellular enzymes tested for their activity in the breakdown of lipids using Tween 80 as a substrate."</data>
