    <node id="&quot;PROTEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme that hydrolyzes proteins, utilized in the mealworm's digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protease is an enzyme whose activity was measured through the hydrolysis of p-nitroaniline."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protease is an enzyme capable of breaking peptide bonds in proteins, contributing to the metabolic variety seen in some bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protease is an enzyme that breaks down proteins into smaller peptides or amino acids, commonly detected in biochemical assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc</data>
    </node>
