      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The modified method of Preiser et al. is used to measure protease activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme that breaks down ester bonds, involved in breaking down polyurethanes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esterase is an enzyme whose activity was determined through the hydrolysis of p-nitrophenyl acetate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esterase, an enzyme that hydrolyzes ester bonds, with substantial activity observed in bacterial strains like Achromobacter xylosidans M9."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esterase, an enzyme that acts in the enzymatic recycling of thermoplastic polyurethanes, showing a synergistic effect with amidease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esterase is an enzyme showing increased activity in larvae fed polyethylene diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558</data>
    </node>
