    <node id="&quot;TOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toxicity refers to the degree to which a substance can harm organisms, as studied in the impact of microplastics like PVC, PS, and PLA on larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects caused by certain plastics like polyethylene on yellow mealworm health and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the degree to which a substance can harm organisms. The toxicity of polystyrene microplastics to earthworms is decreased by a protective soil layer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the degree to which a substance can harm organisms, which is evaluated in the DEB model context."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0afd02f25b584d6e3a755fc7272b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </node>
