    <node id="&quot;AROMATIC COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aromatic compounds are a class of compounds, some of which are broken down by the enzymatic activity in Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic compounds characterized by planar ring structures, significant in metabolic degradation pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aromatic compounds such as benzoate, amino benzoate, and fluorobenzoate serve as metabolic intermediates during PET degradation, with gut microbes showing chemotaxis towards them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964</data>
