      <data key="d2">chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAC640&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene significantly upregulated in PS-/CS-fed larvae for oxidizing polymers' side chains or breaking C-C bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is a gene that was upregulated in both PS- and CS-fed Tenebrio molitor and expressed in E. coli, showing degradation potential for polystyrene and lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is a laccase enzyme involved in the degradation of lignocellulose and PS, examined for its activity and kinetics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is a laccase enzyme that can degrade lignin and is involved in the degradation of plastics via oxidation reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is an enzyme referenced in the context of being used to treat PS/CS samples, possibly for experimental observations on changes in surface morphology and functional groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. COLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common bacterium used as a reference in studies about biofilm formation and microbial interactions with nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a bacterium used as a negative control in biofilm production experiments on polystyrene surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a common bacterium in which the lac640 gene was expressed to demonstrate its capability to degrade PS and lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is used for the overexpression of the lac640 gene to analyze its degradation capabilities on plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a commonly studied bacterium used in various biological and ecological studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a model bacterium used as a reference with a doubling time of 68.3 minutes in its exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is used as a negative control in the study, showing no degradation activity on polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escherichia coli is a reference strain used to compare doubling time in nutrient media experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
