    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CK GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CK group is the control group of mealworms in the study, used for comparisons against PS and CS-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEOMIC SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteomic sequencing is used in the study to analyze protein expressions related to PS and CS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEGG GENE ANNOTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KEGG gene annotation is used to classify and understand gene function changes in different dietary groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZOATE DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzoate Degradation is a pathway involved in the metabolism and breakdown of benzoate within PET degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benzoate degradation is a metabolic pathway enriched in PS and CS-fed groups, indicating specific microbial activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd</data>
