      <data key="d2">chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG-CHAIN FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acids with long aliphatic tails, involved in/metabolized by lipid biosynthesis and degradation pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long-Chain Fatty Acids are the products of polymer degradation metabolized for energy through processes like β-oxidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long-chain fatty acids are lipids that undergo β-oxidation, breaking down into acetyl-CoA for energy production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long-chain fatty acids are a type of fatty acid with 13-21 carbon atoms, playing a role in energy storage and cellular structure in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKYLGLYCEROL MONOOXYGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkylglycerol Monooxygenase is involved in the oxidative cleavage of the benzene ring in the degradation of PS and lignin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLESTERASE (CES1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylesterase (CES1) is responsible for hydrolyzing esters into long-chain fatty acids during degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG-CHAIN FATTY ACID-COA LIGASE (ACSL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Long-Chain Fatty Acid-CoA Ligase (ACSL) activates long-chain fatty acids, preparing them for further metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Β-OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"β-Oxidation refers to the catabolic process where fatty acids are broken down to generate acetyl-CoA, entering the TCA cycle for energy production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYP4/6&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
