    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial diversity assesses the variety and differences in the microbial communities found in the gut of larvae, affected by diet and ecological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial diversity refers to the variety of microorganisms present in a given ecosystem, crucial for degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial diversity refers to the variety of microorganisms present in an environment, contributing to the resilience and functions of ecosystems, notably affected by pollutants like hexachlorocyclohexane."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669</data>
    </node>
