    <node id="&quot;MEALWORMS (TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms are a type of larvae known for their ability to degrade polystyrene, altering their gut microbiome and metabolic pathways in response to the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, capable of biodegrading major plastic polymers, including high-crystallinity PET."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOST GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Host genes in mealworms are upregulated for PET depolymerization and metabolism, playing a crucial role in the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER CHAIN SIZE&quot;">
