    <node id="&quot;PET DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process by which polyethylene terephthalate, a type of plastic, is broken down into its monomers or smaller units."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET depolymerization is the breakdown of PET plastics facilitated by various biological mechanisms, including microbial activity and isotopic exchange."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which T. molitor larvae break down poly(ethylene terephthalate) (PET) polymers, shown to occur independently of gut microbes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c</data>
