      <data key="d1">"A non-parametric method for testing whether samples originate from the same distribution, used here to analyze microbiome data."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Kruskal-Wallis test is a non-parametric method used for comparing multiple groups, allowing differential analysis of unigenes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A non-parametric method used for comparing diversity indices across groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"A statistical test used to identify differences in median values across multiple groups, applied here to test diversity indices."</data>
