      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;*DAPHNIA MAGNA*&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Daphnia magna are used in ecotoxicological simulations to assess the toxicity of polyethylene degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;*RATTUS NORVEGICUS*&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rattus norvegicus are used in simulations to evaluate the ecotoxicity of polyethylene degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ecotoxicity refers to the potential for chemical substances to harm ecosystems, as studied in relation to polyethylene degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE PHYSICAL-CHEMICAL PROPERTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The physical and chemical properties of polyethylene, such as polymer chain branching and crystallinity, affect its degradation by Tenebrio larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
    </node>
