    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEPIDOPTERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lepidoptera is an order of insects, including moths and butterflies, some of which have been observed to decompose plastics as a food source in vivo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lepidoptera is the order of insects that includes butterflies and moths, noted for their potential in plastic biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lepidoptera is the order to which Greater Wax Moth belongs, characterized by species such as moths and butterflies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPODOPTERA FRUGIPERDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spodoptera frugiperda, known as the fall armyworm, capable of degrading polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTICS (PCPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE's biodegradability is influenced by its physical characteristics such as molecular weight, branching, and crystallinity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRALIDAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A family of moths, some of which have larvae capable of plastic ingestion and biodegradation, like the Indian mealmoth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyralidae is a family of moths, whose larvae are noted for their ability to chew and ingest plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyralidae, a family of moths, is involved in biodegradation studies, particularly in the breakdown of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
