      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CI is an indicator of the oxidation level and degree of aging of microplastics impacting their biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl Index is a measure obtained from FTIR spectra to quantify the extent of oxidation in polyethylene during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Carbonyl index measures the oxidation levels of polyethylene microplastics through spectroscopy, based on carbonyl peak intensity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a measure used to quantify the presence of carbonyl groups, which can indicate oxidative degradation in polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
