      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval diet refers to the feeding regimen for the larvae, influencing factors like microbial community and physiological responses which were analyzed in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-AOC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-AOC stands for total antioxidant capacity, a measure used to assess the oxidative stress levels in larvae exposed to PE MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QSR PREDICTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"QSR prediction refers to the quantitative structure-activity relationship used to predict the toxicity of PE MPs degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATIONAL TAXONOMIC UNITS (OTUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clusters used to categorize and analyze microorganisms based on genetic identity in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs are classification entities used to categorize and identify microorganisms based on genetic sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Units used for classifying groups of closely related individuals or sequences in microbial studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs are operational definitions used to classify groups of closely related individuals or sequences, often based on the similarity of 16S rRNA gene sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVA 138 16S RRNA DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATABASE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Silva 138 database is used for taxonomic analysis of 16S rRNA gene sequences, aiding in microbial identification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABUND JACCARD DISTANCE-BASED REDUNDANCY ANALYSIS (DBRDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"dbRDA is a statistical method used to analyze variation in microbial community data based on abundance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VARIATION PARTITIONING ANALYSIS (VPA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOMETRIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"VPA is a statistical analysis method that partitions the variance in PS consumption based on different contributing factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"VPA is a statistical method used to determine the explanatory value of different variables in a study."&lt;SEP&gt;"VPA is based on partial RDA to distinguish the unique and shared influence of variables on PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTIAL LEAST SQUARES STRUCTURAL EQUATION MODELING (PLS-SEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PLS-SEM is a modeling technique used to study relationships among variables in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMARTPLS3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SmartPLS3 is a software used for conducting Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modeling (PLS-SEM)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATH COEFFICIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Path coefficients represent the strength and direction of relationships between variables in SEM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATISTICAL GOODNESS OF FIT (GOF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GOF is a statistic used to determine how well a model fits a set of observations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHTED GENE CO-EXPRESSION NETWORK ANALYSIS (WGCNA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WGCNA is a method used to find clusters of highly correlated genes and to relate gene networks to other traits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAX4FUN2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tax4Fun2 is a program used for predicting functional profiles of microbial communities based on 16S rRNA marker gene data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T.E.S.T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T.E.S.T is a tool used to perform quantitative structure-activity relationship (QSR) predictions for assessing chemical toxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RATTUS NORVEGICUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rattus norvegicus, the Norway rat, is used in the study to predict acute oral toxicity of chemical substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORIGIN (V. 2022B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Origin is a software suite used for data analysis and graphing in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Origin is a software used for statistical analysis and graphing in various scientific studies, version 2022b was employed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOVA ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ANOVA (Analysis of Variance) is a statistical method used to assess the differences in specific response variables, such as survival rates and microbial diversity, in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR ANALYSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR (Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy) analyses indicate formation of oxidative functional groups in biodegraded polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to obtain the infrared spectrum of absorption, emission, and photoconductivity of polyethylene in the study to identify functional groups formed during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analyses are used to detect chemical changes in the fecula of mealworms, suggesting polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy analyses used to assess the chemical structure and biodegradation of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPECR, or the Specific Plastic Consumption Rate, measures the amount of polyethylene consumed by the larvae per day."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL POLYMER CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The residual polymer content refers to the percentage of polyethylene remaining after being processed by larvae, measured to evaluate biodegradation efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MN (NUMBER AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mn represents the average molecular weight of polymers, important for understanding how polymers degrade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MW (WEIGHT AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mw provides an average based on the weight contributions of the polymer molecules, indicating polymer stability and changes post-biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MZ (Z AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mz reflects a higher moment of polymer molecular weight distribution, capturing significant changes in polymer chain length upon degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLIC ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylic acids are formed during the oxidation and biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids formed as a result of oxidative degradation of polyethylene, detectable in chemical analysis through FTIR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are part of the mealworm biodegradation byproducts that undergo pyrolysis in specific temperature ranges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic compounds released by PVC that contribute to mass loss in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KETONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ketones are a type of functional group identified through FTIR analysis, indicating degradation effects on polyethylene chains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ketones are another oxidized product indicating degradation of the polyethylene polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ketones are compounds with a carbonyl group attached to two hydrocarbon groups, often mentioned as environmentally and health hazardous substances in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T. OBSCURUS LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another group of larvae used to compare survival rates and dietary impacts with T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae of Tenebrio obscurus used in antibiotic suppression tests and microbial community analyses."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae participate in the biodegradation of LLDPE, LDPE, and HDPE microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae, as members of the insect class, participate in biodegrading polyethylene polymers, displaying unique consumption rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae are another type of larvae used for the biodegradation of PE foams in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The carbonyl index is a measure used to indicate the level of oxidation in plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbonyl index measures the degree of oxidation of polyethylene polymers in the frass of T. molitor and T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbonyl index measures the level of oxidation in polyethylene, indicating polymer degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDEHYDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aldehydes are found as a result of oxidative reactions in the polyethylene during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactones represent cyclic esters formed as a structural marker in polyethylene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O-C GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-O-C groups are indicative of oxidative changes in polyethylene polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PE CONSUMPTION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The specific polyethylene consumption rate indicates the amount of PE consumed by larvae over a certain period, reflecting their metabolic activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PE IN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual polyethylene in frass refers to the amount of unconsumed PE found in the waste of larvae, indicating the extent of degradation or metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CI (CARBONYL INDEX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbonyl index is used to quantify the degree of oxidation in polyethylene, involved in assessing its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMINOIC GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An aminoic group is incorporated into the structure of oxidized polyethylene as observed in larvae frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDEHYDE GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An aldehyde group is incorporated into oxidized polyethylene, which is noted in the spectral analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHYL GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methyl groups are identified as part of the increased peaks shown in the NMR spectra from T. molitor and T. obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNSATURATED ALLYLIC GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This group is identified as part of the oxidative degradation process of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE POWDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE powders, including LDPE, HDPE, and LLDPE, are the experimental materials fed to T. molitor and T. obscurus to study their biodegradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC PRODUCTS (MPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic products of polyethylene degradation, indicated by increased PE residues in the frass of T. molitor and T. obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENG ET AL., 2019&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A reference study that previously analyzed the oxidative ability of T. molitor and T. obscurus on polystyrene, providing background context."&lt;SEP&gt;"A study that examined the diet and biodegradation capabilities of T. obscurus in relation to gut microbes and antibiotic influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reference to prior research contributing insights into polymer breakdown by larvae and microbe interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENG ET AL., 2023A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reference to a study detailing nutritional components such as Cys content in T. obscurus, relevant to the amino acid differential analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DING ET AL., 2023&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Study referenced for providing comparative data on amino acid content, such as Cys, in T. obscurus and T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1.4 TO 1.7 PPM (NMR SPECTRA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific range in the 1H NMR spectra indicating extra peaks in the frass samples from T. molitor compared to T. obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPED is a type of polymer mentioned in the text along with its quantified properties, given in mean and standard deviation, which were not determined in some cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLDPED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LLDPED is a type of polymer with specific measured properties provided in terms of mean and standard deviation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HDPED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HDPED is another polymer analyzed in the study, with certain properties not determined and others provided with mean and standard deviation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WB D&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WB D is wheat bran used as a control or comparative product in the study, showing distinct measured properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPEY is a mentioned product with specific properties studied, given in terms of mean and standard deviation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLDPEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LLDPEY is a polymer with provided quantitative attributes, mentioned in the context of gut microbiome diversity study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HDPEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HDPEY is a type of polymer analyzed for its properties, mentioned with mean and standard deviation values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WBY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WBY refers to wheat bran used in the study as a comparative product to polymers, highlighting different measured properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMPSON DIVERSITY INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOSTATISTICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An index used to measure microbial species richness and diversity based on proportions of species present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simpson Diversity Index is used to measure the diversity of the gut microbiome in the larvae of Tenebrio species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEIP EVENNESS INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heip Evenness Index assesses the evenness in the species diversity of gut microbiomes of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HDPE-FED LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HDPE-fed larvae are characterized by lower evenness in their gut microbial community, suggesting dominant taxa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVINS OTU ABUNDANCE MATRIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Levins OTU Abundance Matrix is a method for assessing the niche breadth and environmental interactions of OTUs in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NICHE BREADTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Niche breadth refers to the extent of resource utilization by OTUs, as measured by the Levins OTU abundance matrix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Β DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"β Diversity measures the changes in the gut microbial community composition between different groups of Tenebrio larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ΒNTI/RCBRAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"βNTI (Beta Nearest Taxon Index) and RCbray are methods used to analyze microbial community assembly in Tenebrio larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTIAL LEAST SQUARES PATH MODELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL METHOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Partial least squares path modeling is used to analyze the effects of variables on gut communities and molecular weight changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MN (NUMBER AVERAGED MOLECULAR WEIGHT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mn refers to the average molecular weight of polymer numbers, a parameter analyzed in relation to microbial community changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MW (WEIGHT AVERAGED MOLECULAR WEIGHT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mw is the weight-averaged molecular weight of polymers, studied alongside microbial changes in Tenebrio larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MZ (SIZE AVERAGED MOLECULAR WEIGHT)&quot;">
