    <node id="&quot;STRAIN YT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain YT2 is a microorganism capable of degrading PS (polystyrene) by oxidizing its structure, resulting in more polar derivatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strain YT2 is capable of degrading PS films by forming biofilms, altering surface topography and increasing oxygen content on the film's surface."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C−O GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The C−O group is a functional group observed in PS films when oxidized by strain YT2, indicating increased polar compound formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;$M_N$ AND $M_W$ VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"$M_n$ and $M_w$ represent the number-average and weight-average molecular weights, respectively, of polymers used in studying how Styrofoam is degraded by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESEM IMAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental scanning electron microscopy (ESEM) images provide visual data on gut microorganisms in mealworms and biofilm structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;$\DELTA^{13}$C VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"$\delta^{13}$C values are isotope ratios used to analyze CO2 production and confirm metabolic activities in experiments with mealworms fed labeled PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R. RUBER C208&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R. ruber C208 is a bacterial strain used as a comparison in studying polystyrene degradation efficiency, showing lower degradation efficacy compared to strain YT2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RNA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 16S RNA gene is utilized in constructing a phylogenetic tree for strain YT2, indicating its genetic relation and identity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC (GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An analytical method used to measure ethylene production in nitrogen fixation assays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gas Chromatography is a technique used to analyze the extracts from cultures inoculated with strain YT2 and control samples to determine degradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DECREASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight decrease refers to the reduction in the average molecular weight of polystyrene due to degradation by strain YT2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LCFBM (LIQUID CULTURE FERMENTATION BROTH MEDIUM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LCFBM is the growth medium used for incubating strain YT2 with polystyrene samples to facilitate degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC/MS (GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY-MASS SPECTROMETRY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC/MS is an analytical method used to identify water-soluble degradation products from polystyrene pieces in the presence or absence of strain YT2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE CATABOLIC CLUSTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The styrene catabolic cluster is a group of genes responsible for the degradation of styrene by Pseudomonas sp. strain Y2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL STYRENE DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial styrene degradation is the breakdown of styrene by microorganisms through biochemical processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTODEGRADED POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photodegraded polymers are polymers that have been broken down by exposure to light, specifically investigated here for their biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photodegraded polymers are polymers that have undergone degradation due to exposure to light, making them more susceptible to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL DEGRADATION OF STYRENE OLIGOMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial degradation of styrene oligomer refers to the breakdown of styrene oligomers by microorganisms, indicating their ability to process complex organic compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION OF SYNTHETIC PLASTIC AND FOAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation of synthetic plastic and foams involves the breakdown of these synthetic materials by biological means, such as microbial action."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNTHETIC PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Synthetic plastic is a man-made material composed of polymers, often resistant to natural degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PACKAGING FILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Packaging films are thin layers of plastic material used for protecting and containing products, tested for resistance against insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VELVETBEAN CATERPILLAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The velvetbean caterpillar, Anticarsia gemmatalis, is an insect that hosts gut bacteria which aid in its digestion and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene plastic is a type of plastic that can be degraded using solid-phase photocatalytic processes with TiO2 as a photocatalyst."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIO2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TiO2, or titanium dioxide, is used as a photocatalyst in the solid-phase photocatalytic degradation of polystyrene plastic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;L. E. VISOTTO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"L. E. Visotto is one of the authors of the study on gut bacteria's contribution to digestion in velvetbean caterpillars."</data>
