      <data key="d2">chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M. CHAI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M. Chai is one of the authors of the study on photocatalytic degradation of polystyrene plastic using TiO2 as the catalyst."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Y. ZHU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Y. Zhu is one of the authors of the study on photocatalytic degradation of polystyrene plastic using TiO2 as the catalyst."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMIN B6&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamin B6 metabolism shows varied responses in different insect models when exposed to plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL CARBON METABOLISM (CCM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CCM includes a suite of compounds fundamental to cellular pathways and is analyzed in this study to understand insect metabolism when exposed to plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"CCM refers to the metabolic pathways analyzed in the study to understand the effect of plastic exposure on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Carbon Metabolism is a suite of biochemical pathways fundamental in all living organisms, responding to nutrient availability and steering nutrients for physiological needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Carbon Metabolism refers to the integrated processes of metabolic pathways that involve carbon flow, analyzed in the context of insect interactions with plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRIMIDINE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Essential metabolic pathway for RNA and DNA synthesis, as well as for membrane lipid biosynthesis and protein glycosylation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrimidine metabolism is a cellular process involved in generating necessary substrates for basic cellular functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrimidine metabolism was found to be elevated in Black Soldier Fly larvae when reared on Polyethylene terephthalate (PET)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein products derived from insects reared on plastic substrates are considered valuable for their potential nutritional benefit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIPTERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diptera is the taxonomic order to which the Black Soldier Fly belongs, known for species that can degrade plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARASTOC GOLDEN YOLK® POULTRY PELLETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Barastoc golden yolk® poultry pellets are used in the diet for rearing BSF larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEE WAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bee wax is a natural substance consumed by Greater Wax Moth, potentially aiding its ability to degrade plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLASSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molasses is a supplement mixed with water and applied during the study to potentially affect insect metabolism when exposed to plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molasses is used as a food supplement, improving energy utilization for mealworm and wax moth models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK SOLDIER FLY (BSF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BSF is an insect model used to study metabolic interactions and responses to different plastic types."&lt;SEP&gt;"BSF is one of the insect species used in the study to evaluate the impact of exposure to different plastics on insect metabolism and larval development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black Soldier Fly refers to the genus of the used larvae, recognized for its potential in biodegradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM (MW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MW is another insect species used in the study, reared and fed on wheat bran, fresh carrot, and sweet potato."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm is an insect model used to study metabolic responses and plastic degradation when reared on various plastic substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH (WM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WM is also an insect species involved in the study to assess the effects of plastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth is an insect model that shows positive metabolic responses to plastic substrates and food supplements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
