    <node id="&quot;NANOPOLYSTYRENE (NPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nanopolystyrene is a form of polystyrene reduced to nanometer-sized particles commonly studied for degradation by bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nanopolystyrene refers to smaller-sized polystyrene particles that are biodegraded more efficiently compared to larger polystyrene films, owing to their greater surface area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEM (TRANSMISSION ELECTRON MICROSCOPE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TEM is a microscopy technique used to observe the internal structure and chemical changes in nanoplastic particles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL SIGNALING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial signaling refers to the communication between microorganisms, which can be disrupted by nanoplastic pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWIGWORM DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The diet of mealworms includes expanded polystyrene (EPS) and polyethylene (PE), which is utilized in the study to analyze plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANOPOLYMER STYRENE (NPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nanopolymer Styrene (NPS) is synthesized as part of the study and characterized using various techniques to understand its degradation properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLOMETABOLIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Holometabolic refers to insects that undergo complete metamorphosis involving four life stages: egg, larva, pupa, and adult."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holometabolic refers to the complete metamorphosis that Tenebrio molitor undergoes, including life stages such as egg, larva, pupa, and imago."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC CAPABILITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic capabilities describe the bacterium's ability to enhance plant growth and exhibit biopesticidal and antifungal properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANHYDROUS ETHANOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anhydrous ethanol is used in the sterilization process of polystyrene films, emphasizing its solvent properties in laboratory settings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterilization refers to the process applied to the polystyrene films to ensure they are free from any contaminants before experimentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL AND CHEMICAL PROPERTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical and chemical properties are analyzed in the study to characterize the synthesized nanopolymer styrene using techniques like XRD and SEM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NPS (NANO-POLYSTYRENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NPS (Nano-polystyrene) was the sole carbon source in the media to test bacterial degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON-FREE BASAL MEDIA (CFBM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEDIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CBFM is the medium used for culturing bacteria with NPS as the sole carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon-Free Basal Media was used to test the ability of microbes to degrade NPS as their sole carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESCHERICHIA COLI ATCC 25922&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Escherichia coli strain ATCC 25922 was used as a negative control in the experiments on NPS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LURIA-BERTANI (LB) BROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEDIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LB Broth serves as a standard medium for bacterial culture and was used for purifying isolates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORMAL SALINE SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEDIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Normal Saline Solution was used to homogenize the gut contents of mealworms before culturing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POUR PLATE METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Pour Plate Method was employed to culture bacteria on NPS-CFB agar media."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-PRESSURE STEAM STERILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-Pressure Steam Sterilization was used to sterilize media and tools to prevent contamination during experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An autoclave was used for the high-pressure steam sterilization of media and tools."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZNSO4 · 7 H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zinc sulfate used as a trace element in Carbon-Free Basal Media to support bacterial growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MNSO4 · H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Manganese sulfate used as a micro-nutrient in Carbon-Free Basal Media for bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FESO4 · 7 H2O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iron(II) sulfate used in CFBM to provide essential iron for microbial growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEGATIVE CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL SETUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Negative control uses uninoculated flasks to assess background activity, ensuring observed changes are due to the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POSITIVE CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL SETUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Positive control uses emulsified NPS to validate the degradation capability of NPS degrading isolates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD PLATE COUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standard Plate Count is a method for quantifying viable bacterial cells in a sample based on Bankier et al.'s methodology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard Plate Count is a process used to determine the number of viable bacterial cells in a sample, differentiating between bacterial growth and cloudiness caused by Nano-polystyrene in the medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TURBIDITY ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Turbidity Assay is a process used to measure the reduction in cloudiness of an NPS emulsion by measuring absorbance changes before and after incubation with a culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Turbidity Assay is used in this context to indirectly assess bacterial growth by measuring the cloudiness of a liquid culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Turbidity assay is a method used to assess the relative bacterial growth or the effectiveness of biodegradation by measuring cloudiness in a culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANO-POLYSTYRENE (NPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nano-polystyrene is a polymer material that can cause cloudiness in liquid media, challenging the differentiation from bacterial cell growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BANKIER ET AL. (2018)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bankier et al. (2018) refers to the approach used for bacterial enumeration in the study, contributing to standardized methodologies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BROMOCRESOL PURPLE (BCP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bromocresol Purple is an indicator used in the Acid Production Assay to detect acid production by indicating a color change."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M9&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An abbreviation for Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9, a bacterial strain isolated from mealworms, examined for its plastic-degrading capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"M9 is a bacterial strain that appears to play a role in the experimental setup for polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"M9 is a microbe involved in biofilm production studies, serving as a subject in experiments on NPS effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"M9, also known as Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9, is a bacterial isolate exhibiting significant capabilities in degrading polystyrene, characterized by its high growth rate and enzymatic activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTAL VIOLET (CV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystal Violet is a chemical stain used to determine biofilm population density through colorimetric absorbance measurement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS OF PS FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight Loss of PS Film is a measure used to evaluate the biodegradation of polystyrene film by microorganisms over a period of 30 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16SRDNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16SrDNA is a gene region used for the identification and phylogenetic analysis of bacterial strains through PCR and sequencing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER XYLOSIDANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium with biocontrol potential against Fusarium wilt of melon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter xylosidans is a bacterial species identified in the study, involved in NPS degradation and biofilm formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGA 11 SOFTWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEGA 11 software is a computational tool used for constructing phylogenetic trees to analyze the evolutionary relations of bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic Activity Screening is a process of evaluating isolates for extracellular enzyme activity, such as cellulases, esterases, lipases, proteases, and laccases on various substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACID PRODUCTION ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acid Production Assay is a process used to detect and quantify acid production by bacterial isolates using NPS as a sole carbon source, indicated by a color change in the presence of Bromocresol Purple."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON-FREE BASAL (CFB) MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon-Free Basal Media is used in the Acid Production Assay to provide a controlled environment without carbon sources, helping to test bacteria's ability to produce acid using NPS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACIDITY INDEX (AI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acidity Index is a measure used in the Acid Production Assay to quantify acid production, calculated by comparing the diameters of yellow zones and the colony."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTAL VIOLET STAINING METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystal Violet Staining Method is a process used to quantify biofilm density by staining bacterial biomass and measuring the absorbance of ethanol extracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE (PS) FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene Film is a polymer material whose biodegradation is tested by measuring weight loss after incubation with microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCR AMPLIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to amplify DNA sequences for the identification and study of nitrogen-fixing bacterial isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR Amplification is a biological process used to amplify specific regions of bacterial DNA, such as 16SrDNA, for identification and phylogenetic analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR Amplification is a technique used to replicate DNA segments, crucial for analyzing genetic material such as 16S rRNA genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR Amplification is a laboratory method used to amplify DNA regions of interest from the mealworm's gut microbiome for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLULASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellulases are enzymes evaluated for their ability to act against bacteria on NPS emulsion using carboxymethyl cellulose as the substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulases are enzymes that break down cellulose, an important component of plant structure, enabling decomposition of plant material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellulases are extracellular enzymes tested for activity using carboxymethyl cellulose as a substrate to understand their role in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL DIGESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial digestion is a physical method used to isolate nanoplastics from biological cells using 10% KOH, promoting effective cell digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTICLE COUNT ANALYSIS (PCA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to analyze the count and size of nanoplastic particles using an inverted microscope and ImageJ software for image processing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYMETHYL CELLULOSE (CMC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substrate used for testing cellulase activity when evaluated against bacteria capable of growing on NPS emulsion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWEEN 20&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substrate used to evaluate esterase activity in the hydrolytic process involving bacteria on NPS emulsion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tween 20 is a detergent used in cleaning solutions to help separate and purify polystyrene fragments during experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWEEN 80&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substrate used to assess lipase activity for bacteria growing on NPS emulsion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUAIACOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substrate used for determining laccase activity in bacteria via color change."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IODINE SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Used to saturate plates in cellulase assays for detecting hydrolysis zones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOH (POTASSIUM HYDROXIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Used in the microbial digestion process for isolating nanoplastics without affecting their structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLOROFORM: ISOPROPANOL MIXTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solvent system used for separating nanoplastics from other materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTICLE SIZE ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A quantitative analysis of nanoplastic particles using Nanosizer to measure diameter and size variation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANOSIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A device used to determine the mean diameter and size variation of nanoparticles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SONICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique utilized to disperse PS particles by breaking up aggregates in a nanoparticle solution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERMENTATION BROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medium that supports microbial growth, mentioned indirectly in the microbial digestion context."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262d7fa1c8f2581943a41cf4897fa253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE STYROFOAM (EPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EPS is a type of plastic material used in the diet setup for mealworm consumption experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANOPLASTIC POWDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nanoplastic Powder is a byproduct of mealworm larvae's chewing and digestion of EPS materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NPS EMULSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NPS emulsion refers to a specific setup or state used in experimental conditions for polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATR-FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED ANALYSIS (ATR-FTIR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ATR-FTIR is an analytical technique used to obtain the infrared absorption spectra to identify functional groups on the NPS surface."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY-MASS SPECTROSCOPY (GCMS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GCMS is an analytical technique used to detect NPS degradation products, involving the separation and analysis of components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANALYSIS OF VARIANCE (ANOVA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ANOVA is a statistical method used to evaluate the differences in plastic consumption and other experimental parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA was used to test differences in mass changes of mealworms and mass loss of materials as part of the study's statistical analyses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUNCAN'S MULTIPLE COMPARISON TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Duncan's multiple comparison test is employed to analyze statistical significance among multiple datasets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M1–9&quot;">
