      <data key="d1">"A bacterial strain suggested to contribute to polystyrene degradation, isolated from the intestines of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterium from Tenebrio molitor, demonstrating 6% biodegradation over 30 days in PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 is a bacterial isolate known for its ability to degrade NPS and produce various enzymes including lipases and laccase."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 is one of the NPS-degrading strains identified in the study, contributing to the biodegradation of nanoplastics."</data>
