      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter sp. AnTc-1 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from T. castaneum larvae's gut, known for its strong association with PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. AnTc-1 is a specific PS-degrading bacterium isolated from insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. AnTc-1 is studied in the context of microbiome studies with Tribolium castaneum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strain known for its ability to degrade polystyrene films, previously documented with significant efficacy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. AnTc-1 isolated from the intestine of Tribolium castaneum degrades polystyrene."</data>
