    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight determination in this context indicates the extent of polymer degradation by measuring the decrease in size of polymer residues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE Frass results from the degradation of Polyethylene, showing changes in molecular weight to 71,483 for \(M_{w}\) and 16,462 for \(M_{n}\), with a molecular weight reduction of 51.84% and 47.61%."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE + BRAN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE + Bran Frass is a modified version of PE Frass, with \(M_{w}\) of 88,898 and \(M_{n}\) of 14,397, showing a molecular weight reduction of 19.46% and 12.76%."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS Frass results from the degradation of Polystyrene, with \(M_{w}\) of 137,523 and \(M_{n}\) of 77,229, showing molecular weight reductions similar to those of unmodified PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + BRAN FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS + Bran Frass is a modified version of PS Frass, characterized by changes in molecular structure and molecular weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENSITY (G/CM³)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Density is a physical property measured in grams per cubic centimeter, indicating how much mass is contained in a volume of a substance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT (\(M_{W}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight (\(M_{w}\)) is the weight of molecules averaged over a sample, often used in characterizing polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT (\(M_{N}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight (\(M_{n}\)) is the number-average molecular weight, providing another measure of polymer characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(M_{W}\) REDUCTION (\%)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(M_{w}\) Reduction is the percentage decrease in the weight-average molecular weight, indicating polymer degradation extent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(M_{N}\) REDUCTION (\%)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"\(M_{n}\) Reduction is the percentage decrease in the number-average molecular weight, another indicator of polymer degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIAN MEAL MOTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indian meal moths are insect larvae reported to possess the ability to degrade polyethylene within their gut, though evidence is preliminary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-SPECIFIC DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic-Specific Degradation refers to the concept that most microorganisms are generally capable of degrading specific types of plastics rather than multiple ones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC FOAM PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic foam products, including low-density polyethylene foam and polystyrene foam, are subject to degradation studies to understand their environmental impact."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT AND DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight and density are characteristics of plastics that were measured and shown in the control materials table of the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRAHYDROFURAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solvent used for extracting polymers from frass in plastic degradation studies with PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is an organic solvent used in polymer synthesis and degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORMS FED PE + BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms provided with both Polyethylene and bran for nutritional variation in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENT'S T TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL TEST"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical method used to determine the significance of results in the plastic degradation study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. COLI K12&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E. coli K12 is a strain of bacteria used as a control in the study to check for possible contamination impacts on the mealworm experiments with plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL MODIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical modification refers to the observed changes in the structure of polyethylene and polystyrene once they were processed through mealworm digestion, including the appearance of new functional groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUTATIVE GAS FRACTION (PGF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Putative Gas Fraction is the unmeasured gaseous component that increases during the experiment, indicating plastic mineralization and degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKENE BOND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkene bonds are unsaturated chemical bonds that show up as peaks in NMR spectra, indicating modification in polymer structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN INCORPORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxygen incorporation is a chemical process involved in the biodegradation of plastics, where oxygen is integrated into polymer chains, facilitating breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen incorporation occurs when oxygen atoms become part of a molecule, as seen in the modified plastics, indicating plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen incorporation refers to the addition of oxygen into polystyrene chains during degradation, which is a critical step in breaking down the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The incorporation of oxygen is a chemical reaction observed during the biodegradation of LDPE, leading to new functional groups and material properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PGF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PGF, or plastic to gut feed conversion efficiency, represents the percentage of ingested plastic converted into mealworm biomass, important for studying the efficiency of plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVERSE SIMPSON INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The inverse Simpson index is used to measure the diversity of a microbial community, indicating how evenly the microbes are distributed among a community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER ABSURIAE YTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter absuriae YTI is a known PE-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut of the larvae of Indian mealmoth, indicating its relevance in plastic degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEBALDELLA TERMIDITIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sebaldella termiditis is an anaerobic bacterium isolated phylogenetically within the Fusobacteria phylum, known to inhabit the termite gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREVIBACTERIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brevibacterium sp. are aerobic bacteria linked to hydrocarbon degradation, particularly involving n-alkanes and possibly polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LISTERIA SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Listeria sp. is among the OTUs associated with the PS-fed gut microbiome, indicating involvement in polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDOMICROBIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pedomicrobium sp. is identified as part of the PS-fed gut microbiome, which is important for understanding polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AQUIBABITAN SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aquibabitan sp. is counted among the OTUs showing significance in the polystyrene-degradation process in PS-fed microbiomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAPROPIRACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unclassified Sapropiraceae is among the bacteria in the mealworm gut microbiome associated with PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURKHOLERIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unclassified Burkholeriales is one of the microbial participants assisting in the degradation of PS in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERMITE GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The termite gut habitat is where Sebaldella termiditis naturally resides and performs its anaerobic functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The termite gut hosts symbiotic microbial communities that contribute to nitrogen fixation, allowing termites to digest woody material efficiently."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOLOGICAL SOLUTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiological Solutions involve the use of microorganisms to address and mitigate environmental issues, such as the degradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PEAR is a software tool described as a fast and accurate Illumina Paired-End read merger used in bioinformatics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QIIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOOL/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"QIIME (Quantitative Insights Into Microbial Ecology) is a bioinformatics software package designed for the analysis of microbial communities by interpreting raw DNA sequencing data."&lt;SEP&gt;"QIIME is a platform enabling analysis of high-throughput community sequencing data, assisting in microbial research."&lt;SEP&gt;"QIIME is a software application that allows for the analysis of high-throughput community sequencing data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qiime, a bioinformatics software package, is used for analyzing and interpreting alpha and beta diversity within microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Software used for sequence data analysis, including alpha diversity and community composition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UPARSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"UPARSE is a method used to cluster Operational Taxonomic Units (OTUs) with a high identity threshold in sequence analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"UPARSE is a tool known for producing highly accurate OTU sequences from microbial amplicon reads."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uparse is software used for clustering sequences into operational taxonomic units (OTUs) based on identity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAIVE BAYESIAN CLASSIFIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Naive Bayesian classifier is used for rapid assignment of rRNA sequences into the new bacterial taxonomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VEGAN: COMMUNITY ECOLOGY PACKAGE&quot;">
