      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGESTED FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Egested frass refers to the waste excreted by the lesser waxworms after consuming polyethylene and wax comb, which is analyzed for changes in chemical composition indicating biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The waste material excreted by superworms and yellow mealworms after consuming different diets, analyzed for changes in composition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZENE RING SKELETON VIBRATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzene ring skeleton vibrations are characteristic peaks indicating the presence of benzene rings and are significant in identifying PS structure changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;−CH₂ STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"−CH₂ stretch represents a functional group change observed in polymer structures during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;−OH STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"−OH stretch is a functional group observed in polymers, indicating chemical structure changes during degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO stretch is a key functional group indicative of the incorporation of oxygen during polymer degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R − OH BEND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R − OH bend describes a functional group formed during the chemical transformation and degradation of polymers like PS and PU."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C − O STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C − O stretch is a functional group highlighting the incorporation of oxygen during the degradation process of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECTRA OF FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spectra of frass indicate the chemical changes occurring in polymers after digestion by larvae, providing insight into the degradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
