    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA TENEBRIONIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mixta tenebrionis is a Gram-stain-negative, facultatively anaerobic, motile bacterium with peritrichous flagella, isolated from the gut of the mealworm Tenebrio molitor. It forms yellow, smooth colonies on LB agar and grows in various environmental conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov. is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of the plastic-eating mealworm Tenebrio molitor L., identified as a novel species within the genus Mixta."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIAEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwiniaeae is a family within the class Gammaproteobacteria, containing the genus Mixta among others. It was recently classified to include 14 genera."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria identified in the gut of mealworms, contributing to nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mixta is a genus of bacteria, which includes species like M. calida, M. gaviniae, M. intestinalis, M. theicola, and now the proposed Mixta tenebrionis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mixta is a genus within the family Erwiniaeae, consisting of species reclassified from the genus Pantoea, and characterized by a monophyletic cluster based on MLSA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mixta is the genus being studied, with strain BIT-26T representing a novel species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
