      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NACL TOLERANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NaCl tolerance describes the maximum salt concentration in which bacteria can survive, expressed as a percentage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOGES-PROSKAUER TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Voges-Proskauer test is a biochemical test for determining the fermentation abilities of bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDOLE PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indole production is a test indicating whether a bacterium can produce indole from tryptophan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRATE UTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrate utilization refers to the ability of bacteria to use citrate as a carbon source, analyzed within strain BIT-26T for species differentiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrate utilization reflects a bacterium's ability to use citrate as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYME ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzyme activities include gelatinase, urease, arginine dihydrolase, lysine decarboxylase, or ornithine decarboxylase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA BILLINGEIAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwinia billingeiae is a bacterium included under the LMG 2613 group with specific EU accession numbers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA TYPOGRAPHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwinia typographi is a species of bacterium listed as DSM 22678, identified through certain HQ accession numbers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GELATINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gelatinase is an enzyme activity test used to determine a bacterium's ability to hydrolyze gelatin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARGININE DIHYDROLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arginine dihydrolase is an enzyme activity determining the ability to convert arginine into ornithine and ammonia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYSINE DECARBOXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lysine decarboxylase is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of lysine into cadaverine and carbon dioxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORNITHINE DECARBOXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ornithine Decarboxylase is an enzyme that catalyzes the decarboxylation of ornithine to putrescine, contributing to polyamine biosynthesis in bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ornithine decarboxylase is an enzyme involved in converting ornithine to putrescine, useful in bacterial identification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ornithine decarboxylase is an enzyme that catalyzes the decarboxylation of ornithine to putrescine, indicative of Mixta tenebrionis's metabolic capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Salicin is a biochemical test that indicates the ability of bacteria to produce acid from this carbohydrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Salicin is a compound metabolized by strain BIT-26T to produce acids, which differentiates it from other species within Mixta."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLOBIOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellobiose is a carbohydrate tested for its ability to be fermented by bacteria to produce acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactose is a sugar tested in bacteria for acid production, indicating carbohydrate utilization capacity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAFFINOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Raffinose is a carbohydrate measured to test bacteria's ability to metabolize it into acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D-ARABINOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"d-Arabinol is tested to verify bacteria's ability to ferment it, indicating substrate utilization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D-FUCOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"d-Fucose is a type of sugar tested for bacterial ability to use it as an energy source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCONATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gluconate is a substrate tested in bacteria to measure their ability to oxidize it into acid forms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2-KETO-GLUCONATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2-Keto-gluconate is a derivative measured for bacterial ability to utilize it in oxidative metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-KETO-GLUCONATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5-Keto-gluconate is analyzed in bacterial strains for their oxidation capacity, informing metabolic profiling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA G+C CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA G+C content measures the percentage of guanine-cytosine in bacterial DNA, informing taxonomy and phylogeny."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DNA G+C content refers to the percentage of guanine and cytosine bases in the DNA of an organism, indicating its genomic composition level. Mixta tenebrionis has a DNA G+C content of 56.08%."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTILOCUS SEQUENCE ANALYSIS (MLSA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MLSA is a process for determining species identification by analyzing multiple genetic loci."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C14:0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C14:0 is a specific type of fatty acid identified in the document with relative quantities measured across different samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"C14:0 represents myristic acid, a saturated fatty acid included in the sample evaluations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C16:0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C16:0 is a saturated fatty acid prevalent in the data provided, with quantities noted in several samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"C16:0, also known as palmitic acid, is one of the predominant fatty acids in Mixta tenebrionis."&lt;SEP&gt;"C16:0 stands for palmitic acid, a saturated fatty acid found in varying percentages according to different studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"C16:0, also known as palmitic acid, is a saturated fatty acid that is a major component of the fatty acids measured in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C17:0 CYCLO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C17:0 cyclo is a cyclic fatty acid referenced in the data, measured across different samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C18:0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C18:0 is a saturated fatty acid whose presence is quantified in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"C18:0 refers to stearic acid, a saturated fatty acid included in the analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C19:0 CYCLO 08C&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C19:0 cyclo 08c is a cyclopropane fatty acid found in some samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C19:0 ISO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C19:0 iso is an iso-branched type of fatty acid mentioned in the context of the findings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUMMED FEATURE 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Summed feature 2 is a composite of fatty acids that cannot be separated, including C12:0 aldehyde and possibly other unknown fatty acids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUMMED FEATURE 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Summed feature 3 consists of C16:1ω7c and/or C16:1ω6c, indicating a combination of fatty acids that cannot be individually differentiated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUMMED FEATURE 8&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Summed feature 8 comprises a mixture including C18:1ω7c and/or C18:1ω6c, forming part of the combined fatty acid features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN BIT-26T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain BIT-26T is a Gram-stain-negative, facultatively anaerobic, rod-shaped bacterium with notable physiological and biochemical characteristics isolating it as a novel species within the genus Mixta."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strain BIT-26T is the bacterium under investigation, marked as a novel species in the genus Mixta."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA, PANTOAEA, AND TATUMELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwinia, Pantoaea, and Tatumella are genera related to Mixta, showing genome similarity percentages with strain BIT-26T."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRNASCAN-SE VERSION 1.3.1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"tRNAscan-SE version 1.3.1 is a software tool used for identifying tRNA genes in the genome sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENOME-TO-GENOME DISTANCE CALCULATOR (GGDC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The GGDC is a web server tool used for conducting in silico DNA-DNA hybridization tests to measure genome similarity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EZBIOCLOUD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EzBioCloud is a comprehensive database containing taxonomic information of 16S rRNA gene sequences and whole-genome assemblies, essential for microbial taxonomy and phylogeny."&lt;SEP&gt;"EzBioCloud is an online platform used for Average Nucleotide Identity (ANI) calculations to assess genomic similarities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA GAVINIAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mixta gaviniae is one of the species showing the highest genomic similarity to strain BIT-26T."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANTOEA EURINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pantoea eurina is a type species of the genus Pantoea, showing genomic distinction from strain BIT-26T."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TATUMELLA CITREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tatumella citrea is a type species of the genus Tatumella, used in comparison to assess the novelty of strain BIT-26T."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G+C CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G+C content refers to the percentage of guanine and cytosine nucleotides in the DNA, used to characterize the strain BIT-26T genome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBIC GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobic growth represents the ability of the isolate to grow without oxygen, tested in an anaerobic atmosphere."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL MOTILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell motility is evaluated by observing the spread of bacterial growth, indicating active movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEM (TRANSMISSION ELECTRON MICROSCOPY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TEM is a technology used to visualize flagella and other cellular details at high magnification in bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH TEMPERATURE RANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The growth temperature range is tested to determine optimal and range conditions for the isolate's development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PH VALUE RANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pH range tested defines the acidity or basicity conditions under which the bacterial isolate can thrive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA TENEBRIONIS SP. NOV.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mixta tenebrionis is a newly proposed species within the genus Mixta, distinguished by its phenotypic characteristics and identified from phylogenetic and chemotaxonomic analyses."</data>
