      <data key="d2">chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROTARY EVAPORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technique used to concentrate solutions by removing solvent through evaporation, applied in the polymer extraction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rotary Evaporation is a technique used to concentrate residual polymers from frass by removing solvents."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DARK INCUBATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm groups are incubated in the dark to control environmental variables affecting their growth and plastic consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMIDITY CONDITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Set at 80 ± 4.9% during incubation of mealworms to maintain a specific environmental condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE CONDITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maintained at 26.5 ± 1°C during mealworm incubation for stability in experimental conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGILENT PL - GPC220&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agilent PL - GPC220 is used for gel permeation chromatography, with a column and specific temperature and concentration settings, for analyzing materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAVIMETRIC ANALYZER (STA449C)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The STA449C is a thermogravimetric analyzer used for the thermal characterization of materials, specifically frass from mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BETA DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beta Diversity refers to the variety of species between different habitats or environments, indicating the environmental impact of diet changes on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beta diversity assesses the change in microbial communities between different environments or conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beta diversity measures the change in species composition between different ecosystems, contributing to an understanding of community differentiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FT-IR SPECTROMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The FT-IR Spectrometer is used to detect functional groups in both frass and plastic samples through spectral analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTASSIUM BROMIDE (KBR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KBr is used as a medium in FT-IR spectroscopy to obtain background spectra prior to analyzing samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium bromide is a salt used to create homogeneous powders for spectroscopic analysis, specifically within FTIR scanning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Used to prepare frass samples for FTIR scanning and analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potassium bromide is used to create homogeneous powders for FTIR scanning and analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABI GENEAMP® 9700 PCR SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ABI GeneAmp® 9700 PCR System is employed to amplify the V4 region of the 16S rRNA gene for analyzing gut microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ION SS XL SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ion SS XL System is used for sequencing the 16S rRNA gene amplicons to analyze the gut microbiome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTADAPT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cutadapt is a software tool used for trimming sequences, including removing barcodes and primers from raw reads."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UCHIME ALGORITHM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The UCHIME Algorithm is used to detect and remove chimeric sequences during genetic analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVA DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The SILVA database is used for the taxonomic identification of microbial sequences based on OTU representative sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FT-IR ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FT-IR analysis is used to examine the functional groups present in the plastics and frass, indicating changes due to biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-O stretch is another functional group appearing in the frass, signaling chemical changes in the polymer structure during biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TG ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TG analysis stands for thermogravimetric analysis, used to measure the weight loss and thermal decomposition of plastics and frass produced by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOGENIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathogenic describes organisms, like some strains of Spiroplasma, that can cause disease, although in the mealworm context, these bacteria are not harmful."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56</data>
