    <node id="&quot;CRONOBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Gram-negative bacterial genus found to be significantly over-represented in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter belongs to the family Enterobacteriaceae, identified in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a Gram-negative bacterium known to form biofilms on plastic, with potential enzymatic pathways for plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a bacterial genus found in the gut microbiota of polystyrene-fed Alphitobius diaperinus and associated with plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter is a genus of bacteria identified as significantly more abundant in polystyrene samples, potentially associated with plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter, a genus of bacteria in Gammaproteobacteria, appeared with notable differential abundance in PS samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
