      <data key="d2">chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRANDON ET AL. (2018A)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A study referenced for comparison with current experimental results concerning insect diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL. (2021)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STUDY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A previous work that analyzed plastic degradation over a single time period, serving as a point of reference for the current study."&lt;SEP&gt;"A study used as a comparison point for evaluating current experimental findings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cations are positively charged ions, including Mg²⁺, Na⁺, and K⁺, observed in the study in relation to insect diets and metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cations such as potassium, sodium, magnesium, and calcium are analyzed in the context of biochemical processes in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MG²⁺&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magnesium is an essential mineral involved in several biochemical activities, notably in cellular energy production processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOCHONDRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CELLULAR COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitochondria are energy-producing organelles that act as major intracellular Mg²⁺ reservoirs and are involved in energy metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;V-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"V-ATPase is an enzyme that plays a dominant role in osmoregulation and excretion in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NA⁺/K⁺-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase is an enzyme involved in osmoregulation and is stimulated synergistically by NH₄⁺ and K⁺ for ammonia transport."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMO-GRAVIMETRIC ANALYSIS (TGA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermo-gravimetric analysis is a process used to evaluate the presence of PS in insect frass through heating under a nitrogen atmosphere."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIET 1, 2, 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Different diets fed to insects containing varying ratios of Bran and PS to study their impacts on metabolite concentration in insect frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NA⁺&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium is a mineral important for osmoregulation and excretion in insects, playing a role in cellular functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K⁺&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potassium is a mineral that, along with sodium, contributes to osmoregulation and cellular functions in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NH₄⁺&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ammonium is a compound involved in the transport of ammonia from hemolymph to cytoplasm in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy metabolism refers to the biochemical processes that produce energy in cells, influenced by Mg²⁺ and mitochondrial activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRON TRANSPORT CHAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The electron transport chain is a series of reactions that produce ATP in mitochondria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADP/ATP TRANSLOCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ADP/ATP translocation is the process of exchanging ADP and ATP across mitochondrial membranes, crucial for cellular energy management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER (\(H_2O\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A ubiquitous chemical substance used in one of the diets to potentially influence the degradation of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\(^1H\) NMR (\(^1\) HYDROGEN NMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nuclear magnetic resonance technique used to observe the hydration, chemical nature, and transformations of hydrogen atoms in molecules, revealing PS-derived oligomers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL SHIFTS (\(\DELTA\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reference marks in NMR spectra indicating the environment of hydrogen atoms in the molecular structure, identifying PS oligomers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS OLIGOMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLYMER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS oligomers are smaller polymer chains derived from polystyrene, observed in the frass resulting from the biodegradation process in different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short chains or fragments of polystyrene formed during its degradation process, identified by \(^1H\) NMR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AEROBIC MICROBIAL STRAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial species that require oxygen to metabolize and potentially contribute to the degradation of PS in the insect gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADATION TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The specific temperature range at which polystyrene undergoes thermal breakdown, differing in various experimental conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DTGA PEAKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peaks derived from the derivative of thermogravimetric analysis plots, showing transitions and thermal stability of substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE OF TRANSITION (T\(_{\TEXT{TRANSITION}}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The specific temperature at which a material undergoes a phase change, such as degradation or melting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELTING POINT (T\(_{\TEXT{M}}\))&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The temperature at which a solid becomes a liquid, used to describe the melting behavior of polystyrene and its blends."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNICATION BETWEEN DIETS AND DECOMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The interaction between different diets and their influence on the degradation of polystyrene in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERS LIKE POLY(A-METHYL STYRENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLYMER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other polymers similar to polystyrene, observed for comparison in their thermal properties during degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS (Polystyrene) depolymerization involves breaking down polystyrene into its monomers, a process influenced by gut microbes in T. molitor and Z. atratus."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS depolymerization refers to the breakdown of polystyrene into smaller molecules, which in this study is linked to biodegradation and reduction in molecular weight of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breakdown of PS polymer chains into smaller molecules during mealworm digestion, tracked by GPC analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMS (Tetramethylsilane) is used as a reference standard in NMR spectroscopy for chemical shift calibration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION MECHANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation mechanisms refer to biological processes that result in the breakdown of organic substances, such as polymers, by microorganisms or other biological entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the enzyme and microbiome-related pathways utilized by mealworms to degrade plastics in their gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER FRAGMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer fragmentation is the process of breaking down polymers into smaller parts, a phenomenon observed in biodegradation studies regarding PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AROMATIC PROTONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aromatic protons are hydrogen atoms attached to aromatic systems, used in NMR to identify chemical structures in PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL SHIFTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical shifts are variations in the NMR frequency of a nucleus influenced by its environment, used to interpret molecular structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical shifts observed in NMR spectra denote structural changes in biodegraded polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APOPTOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apoptosis, or programmed cell death, is influenced in mealworms as they biodegrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATION CONCENTRATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cation concentrations refer to levels of ions like potassium, sodium, magnesium, and calcium in mealworms, impacting biochemical processes during polystyrene biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLULAR ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellular activity refers to physiological changes at the cellular level in mealworms during polystyrene biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANALYTICAL CHEMISTS (AOAC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Association of Analytical Chemists (AOAC) provides official methods of analysis, which may have relevance to the methodologies used in biodegradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENRICHMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enrichment refers to the process of enhancing the microbial community to increase the biodegradation of polystyrene in experimental settings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL MASKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disposable surgical masks made of polypropylene material used as experimental feedstock for larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical masks are made of polypropylene, composed of an outer, middle, and inner layer, and widely used during the COVID-19 pandemic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical masks are used as dietary components influencing the gut microbiome of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOPLASTIC STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermoplastic structures in polypropylene vary among mask layers, affecting their biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE LAYER (MELT-BLOWN FILTER)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The middle layer of surgical masks, composed of a melt-blown filter, is specifically analyzed for its biodegradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUTER LAYER (NON-WOVEN FABRIC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The outer layer of surgical masks, typically colored and non-woven, is a different structure for biodegradation analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INNER LAYER (FIBER MATERIAL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The inner layer of surgical masks, often made of non-woven fiber, presents a distinct structure in biodegradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITS GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ITS genes are sequences used to identify and study fungal communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PP (polypropylene) plastic is a type of plastic material used in masks, biodegradable by certain microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WUXI INSECTS BREEDING PLANT, JIANGSU, CHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Location where yellow mealworm larvae were sourced."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL WHEAT BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natural wheat bran is used as a control feedstock for larvae in plastic consumption experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL SURVIVAL RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the percentage of larvae alive at the end of an experimental period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The survival rate of T. molitor larvae is an important metric in the study to evaluate the adverse effects of consuming microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELT BLOWN FILTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Melt blown filtration is a type of nonwoven material with a compact structure, used in mask middle layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATR-FTIR (ATTENUATED TOTAL REFLECTION-FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ATR-FTIR is employed to characterize the depolymerization and degradation of residual polymers in mask-fed larval frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DSC-TGA (DIFFERENTIAL SCANNING CALORIMETRY AND THERMOGRAVIMETRIC ANALYSIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DSC-TGA analyses are conducted to study thermal properties and degradation behavior of polymers in mask-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONDUCTIVE ADHESIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conductive adhesive is a material used to prepare frass samples for SEM analysis to increase electrical conductivity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE LAYER (FILTER LAYER)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Middle layer of masks, made of melt-blown material, showing higher consumption rates by larvae due to its physical compactness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUTER AND INNER LAYERS (NONWOVEN FABRIC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Outer and inner layers of masks are made from nonwoven fabric, less consumed by larvae compared to the middle layer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
