      <data key="d1">"A bacterium known for its ability to degrade low-density polyethylene, contributing to biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium capable of deteriorating pretreated linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium noted for participating in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium species to which strain SCGB1 belongs, and it is characterized by its ability to degrade plastics such as polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium with the potential to biodegrade low-density polyethylene thermoplastic substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIAN MEAL MOTH (PLODIA INTERPUNCTELLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Indian meal moth is involved in polyethylene degradation and is a species of interest for plastic biodegradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOCHONDRIAL CYTOCHROME OXIDASE (MTCOI) GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
