    <node id="&quot;LARVAL STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Larval Stage is the developmental phase where waxworms primarily consume their diet, crucial for studying feeding behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPAL STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Pupal Stage refers to the phase following the larval stage in waxworms, during which development into moths occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT MOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adult Moth is the final life stage in waxworms' development, used to calculate longevity after death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVABILITY RATE&quot;">
