    <node id="&quot;HDPE MP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HDPE microplastics are high-density polyethylene particles studied for their degradation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE MP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPE microplastics are low-density polyethylene particles that are more efficiently degraded than HDPE by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M_N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M_n refers to the number average molecular weight, indicating the average size of polymer chains in a sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"M_n represents number-average molecular weight, a measure analyzed in the context of microplastics degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M_W&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M_w denotes weight-average molecular weight, another measure used to assess changes post-degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"M_w refers to the weight average molecular weight, showing how the distribution of molecules by weight changes during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45</data>
    </node>
