      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GPC analysis is used to evaluate the depolymerization and degradation of polystyrene materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIEVE MAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stainless-steel sieve mat divides the incubator into two floors, facilitating the separation of eggs and the growth of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR (NUCLEAR MAGNETIC RESONANCE) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR spectroscopy is used to analyze chemical shifts and modifications in egested PS associated with mealworm digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR (FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED) SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR spectroscopy is utilized to confirm chemical modifications and detect functional groups present in PS after mealworm digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEARSON CORRELATION TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOMETRIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical method used to assess the linear relationship between mealworm survival rates, PS consumption, and other variables."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTIAL CORRELATION TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOMETRIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical tool to evaluate the independent associations between variables, adjusted for other variables."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REDUNDANCY ANALYSIS (RDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RDA is a method to analyze the relationships between survival rate, PS consumption, and several environmental factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"RDA is a statistical method used to determine the variation in PS consumption related to various factors like density."&lt;SEP&gt;"RDA is an analytical method used in the study to verify the effective biodegradation of aged microplastics by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"RDA is used to identify the relationship between aging indexes and microbial communities during microplastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redundancy analysis (RDA) is a statistical method used to analyze ecological and environmental data, including the relationships between microbial communities and environmental variables."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3</data>
    </node>
