      <data key="d1">"Whey is a conventional type of feed that, when used for Tenebrio molitor, results in lower larval mortality but slower development cycle rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whey is a type of feed used in the study, producing a higher content of fatty acids in mealworm larvae compared to other feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whey is another feed type for mealworm larvae, providing distinct fatty acid proportions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whey, a byproduct of cheese production, is used as a dietary supplement for larvae in rearing experiments."</data>
