      <data key="d1">"Potatoes are used as a feed that resulted in the lowest mortality among mealworms in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes are used as a feed type for mealworm larvae, yielding differing fatty acid profiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes are used as feed, specifically noted for a higher proportion of C20 acid compared to polystyrene and whey."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes are used as one of the feed types administered to larvae in feeding experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Potatoes were used as feed in the study, resulting in specific changes in the fatty acid composition in mealworm larvae."</data>
