    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAT-AND-BONE MEAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Meat-and-bone meal is an animal byproduct included in larval feed to ensure adequate protein intake."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WARE POTATOES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ware potatoes are used as a feed source in mealworm diets, noted for causing the lowest mortality rate among the groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ware potatoes are used as feed, impacting the nutritional profile of larvae in the study, particularly in protein and fat content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ware potatoes serve as a representative of the carbohydrate diet in the experiment, contributing energy and minimal protein."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ware potatoes, used as feed in the experiment, had lower mortality rates compared to certain other feeds but did not accelerate development as effectively as wheat bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRIED WHEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dried Whey is one of the feed types analyzed for its fatty acid content, showing higher proportions for certain monoenoic fatty acids compared to other feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried Whey is used as a feed component and its fatty acid content is measured in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is a dairy by-product used as a feed source in mealworm diets, offering moderate nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is used as a feed in the experiment, contributing to specific crude protein and fat content values in larvae and excrement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey is used as a representative of the protein diet in the experiment, offering high energy content and significant protein value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dried whey was used as feed in the experiment, and its effects on mortality were observed, including an error in week five which influenced the results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SELENIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
