      <data key="d2">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIST17 DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOURCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NIST17 database is used to identify compounds based on chromatographic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAJORBIO BIO-PHARM TECHNOLOGY CO., LTD.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A company located in Shanghai, China, responsible for sequencing the V3-V4 region of the 16S rRNA gene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPSS 20.0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Statistical software used for performing ANOVAs and other statistical analyses in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATISTICAL ANOVAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ANOVAs are statistical methods used to analyze variance among different groups in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL MICROORGANISMS OF SUPERWORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These microorganisms are able to degrade PS into low-molecular-weight substances, indicating their significant capability in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;¹H-NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proton Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (¹H-NMR) helps detect new chemical peaks in frass from larvae fed on PS only, demonstrating specific depolymerization patterns and chemical changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O, C=O, R-OH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical functional groups identified in FTIR analysis which indicate oxidation and depolymerization processes during the degradation of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHA DIVERSITY ESTIMATORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indexes like Shannon and Simpson used to gauge community diversity within the gut microbiome during the polystyrene degradation study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACE AND CHAO ESTIMATORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Statistical tools used to measure the taxonomic richness of gut bacterial communities involved in the degradation of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T. CASTANEUM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T. castaneum larvae are insects studied for their gut microbiome in relation to PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. castaneum larvae are one of the species being studied, and their gut microbiome was analyzed to understand its role in polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACE INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An estimator of species richness that calculates based on abundant and rare OTUs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ace index estimates species richness in a community, highlighting the abundance of rare species in the microbiome samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAO INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical index that estimates species richness within yellow mealworm fungal communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chao index is used to calculate species richness, focusing on accounting for unseen species within the microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coverage measures the extent to which a sample represents the true diversity of a community, emphasizing the completeness of microbial sampling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WANG ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wang et al. conducted a study on the gut microbiome of plastic- and bran-fed T. castaneum larvae, focusing on the association with PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tmol, referred to as yellow mealworm, is a species involved in gut microbiome studies for PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GMEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gmel, referred to as greater wax moth, is a species involved in gut microbiome studies for PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZATR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zatr, or superworm, is a species involved in gut microbiome studies for PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLIC ESTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylic Esters are represented as metabolic intermediates in the degradation of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phenol is a toxic compound detected in PS samples but not in the gut and frass of larvae, suggesting degradation by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPTANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heptane is a potentially dangerous compound detected in PS samples, potentially not toxic in insect guts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. DAVIDIS LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P. davidis larvae are insects studied for their PS-degrading gut microbial community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT FLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut flora refers to the complex community of microorganisms that live in the digestive tracts of insects, aiding in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2-PROPENOIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2-propenoic acid is a metabolic intermediate identified in the gut of larvae during PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENZENEPROPANOIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benzenepropanoic acid is one of the metabolic byproducts found in the larvae's gut related to PS metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEHENIC ALCOHOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Behenic alcohol is identified as one of the metabolic intermediates in the biodegradation of PS in larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYME SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The enzyme system in insect larvae contributes to the biodegradation process of plastic, along with gut microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BETA ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beta analysis is a statistical method used to compare microbial community structures in insect guts over varied PS feeding times."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL AND ENZYMATIC DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process involves using microbes and enzymes to break down synthetic plastics, a critical step in reducing pollution and managing waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRICHODERMA HAMATUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fungus isolated from plastic-polluted environments, capable of attacking synthetic polymer films, aiding in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIMONY TRIOXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A compound used as a flame retardant in plastics, complicating the biodegradation of these materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antimony trioxide is commonly used as a flame retardant synergist in combination with other compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56425bd62513be46b9165bfd84f0dd0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENRICHMENT FROM GUT MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enrichment from gut microbiome refers to the use of robust communities of gut microorganisms to enhance or study the degradation of substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE-POLYSTYRENE FOAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste-polystyrene foams refer to discarded foam materials made of polystyrene, often targeted for recycling or biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGNETIC CARBON MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magnetic carbon material derived from waste-polystyrene foams is investigated for its applications in adsorption and redox supercapacitors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNGAL ISOLATES&quot;">
