    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALACHITE GREEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malachite Green is a chemical compound used in dyes and antimicrobials, with a styrene core structure, showing potential degradation by Kocuria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malachite green is a chemical dye with a styrene core structure, used as a textile dye and antimicrobial agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malachite green is a synthetic dye used in various industrial applications, subject to biodegradation by certain microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOCURIA ROSEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kocuria rosea is a microorganism capable of degrading malachite green, a compound with a styrene core structure, potentially indicative of its ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kocuria rosea is a species of Kocuria bacteria known to degrade malachite green, suggesting a potential for degrading similar compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8</data>
