    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOEOPHYLLUM TRABEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gloeophyllum trabeum is a wood-rotting fungus that has the capability to degrade polystyrene sulfonate through hydroquinone-driven Fenton chemistry."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLUS ORYZAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus oryzae is a fungus from which a biodegradable plastic-degrading enzyme has been purified and characterized."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AZOTOBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Azotobacter is a genus of bacteria, known for their ability to fix nitrogen and degrade various compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Azotobacter is a genus of nitrogen-fixing bacteria, some species of which are found in the gut of various insect species involved in nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </node>
