      <data key="d2">chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPER WORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Super worm, often associated with Zophobas morio, is another larval form studied for its potential in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOBID BEETLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anobid beetles are a group of beetles that host symbiotic organisms assisting in sterol biosynthesis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICE PLANTHOPPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rice planthoppers are insect pests of rice that harbor symbiotic organisms which assist in sterol biosynthesis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDGIT&quot;">
