      <data key="d1">"PP (polypropylene) biodegradation is a complex process carried out by specific larvae and their gut microbes, leading to the reduction in molecular weight of PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP biodegradation refers to the degradation of polypropylene polymers into simpler substances by microorganisms, involving processes like depolymerization and surface hydrophobicity reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spiroplasma is a dominant genus specifically associated with the degradation of PP in yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC POLYMER DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ascomycota is involved in degrading various polymers in fungal communities of plastics-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
