    <node id="&quot;AEROBIC CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aerobic conditions are environments with the presence of oxygen, where some bacterial strains can also show degradation activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to an environment where oxygen is present, allowing aerobic organisms or activities to metabolize substrates like polystyrene effectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to environments where oxygen is present and are typically where traditional plastic-degrading microorganisms have been studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to environments with oxygen, influencing different microbial metabolisms compared to anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to environments with the presence of oxygen, under which certain bacterial strains show different biodegradation capabilities of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental conditions with oxygen presence, in which some microbes, including E. hormaechei LG3, degrade plastic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
