    <node id="&quot;SALMON (V.1.9.0)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Salmon is a software tool used for quantifying transcript expression levels from RNA-seq data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAPHPAD PRISM 9&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GraphPad Prism 9 is a software application used for statistical analysis and graphing of experimental data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain SCGB1 is a bacterium belonging to the same species as Bacillus amyloliquefaciens, known for degrading both polyethylene (PE) and PS, but exhibiting effectiveness only under aerobic conditions in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT OF LATE-INSTAR PS-FED LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut of late-instar PS-fed larvae serves as an ecological niche where microorganisms like strain LG3 are enriched for their ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FMM MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FMM Medium is a growth medium used in the experiments to cultivate microorganisms like strains LG3 and SCGB1 for polystyrene degradation analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"FMM Medium is a specific nutrient medium used to culture microorganisms in the presence of PS films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAKING INCUBATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A shaking incubator is an apparatus used to maintain aerobic conditions by agitating samples at a set speed, crucial for microbial cultures like those studied in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATIONARY INCUBATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stationary incubator is used to maintain samples under specific conditions without agitation, facilitating experiments under anaerobic conditions for PS-degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. HORMAECHEI LG3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated for its high anaerobic PS-degrading activity, showcasing efficiency under both anaerobic and aerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. hormaechei LG3 is a strain observed to form biofilms and degrade PS films under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another PS-degrading bacterium with distinct metabolic characteristics, compared with LG3."&lt;SEP&gt;"B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a bacterial strain that shows specific metabolic activity differences compared to Enterobacter strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a strain that causes changes in PS film weight and has a distinct growth pattern compared to strain LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT CHANGE ON AGAR PLATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight Change on Agar Plate indicates changes in the weight of PS films after exposure to microbial strains such as E. hormaechei LG3 or B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LG3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LG3 is a bacterium that can degrade PS anaerobically, playing a role in maintaining cell growth, adhesion ability, and viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"LG3 is a strain of Enterobacter hormaechei known for its ability to oxidize and depolymerize polystyrene (PS) under anaerobic and aerobic conditions. It effectively forms biofilms and degrades various PS materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SCGB1 is a strain of Bacillus amyloliquefaciens used in comparative experiments for PS biodegradation. It is less effective than LG3 under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FE-SEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FE-SEM is a technique used for imaging structures like bacterial cells in experiments at the microscopic level."&lt;SEP&gt;"FE-SEM is a technology used for visualizing interactions between bacteria and polystyrene (PS). It helps in observing changes in microsphere beads when incubated with bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEROXIDASE (EFEB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peroxidase (efeB) is an enzyme that shows increased expression in strain LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS under anaerobic conditions, particularly reactive to aryl alcohol compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROLASE (UBI GENES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrolase (ubi genes) is an enzyme that is upregulated in strain LG3 under anaerobic conditions, contributing to PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THIOL PEROXIDASE (PXC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thiol peroxidase (pxc) is a peroxidase family enzyme whose expression levels increase significantly in strain LG3 after Mi-PS treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIOFERRITIN COMIGRATORY PROTEIN (BCP) (GENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterioferritin comigratory protein (bcp) is part of the peroxidase family, with increased expression in strain LG3 following Mi-PS treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARYL ALCOHOL COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aryl alcohol compounds are chemical structures involved in the biodegradation process of polystyrene, specifically targeted by certain enzymes in strain LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDIZED PS (POLYSTYRENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidized PS refers to polystyrene that has undergone chemical modifications, such as oxidation, to facilitate its biodegradation by microorganisms like LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC PATHWAY ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic pathway enzymes are involved in the chemical reactions that take place during the degradation of polystyrene by strain LG3 under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSCRIPTOME SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transcriptome sequencing is a technique used to analyze RNA transcripts and identify the differentially expressed genes in LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS compared to maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WCA VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WCA values, or water contact angle values, are used to quantify the changes in surface properties of polystyrene films after bacterial exposure, indicating physical changes due to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALIPHATIC ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aliphatic alcohols are chemical compounds identified through SPME/GC-MS analysis as products of PS biodegradation by LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AROMATIC ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aromatic alcohols are another type of chemical compounds produced during the biodegradation of polystyrene by microorganisms, identifiable through chromatographic analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLAR PROTEIN-CODING GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagellar protein-coding genes, including ycgR, flgH, and flp, are downregulated in strain LG3 when metabolizing Mi-PS, affecting the bacterium's motility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID A SYNTHESIS PATHWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid A synthesis pathway involves enzymes that are upregulated in strain LG3 when exposed to Mi-PS, highlighting changes in lipid metabolism during PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCOLYTIC PATHWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The glycolytic pathway, a primary method of glucose metabolism, shows downregulation of its enzymes in strain LG3 when utilizing Mi-PS as a carbon source instead of maltose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPME/GC-MS ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPME/GC-MS analysis is a coupled technique used to identify volatile compounds like alcohols produced during PS biodegradation by strain LG3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPME/GC-MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SPME/GC-MS is a technique used for identifying hydroxyl compounds and analyzing chromatograms in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"SPME/GC-MS is a technology used to detect PS derivative molecules, aiding in the analysis of anaerobic biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solid Phase Microextraction combined with Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry, used to analyze volatile compounds during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYL COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxyl compounds are identified as degradation products through chemical analysis like SPME/GC-MS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALIPHATIC AND AROMATIC ALCOHOLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aliphatic and aromatic alcohols are degradation products observed during PS metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER LG3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter LG3 is a strain capable of degrading PS aerobically and anaerobically, possessing superior degradative enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SCGB1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter SCGB1 is a gut bacterium with reduced PS degradation activity under anaerobic conditions, producing distinct metabolites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SPP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter spp. are a genus of bacteria detected in mealworm guts, participating in nitrogen fixation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter spp. is a genus that plays a vital role in anaerobic PS biodegradation in various organisms, including insects and humans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxylase is another enzyme involved in the biodegradation of PS, facilitating the metabolism of compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHYL 2-HYDROXYBENZOATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methyl 2-hydroxybenzoate is identified as a secondary product formed by strain LG3 under anaerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOBUTYRIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isobutyric acid is a specific metabolite formed by strain SCGB1 during PS metabolism under aerobic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOVALERIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isovaleric acid is another specific metabolite produced by strain SCGB1 in the presence of oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUTYL RUBBER STOPPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Butyl rubber stopper is used to seal the FMM medium in experimental settings to maintain anaerobic conditions."</data>
