      <data key="d1">"Vinyl plastics, including PS, PE, PVC, PP, and SBR, are synthetic materials rich in carbon but deficient in nitrogen, posing nutritional challenges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACETYLENE REDUCTION ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bioassay used to estimate the nitrogen-fixing capacity of bacteria by measuring the conversion of acetylene to ethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method used to confirm the nitrogen-fixing ability of the mealworms by measuring the reduction of acetylene to ethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acetylene reduction assay is a laboratory technique used to measure the activity of nitrogenase by detecting the conversion of acetylene to ethylene, indicating nitrogen fixation activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acetylene reduction assay is a method used to measure nitrogenase activity as a proxy for nitrogen fixation in gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An experimental method used to measure the nitrogen-fixing activity of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN ISOTOPIC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen isotopic analysis is a method used to trace the assimilation of nitrogen by assessing the isotopic signatures in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIROCHAETA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spirochaeta is a genus of bacteria identified as potentially involved in nitrogen fixation within the insect gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREPONEMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treponema is a bacterial genus potentially involved with nitrogen fixation processes within insect hosts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEIJERINCKIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beijerinckia is a genus of bacteria isolated from the guts of nitrogen-fixing insects, known for its association with nitrogen fixation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beijerinckia is a genus of nitrogen-fixing bacteria found in association with various insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
