      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United Nations is an international organization involved in setting goals for the reduction of plastic waste worldwide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROIA GRISSELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achroia grissella, also known as the lesser wax moth, has been shown to depolymerize high-density polyethylene microplastics in a gut environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR OXIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme involved in the extracellular breakdown of polystyrene (PS) by gut microbes in Zophobas atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracellular oxidase is an enzyme produced by microbes within the gut of Zophobas atratus larvae, aiding in PS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UV RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"UV radiation contributes to the oxidative degradation of aged PE, making it more susceptible to further breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"UV radiation is an environmental factor that accelerates the aging process of plastics by altering their physicochemical characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ultraviolet radiation, which facilitates surface oxidation of aged polyethylene, making it more susceptible to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGING EFFECT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aging effect refers to the changes in MP physico-chemical properties due to environmental factors like UV radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REACTIVE OXYGEN SPECIES AND EXTRACELLULAR OXIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This reaction refers to the combined chemical processes that facilitate the degradation of plastics by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY–MASS SPECTROMETRY (GC-MS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC-MS is a method used to identify the biodegradation products of microplastics processed by insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL AGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental aging refers to the processes that alter the physicochemical properties of plastics, impacting their ability to be biodegraded."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRISTINE MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pristine MPs are microplastics in their original, unaltered form prior to undergoing environmental aging or biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pristine MPs are untreated microplastics with less consumption preference compared to aged MPs by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pristine MPs refer to microplastics in their original, unaltered state, used as a control in the study to compare against aged MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGED MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aged MPs are microplastics that have been exposed to environmental factors such as UV radiation, altering their properties and affecting degradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aged MPs are microplastics that have undergone specific transformations due to environmental aging processes affecting their biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aged MPs refers to microplastics that have undergone aging processes, affecting their physical properties and thus their degradation and consumption by organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIFIC SURFACE AREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific surface area refers to the total surface area per unit of mass, significant in the degradation efficiency of aged microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN-CONTAINING GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These groups are products of oxidation reactions on microplastic surfaces, contributing to alterations in degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation products are the resultant compounds identified after plastics are broken down by organisms like insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPOLYMERIZATION PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Depolymerization products are the result of breaking down polymers into monomers or smaller units, identified as a result of plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMO-NICOLET 6700 SERIES FTIR SPECTROMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The FTIR spectrometer is used for analyzing the main changes in functional groups of plastics after biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHENZHEN WEIIKE MENG TECH GROUP CO., LTD.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tech group involved in conducting microbial community analysis in the study, using DNA extraction and sequencing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREENGENES 16S RRNA DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A reference database used for analyzing and classifying sequences obtained from the gut microbiome analysis of T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALLADIUM COAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palladium coating is applied to the T. molitor larvae intestines to prepare them for SEM analysis, enhancing imaging accuracy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-PERFORMANCE SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPE (JSM-6490LV SEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A high-resolution microscope used for observing the structural changes in T. molitor larvae after experimentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE GASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethylene gases are used in the pretreatment and preservation of samples for microbial analysis or during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MN, MW, MZ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mn, Mw, and Mz denote number-average, weight-average, and size-average molecular weights respectively, used to characterize the properties of polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT CHANGE OF LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The weight change of T. molitor larvae is measured to assess the impact of different diets, including microplastics and bran, on their growth and health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Starvation group comprised larvae that were not provided any supplementary diet besides PS, leading to a lower survival rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"The starvation group serves as a control group that is not fed, used to compare the effects of different diets on larval growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BITE MARKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bite marks on microplastics are observed as evidence of T. molitor larvae ingestion and the physical degradation of the material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXIC ADDITIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toxic additives are harmful chemicals potentially found in microplastics that can negatively impact larval growth and health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRACANTANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-chain alkane (C40H82) observed in the biodegradation products of aged PE-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRATETRACONTANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-chain alkane (C44H90) present in the frass of pristine PE-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2-HYDROXYACETIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An oxygen-containing compound (C2H4O3) found in higher amounts in the byproducts of aged PE biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-METHYL-2-HEXANONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An oxygen-containing compound (C7H14O) found in the byproducts of aged PE biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1-(2-BUTOXYETHOXY)PROPAN-2-OL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An oxygen-containing compound (C9H20O3) found in the byproducts of aged PE biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2-HYDROXYPROPYL METHACRYLATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An oxygen-containing compound (C7H12O3) found in the byproducts of aged PE biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,3-DI-TERT-BUTYL-2,5-DIMETHYLBENZENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1,3-di-tert-butyl-2,5-dimethylbenzene is a normal antioxidant additive found in the frass of PS-fed larvae, used in plastic production."&lt;SEP&gt;"1,3-di-tert-butyl-2,5-dimethylbenzene is an antioxidant additive found in the frass of PS-fed larvae, indicating its use in plastic production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A compound (C16H26) found in the frass of PS-fed larvae, identifiable as a common antioxidant additive in plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN-CONTAINING COMPOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Compounds that include oxygen atoms, found in higher concentration in the biodegradation byproducts of aged polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen-containing compounds result from the oxidative degradation of aged PE, including substances like 2-hydroxyacetic acid and 5-methyl-2-hexanone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-N GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nitrogen-attached functional group in the biodegradation products of PS-fed larvae, indicating chemical changes in the polymer structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONJUGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical feature contributing to the shift in frequency observed in the biodegradation products, indicating interaction in the polymer structure between nitrogen and aromatic rings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC-MS (GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY-MASS SPECTROMETRY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An analytical method used to identify the degradation products of microplastics in the frass of Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEXATRIACONTANE (C36H74)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hexatriacontane is a long-chain alkane found in the frass of aged PE-fed larvae, indicating that it is a byproduct of PE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRACONTANE (C40H82)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tetracontane is a long-chain alkane similar to hexatriacontane, also found in the frass of aged PE-fed larvae as a degradation byproduct."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN ELEMENT (N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL ELEMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nitrogen element is involved in direct bonding with the benzene ring in the excrement of aged PS-fed larvae, causing frequency shifts due to conjugation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2-HYDROXYACETIC ACID (C2H4O3)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2-hydroxyacetic acid is one of the oxygen-containing compounds formed as a byproduct of aged PE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-METHYL-2-HEXANONE (C7H14O)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5-methyl-2-hexanone is one of the oxygen-containing compounds identified in the byproducts of aged PE degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1-(2-BUTOXYETHOXY)PROPAN-2-OL (C9H20O3)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1-(2-butoxyethoxy)propan-2-ol is an oxygen-containing compound found as a byproduct in the degradation of aged PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2-HYDROXYPROPYL METHACRYLATE (C7H12O3)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2-hydroxypropyl methacrylate is an oxygen-containing compound formed during the degradation of aged PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRATETRACONTANE (C44H90)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tetratetracontane is a longer chain alkane produced in the frass of pristine PE-fed larvae, indicating the degradation state of the polymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MPS (MICROPLASTICS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MPs are small plastic particles being studied for their biodegradation by larvae, focusing on changes due to aging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER CONTACT ANGLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water contact angle measures hydrophobicity, impacting microbial adhesion and growth on microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN FREE RADICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxygen free radicals are reactive species formed by the binding of oxygen to polymers during biodegradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANT ADDITIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antioxidant additives prevent oxidation in plastics and are detected in the frass of plastic-fed larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAE GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae growth is adversely affected by the consumption of microplastics, with observed changes in physiology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERWORMS (ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS) LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superworms (Zophobas atratus) larvae are species known for their ability to degrade plastics, including polystyrene, through gut microbial activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEFENSE RESPONSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Defense responses in organisms like earthworms are protective mechanisms activated to deal with stressors such as exposure to microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGING INDEXES OF MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aging indexes of microplastics refer to measurements that assess the changes in microplastic properties due to environmental exposure over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER XYLOSOXIDANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achromobacter xylosoxidans is a microorganism that colonizes high-density polyethylene, playing a role in its biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE (LOW DENSITY POLYETHYLENE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPE is a type of plastic that undergoes biodegradation by certain bacteria and fungi."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PBAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PBAT is a type of biodegradable plastic that affects bacterial communities when incubated with soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lead is a heavy metal that can be adsorbed and desorbed by microplastics, playing a significant role in environmental pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CADMIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A heavy metal studied alongside microplastics to assess its toxicity in zebrafish larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A heavy metal which, in conjunction with polystyrene microplastics, affects metabolic regulation and neutrophil expression in zebrafish larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cadmium is a toxic metal that interacts with microplastics, influencing their adsorption and desorption behavior in the gastrointestinal environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FT-IR (FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FT-IR is a technique used to characterize plastics and study their biodegradation by insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATR-FT-IR (ATTENUATED TOTAL REFLECTION FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ATR-FT-IR is a variation of FT-IR, providing detailed insights into the biodegradation processes of insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVOFLOXACIN HYDROCHLORIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Levofloxacin hydrochloride is an antibiotic whose adsorption by microplastics is studied in different functional group conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Levofloxacin hydrochloride is an antibiotic whose adsorption by microplastics is studied in terms of oxygen functional groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSCRIPTOMIC RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transcriptomic response refers to the changes in gene expression of mealworms when fed with plastics, affecting their growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
    </node>
