      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth of bacteria is measured in different media to understand their degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADATION OF POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degradation of polystyrene is studied using isolated microorganisms from mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZEISS SCOPE. A1, AXIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zeiss Scope. A1, AXIO are types of microscopes used to observe bacterial attachment on surfaces and degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT CHANGE OF MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The study measures weight change in mealworms to determine the impact of an EPS-only diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL ATTACHMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process by which bacteria attach themselves to surfaces such as polystyrene films, observed using microscopes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABSORBANCE AT 600 NM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common method to gauge microbial culture density by measuring light absorbance at 600 nm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. SEPTICUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter septicus is a bacterial strain that showed typical bacterial growth except for strains MA21, MA62, and MA65, which experienced autoaggregation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENT MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrient media like LB and TYE were used to observe bacterial growth. TYE is a sodium chloride-free version of LB."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AEROMONAS HYDROPHILA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aeromonas hydrophila is a bacterial strain identified in mealworms, with 7 identified strains and 1 strain tested for EPS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SOLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter soli is a strain identified from the digestive tracts of mealworms, with one strain tested for EPS degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA GRIMMONTII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Klebsiella grimmontii is identified as a single strain in mealworms, one of which was used in an EPS degradation test."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOAGGREGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Autoaggregation in the context refers to the clumping together of A. septicus strains, affecting growth measurement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Autoaggregation refers to the ability of bacteria to aggregate with each other, promoting surface adhesion and stability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOUBLING TIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doubling time is a measure of how quickly a bacterial population doubles, used to evaluate growth under different conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doubling time is the period it takes for a population of cells to double in number, used here to compare the growth rates of different bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLASTN HOMOLOGY SEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BLASTN Homology Search is a method for finding regions of similarity between nucleotide sequences, used to identify bacterial strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. NITROREDUCENS MA77&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterium involved in breaking down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterium sensitive to salt, with a documented doubling time in LB medium during its exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 is capable of adhering to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 is identified for its ability to break down polystyrene in specific salt conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 plays a significant role in polystyrene degradation by attacking surface structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. nitroreducens MA77 was observed to degrade polystyrene particles effectively, reducing their number and altering their structural features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. TUMEFACIENS MA92&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. tumefaciens MA92 contributes to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterium with a doubling time of 113.4 minutes in LB medium during the exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 is a strain that can adhere to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 is one of the bacterial strains involved in the polystyrene degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92 was involved in adhesion experiments with polystyrene, affecting its surface structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. tumefaciens MA92, identified as polystyrene-degrading bacteria from various insect intestines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. MULTIRESINIVORANS MA11&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P. multiresinivorans MA11 adheres well to polystyrene film, indicating potential in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 demonstrated high adhesion to polystyrene and affected the integrity of polystyrene particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterial strain isolated for its abilities to decompose polystyrene in enriched culture conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterium involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is a bacterium with specific growth characteristics in comparison to other strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. multiresinivorans MA11 is capable of creating micro-cracks on polystyrene and shows potential for degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K. GRIMMONTII MA76&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"K. grimmontii MA76 is a bacterial strain examined for its growth and potential polystyrene degradability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P. PLECOGLOSSICIDA MA93&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P. plecoglossicida MA93 displayed a high degree of adhesion to polystyrene and contributed to its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 displays potential in degrading polystyrene, part of the evaluated strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is a bacterium with a specific doubling time in LB medium and its growth characteristics are studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is isolated for its ability to grow on polyethylene and degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 is known to adhere to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"P. plecoglossicida MA93 plays a role in degrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE DEGRADABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene degradability refers to the ability of certain bacteria to break down polystyrene, a polymer, analyzed through phylogenetic studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPONENTIAL PHASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The exponential phase is a stage of bacterial growth where cells divide at a consistent and rapid rate, useful for determining growth characteristics of strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOOTSTRAP ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bootstrap analysis is a statistical method used to estimate the reliability of phylogenetic trees, involved in evaluating the confidence of branches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGA4 SOFTWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MEGA4 software is a computational tool used for conducting phylogenetic and statistical analyses on genetic sequence data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL DENSITY (ABS600)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell density measured at Abs600 refers to the optical density of a bacterial culture at a wavelength of 600 nm, indicative of the cell population size."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. COLI MA4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E. coli MA4 is a strain of E. coli used in the study as part of polystyrene degradation evaluation. It did not show significant growth on polystyrene, indicating limited use of polystyrene as a nutrient."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli MA4 is a strain of bacteria evaluated for its ability to adhere to polystyrene film, though it showed less adhesion, similar to the negative control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. HYDROPHILA MA32&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. hydrophila MA32 is a bacterial strain observed for adhesion to polystyrene film, demonstrating less adhesion like the negative control E. coli."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. hydrophila MA32 is part of the polystyrene-degrading bacterial strains explored in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. hydrophila MA32 shows no activity in degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. hydrophila MA32, similar to E. coli MA4, showed inadequate growth on polystyrene, implying its limited degradation capability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Y. REGENSBURGEI MA19&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Y. regensburgei MA19 exhibited the capability to decrease the size, count, and edge sharpness of polystyrene particles, indicating its degradation capability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Y. regensburgei MA19 is a bacterium identified for its polystyrene degrading capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Y. regensburgei MA19 is a bacterium that contributes to the breakdown of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Y. regensburgei MA19 is a strain capable of adhering to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Y. regensburgei MA19 produces micro-cracks on polystyrene and is part of the study on polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K. GRIMONTII MA76&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"K. grimontii MA76 actively participated in reducing the integrity of polystyrene particles, showcasing its degradation potential."&lt;SEP&gt;"K. grimontii MA76 is a bacterial strain that can adhere to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"K. grimontii MA76 is a strain known for polystyrene degradation affected by salt conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"K. grimontii MA76 is effective in the degradation of polystyrene by affecting surface integrity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;S. MARCESCENS MA42&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"S. marcescens MA42 is a bacterial strain with good adhesion to polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 is a bacterium identified from mealworms, part of polystyrene degrading research."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 is identified as a bacterium that degrades polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 produces micro-cracks in polystyrene and contributes to its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"S. marcescens MA42 showed notable adherence to polystyrene and created micro-cracks on its surface."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. SEPTICUS MA21&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. septicus MA21 is a strain in the study showing a thick bacterial spot from the first day of culture on polystyrene, suggesting efficient degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is a strain of bacteria tested for polystyrene decomposition."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is involved in adhesion and degradation processes on polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is one of the strains capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA21 is one of the three strains that adhere to polystyrene film through autoaggregation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. SEPTICUS MA62&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. septicus MA62 also adheres to polystyrene film via autoaggregation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA62 is a strain in the study that showed a significant bacterial spot after four days when using polystyrene as a nutrient, indicating a stronger degradation ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA62 is another strain investigated for its polystyrene degradation abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA62 is another strain of A. septicus identified in polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA62 shows polystyrene degrading activity, participating in surface changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. SEPTICUS MA65&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. septicus MA65 adheres to polystyrene film with autoaggregation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA65 exhibits polystyrene degradation activity by destroying surface structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA65 is a strain involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA65 is one of the bacterial strains examined for decomposing polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. septicus MA65, similar to A. septicus MA21, demonstrated a strong ability to use polystyrene as a nutrient right from the first day."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICRO-SPRAYED POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Micro-sprayed polystyrene acts as a sole nutrient source to evaluate bacterial decomposition ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Micro-sprayed polystyrene is used as a method to evaluate bacterial degradation of small particles for faster biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL CELL ATTACHMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterial cell attachment to polystyrene film is the initial step in the biodegradation process, involving adhesion of bacterial cells to a surface."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADHESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adhesion is the process by which bacteria attach themselves to surfaces, such as polystyrene film, as a prerequisite for biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c1bb645805a7158e2e18e95313565f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPIC CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microscopic changes refer to alterations observed at a microscopic level on the surface of the polystyrene film due to bacterial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORROSION, HOLES, AND PITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Corrosion, holes, and pits refer to the structural damages observed on polystyrene surface after bacterial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. COLI ATCC 43895&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E. coli ATCC 43895 is a control strain used in experiments to compare the effects of other bacterial strains on polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E. COLI MA04&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E. coli MA04 is one of the strains tested for polystyrene degradation but shows no activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER SP. TM1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter sp. TM1 is isolated from the intestines of T. molitor, showing the ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AEROMONAS SP. TM1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aeromonas sp. TM1, found in the intestines of Z. morio, also presents polystyrene degradation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RHIZOBIUM RADIOBACTER (A. TUMEFACIENS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rhizobium radiobacter, now known as A. tumefaciens, is found in the insect gut, participating in polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGROBACTERIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agrobacterium sp. is found in the digestive tract of mealworms on a polystyrene diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f</data>
    </node>
