      <data key="d2">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAMMARUS DUEBENI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of freshwater amphipod that rapidly fragments polyethylene microplastics into various sizes, including nanoplastics within its digestive tracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammarus duebeni is an organism capable of rapidly fragmenting polyethylene (PE) microplastics (MPs) into smaller particles, including nanoparticles (NPs) in its digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gammarus duebeni, a freshwater amphipod, is known for rapidly fragmenting microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96</data>
    </node>
