    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLULAR LIPIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellular lipids are fats and fat-like substances within cells, studied for changes during the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cellular lipids are fats or fat-like substances found in cells, which can be altered during the biodegradation of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty molecules within cells that can be altered during the biodegradation process of materials like expanded polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN ALTERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in protein structures within cells, observed during the biodegradation of plastics by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein alteration refers to changes in protein structure or composition that can occur during processes like biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein alteration refers to changes in protein structures and functions observed during the biodegradation process of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAE FEEDING CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae feeding conditions encompass the environmental and dietary factors affecting larvae, which can influence their biodegradation activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYELEFIN MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyelefin microplastics are a type of microplastic originating from the breakdown of larger polyelefin plastic products, commonly found in personal-care products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOTOPE ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isotope analysis is a method used to study chemical elements' isotopic composition, which can help understand degradation processes or environmental exposures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTO-DEGRADATION PROCESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photo-degradation processes involve the breakdown of materials, like certain herbicides, through exposure to light."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN BLOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Human blood is a biological fluid in humans that can be contaminated by plastic particle pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC PARTICLE POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic particle pollution refers to the presence of microscopic plastic particles in the environment, potentially contaminating various ecosystems including human blood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrate is a chemical compound that promotes the transformation of sulfonamide antibiotics by peracetic acid and can form harmful disinfection byproducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SULFONAMIDE ANTIBIOTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sulfonamide antibiotics are antibacterial agents that can be transformed by peracetic acid, with potential formation of harmful disinfection byproducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REACTIVE NITROGEN SPECIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reactive nitrogen species are highly reactive molecules derived from nitrogen that contribute to chemical transformations and potential byproduct formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FENTON REACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fenton reactions are chemical processes involving iron and hydrogen peroxide that can be tuned by thiosulfate, influencing kinetic modeling and reaction mechanisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THIOSULFATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thiosulfate is a chemical compound that tunes the iron cycle in Fenton reactions, affecting the reaction kinetics and mechanisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERACETIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peracetic acid is a chemical compound used for disinfecting and known to transform sulfonamide antibiotics in the presence of nitrate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRON CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The iron cycle is a series of processes involving the oxidation and reduction of iron, influenced by compounds like thiosulfate in Fenton reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL PARTICLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil particles form a protective barrier around polystyrene microplastics, reducing their toxicity to soil-dwelling organisms like earthworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUB-MICRON MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sub-micron microplastics are a category of microplastics with sizes ranging from 1–20 μm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small microplastics range from 20–999 μm in size and have unique physicochemical properties that affect their environmental fate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INGESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ingestion is the biological process by which organisms, such as mealworms, consume substances like microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODY WEIGHT REDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body weight reduction is a physiological response indicative of malnutrition or stress, observed in mealworms exposed to PVC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSISTENT MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Persistent microplastics are small plastic fragments that resist degradation, causing long-term environmental issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental health focuses on the aspects of the natural and built environment that may affect human health, such as pollution from microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTICULATE ANTHROPOGENIC CONTAMINANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Particulate anthropogenic contaminants refer to small particles, such as microplastics, that originate from human activity and contaminate the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERRESTRIAL SNAILS (ACHATINA FULICA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species of snail that contributes to the biotransformation of plastic waste by fragmenting commercial PS foam into microplastics through digestive fragmentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT EARTHWORMS (EISENIA FETIDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A species of earthworm capable of breaking down bio-based polyactic acid microplastics into sub-micron particles within their digestive tracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES OF MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to the characteristics such as large specific surface area, tiny size, and strong adsorption capacities that influence the fate of microplastics in the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROPLASTIC-INDUCED STRESS RESPONSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The physiological adaptations seen in organisms exposed to microplastic contaminants, including the production of reactive oxygen species as a stress mechanism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LASER DIRECT INFRARED SPECTROMETRY (LDIR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to determine the presence and quantities of microplastics in the intestines of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDIR is used to identify residual microplastics in mealworm intestines with high precision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LASER LIGHT SCATTERING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A highly sensitive method used to explore residual plastic particles after the biodegradation process by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laser light scattering is a technique used to measure the size distribution of attached plastic particles based on polymer volume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental stress encompasses various adverse factors affecting organisms, such as food scarcity or toxic substances, which are studied under the DEB model."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental stress refers to changes in the environment that challenge the survival and metabolic processes of organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adverse effects on living organisms due to environmental pollutants such as microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURTH INSTAR MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A growth stage of mealworms, characterized by high feed consumption and sensitivity to environmental conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harm to cells and tissues caused by reactive oxygen species as a result of exposure to harmful substances like microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative damage in mealworms refers to the adverse effects caused by reactive oxygen species that were measured using various assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE, PS, AND PVC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE, PS, and PVC are polymers used as microplastics in the biodegradation experiments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,2,4-TRICHLOROBENZENE (TCB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A solvent used for extracting PE during molecular weight analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"TCB is the extraction solvent used for isolating PE in the biodegradation analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4TH-INSTAR MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to a specific growth stage of mealworms characterized by rapid development and high feedstock consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MW, MN, MZ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to different measures of polymer size and distribution used to assess biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms that were fed with polyethylene (PE) microplastics showed specific survival rates and growth patterns during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-fed mealworms are mealworms that consume polyethylene (PE) microplastics, demonstrating certain survival and growth patterns."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms that were fed with polystyrene (PS) microplastics displayed distinct survival rates and changes in body weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS-fed mealworms are mealworms that consume polystyrene (PS) microplastics, showing similar survival and growth patterns to PE-fed mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms that were fed with polyvinyl chloride (PVC) microplastics had unique survival and growth characteristics observed during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC-fed mealworms are mealworms that ingest polyvinyl chloride (PVC) microplastics, showing inhibited growth and survival due to toxic byproducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC PERFORMANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic performance in mealworms refers to the activity level of superoxide dismutase (SOD) related to oxidative stress resistance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALVERN MASTERSIZER 3000&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malvern Mastersizer 3000 is an instrument used for measuring particle size distribution in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIHYDROETHIDIUM (DHE) ASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test used to assess reactive oxygen species levels in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BICINCHONINIC ACID (BCA) PROTEIN QUANTIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bicinchoninic Acid protein quantification is a method used to determine protein concentration in mealworms during the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECTRAMAX ID3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SpectraMax iD3 is a microplate reader used for measuring absorbance in biochemical assays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLAB TECHNOLOGY CO., LTD.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biolab Technology Co., Ltd. is the supplier of assay kits used for analyzing ROS in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENT'S T TEST WITH TUKEY'S CORRECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOSTATISTICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A statistical test used to compare the means of different groups of mealworms for significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic diet refers to mealworms consuming plastics as a food source, which affects their nutrient absorption and growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHLORINATED INTERMEDIATES AND HYDROGEN CHLORIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These substances are toxic byproducts produced during the depolymerization of PVC, potentially damaging mealworms' intestines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL EPITHELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The intestinal epithelium is a layer of cells lining the gut, crucial for nutrient absorption and maintaining homeostasis in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT BACTERIAL CONSORTIUMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut bacterial consortiums refer to the diverse community of bacteria within the mealworm gut, aiding in plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMORPHOUS FRACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amorphous fractions are the disordered regions within polymers like PS and PVC, making them more susceptible to depolymerization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MID- AND SHORT-CHAIN POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mid- and short-chain polymers are smaller polymer units resulting from the depolymerization of larger chains in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL CRYSTALLINITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Material crystallinity determines the degree of structural order in polymers, affecting their susceptibility to degradation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION INTERMEDIATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation intermediates are the transient compounds formed during the breakdown of polymers in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RANDOM INTERNAL SCISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Random internal scission is a type of chemical bond breakage that results in depolymerization, producing mid-chain polymers in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE polymers, or polyethylene polymers, contain side chains and are categorized as crystalline plastics. They are subjected to depolymerization in the mealworm gut microenvironment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PVC polymers, or polyvinyl chloride polymers, are difficult to degrade and remain longer in the mealworm intestines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive model refers to the process by which mealworms digest and process various feedstocks, including microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGICAL-ECONOMIC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Analysis that combines technological and economic factors to evaluate the feasibility and sustainability of processes, such as mealworm-mediated plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDIR TECHNIQUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laser Direct Infrared Spectrometry, a technique used to detect and count residual microplastics after mealworm digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLA AND PBAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradable plastics requiring evaluation for mealworm-mediated digestion and depuration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COPEPODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Copepods are small aquatic crustaceans that, like other organisms unable to break down plastics, suffer from microplastic ingestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRABS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crabs are known to ingest microplastics, leading to potential intestinal blockages and health issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOI CARP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Koi carp are fish that, when exposed to microplastics, experience decreased nutrient uptake and inflammatory responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZEBRA FISH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zebra fish, when ingesting microplastics, can suffer from physical damage and impaired nutritional absorption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAW POWDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Straw powder is provided to mealworms as part of their diet and is digested without issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VEGETABLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vegetables are part of the mealworm diet and do not cause retention or damage in their digestive tract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-DEGRADING INVERTEBRATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Invertebrates capable of degrading plastics, contributing to the biodegradation process and associated oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES OF POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Properties of polymers that affect their degradation and mineralization by invertebrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXICITY OF DEGRADATION INTERMEDIATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potential harmful effects of intermediate products formed during plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PETRO-BASED POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymers derived from petroleum, such as PE, PS, and PVC, involved in plastic degradation studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
