      <data key="d1">"A biodegradable polymer studied for its adsorption and desorption mechanisms with oxytetracycline and other factors such as biofilms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(butylene adipate-co-terephthalate) is a type of biodegradable polymer often studied for its degradation properties and interactions with environmental factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CU(II)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cu(II) is a chemical form of copper commonly found in environmental studies affecting microplastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYTETRACYCLINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxytetracycline is an antibiotic whose adsorption behavior on microplastics is studied in environmental contexts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMIDAZOLIUM-BASED IONIC LIQUIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imidazolium-based ionic liquids are chemicals examined for their toxicity to organisms like Caenorhabditis elegans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISSOLVED ORGANIC MATTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dissolved organic matter refers to organic molecules dissolved in water, influencing the degradation processes of environmental pollutants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER PH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water pH is a measure of the acidity or alkalinity of water, impacting chemical reactions and microbial activity involved in biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL FAUNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soil fauna are animals living in the soil, playing a role in interactions with microplastics and affecting environmental degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE-ENHANCED RAMAN SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface-enhanced Raman spectroscopy is an analytical technique used to detect microplastics smaller than 1 micron in the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG, L.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AUTHOR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yang, L. is one of the authors of the study related to enhancing bioenergy production with carbon capture using microalgae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAPHENE OXIDE QUANTUM DOTS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
      <data key="d1">"Graphene Oxide Quantum Dots are a product used in bioenergy production and carbon capture of microalgae, enhanced by ultraviolet spectrum conversion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Graphene oxide quantum dots enhance carbon capture potential in Microalgae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nano-materials used in the conversion of ultraviolet spectrum to enhance microalgae bioenergy production."</data>
