    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-PURITY PS MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-purity PS microplastics are small particles of polystyrene used in the study to observe the effects of biodegradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL DYSBIOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal dysbiosis refers to the imbalance in the gut microbiome, caused in this context by the biodegradation of polystyrene of various molecular weights."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRAHIGH MOLECULAR WEIGHT POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ultrahigh molecular weight polystyrene is a variant with very large molecular weight, displaying limited biodegradation by mealworms compared to lower molecular weight variants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYNDIOTACTIC POLYSTYRENE (SPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Syndiotactic polystyrene is a structurally organized variant of polystyrene, produced for specialized commercial use due to its different crystallinity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC SOLID WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic solid waste refers to large volumes of discarded plastic products that contribute to environmental pollution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial biodegradation involves the breakdown of plastics by microbes, considered slow in the environment but effective in controlled biological systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE MICROPLASTICS (PS MPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene microplastics are small plastic particles that are characterized by their molecular weights, which are affected when passing through the larval intestinal tract of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIZE-AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Size-average molecular weight is another measure of molecular weight where the size of the polymer molecules is considered."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE OF MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The physiological response of mealworms refers to changes in mealworms' weight, survival rates, and consumption rates when fed different molecular weights of PS MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS REMOVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS removal is the process of reducing the amount of polystyrene microplastics by either consumption or degradation within the mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-1 refers to a specific sample of polystyrene microplastics tested for molecular weight changes after being processed by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-2 refers to another specific sample of polystyrene microplastics characterized by its molecular weight and tested for changes after mealworm digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-3 represents a sample of polystyrene microplastics studied for degradation and change in molecular weight after ingestion by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-4 is a sample of polystyrene microplastics that was tested to observe changes in molecular weight when processed by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-5&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-5 is a distinct sample of polystyrene microplastics examined for degradation and molecular weight variation after mealworm consumption."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-6&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-6 refers to a particular sample of polystyrene microplastics noted for its significant molecular weight change when consumed by mealworms over an extended period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PS CONSUMPTION RATES (SPCRS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific PS Consumption Rates refer to the rate at which different groups of mealworms consumed their respective polystyrene microplastic diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION (ST)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation refers to the diet control group where mealworms were deprived of feed to observe the impacts on their physiological and consumption measures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MWD (MOLECULAR WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MWD is used to describe the distribution of molecular weights of PS polymers post mealworm consumption, indicating degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHANOL-EXTRACTED FRACTION (C_E)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ethanol-extracted fraction is part of the analysis of mealworm frass to determine residual PS content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER-EXTRACTED FRACTION (C_W)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water-extracted fraction in frass analysis determines the extractable part of the residual PS in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THF-EXTRACTED FRACTION (C_T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The THF-extracted fraction is analyzed to estimate residual PS content in mealworm frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROPHILIC COMPONENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrophilic Components are parts of the frass that consist of water-soluble, digested organic compounds and salts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPOPHILIC SUBSTANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipophilic Substances are parts of the frass consisting of fat-soluble substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PS POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual PS Polymers are the leftover polystyrene polymers found in frass after ingestion by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR-WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION (MWD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular-Weight Distribution describes the variety of molecular weights in the polystyrene polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHANOL-EXTRACTED FRACTION (CE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ce refers to the fraction of lipophilic substances extracted using ethanol from frass after polystyrene ingestion by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THF-EXTRACTED FRACTION (CC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cc denotes the fraction of residual and modified PS content extracted using tetrahydrofuran (THF) from frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIZE-AVERAGE MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MZ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mz is an average molecular weight calculation that gives weight to larger molecules, observed in the study during polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MWD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight distribution (MWD) refers to the range of molecular weights present in a polymer sample, influencing how it undergoes biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDO-TYPE DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endo-type depolymerization involves random internal scission of polymer chains, resulting in oligomers and mid-chain polymers through biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER MACROMOLECULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer macromolecules are large molecules composed of repeating subunits, subject to depolymerization under biological conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIGOMERIC PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oligomeric products are shorter polymer fragments resulting from the depolymerization of larger polymer chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MID-CHAIN POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
