      <data key="d2">chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASIC METABOLIC RATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basic metabolic rates are the minimal energy expenditure required to maintain the vital functions of an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL ASSAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical assays are tests conducted to measure stored energy and metabolic activities in mealworms processing plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY EFFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy efficiency in mealworms refers to their ability to convert ingested materials into usable energy for growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONAL POTENTIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritional potential refers to the ability of mealworms to provide nutritional benefits, which is enhanced by their plastic processing capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADAPTIVE PREDISPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adaptive predisposition in mealworms refers to their capabilities to adjust and utilize available resources, like plastics, for survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C8 ESTERASE LIPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C8 esterase lipase is an enzyme associated with elevated activity in both digestive tracts and bacterial communities, indicating its involvement in the degradation of certain compounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OAT - OATMEAL WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OAT is a variant in PCA analysis correlating with the x-axis and influencing enzyme activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEL - CARDBOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CEL is a variant in PCA analysis correlated with the y-axis, impacting enzyme secretions in bacterial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-OXO - OXO-DEGRADABLE POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-oxo is a variant associated with enzyme activity related to polymer degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-REG - POLYETHYLENE REGRANULATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-reg is a variant affecting the secretion of C8 ester lipase, suggesting a potential avenue for polymer degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS - POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS is correlated with strong enzymatic activities in gut bacteria, indicative of degradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N-ACETYL-Β-GLUCOSAMINIDASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N-Acetyl-β-glucosaminidase is an enzyme that participates in the breakdown of glycosaminoglycans and acts in conjunction with other digestive enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEINS, FATS, AND CARBOHYDRATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteins, fats, and carbohydrates are macronutrients essential for various physiological processes and are closely examined in enzyme activity studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Α-CHYMOTRYPSIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"α-Chymotrypsin is an enzyme involved in protein digestion, correlated with certain dietary environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHORUS BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phosphorus bonds are chemical connections involved in the transformation processes catalyzed by enzymes like phosphatases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OATMEAL WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oatmeal waste serves as a diet variant influencing enzyme activities and is analyzed for its effects in nutrient studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDBOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardboard is a diet variant impacting enzyme secretions, serving as a substrate for microbial activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAMMOX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anammox is a biological process where anaerobic ammonium oxidation occurs, contributing to the nitrogen cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREVIBACTERIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brevibacterium is a genus of bacteria that increases in populations in mealworms on a polyethylene-based diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LISTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Listeria is a genus of bacteria whose proportions increase in mealworms when fed on polystyrene-based diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERRUCOMICROBIALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Verrucomicrobiales is an order of bacteria associated with various hosts, including insects, and involved in symbiotic interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Verrucomicrobiales is an order of bacteria identified in the study, linked with N-fixing capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XANTHOMONADALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xanthomonadales is an order of bacteria mentioned in relation to the microbiome characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xanthomonadales is an order of bacteria often found in plant and insect hosts, participating in symbiotic and protective roles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iron is a trace element required for the enzymatic activity of nitrogenase, involved in nitrogen fixation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VANADIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vanadium is a trace element necessary at the active site of nitrogenase for nitrogen fixation in symbionts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANGANESE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Manganese is a trace element that supports the function of nitrogenase in nitrogen-fixing symbionts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NH3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NH3, or ammonia, is a form of nitrogen that can be re-assimilated by symbionts in nutrient-deficient environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT FLAGELLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut flagellates are microorganisms residing in the guts of termites, associated with nitrogen-fixing communities through relationships with Bacteroidales ectosymbionts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRY-WOOD TERMITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dry-wood termites are host organisms in which gut flagellates and their bacterial ectosymbionts, such as Bacteroidales, form nitrogen-fixing communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRIFTING POLYMERIC MATERIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"These materials are synthetic compounds that can float and drift in the marine environment, posing environmental challenges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIOTASSAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A high-throughput qPCR approach that, when combined with next-generation sequencing, examines the diversity of gut microbes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERMITE HOST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Termite host refers to termites serving as host organisms for complex microbial communities within their digestive systems, including Termite Group 1 bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHANOGENIC COMMUNITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBIAL COMMUNITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groups of microorganisms that produce methane as a byproduct of their metabolic processes, detectable using group-specific primers and probes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methanogenic communities consist of methanogens, a type of archaea involved in producing methane and detectable by quantitative real-time polymerase chain reaction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8cc3aa81b03290b589ccf0a1548ca0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUANTITATIVE REAL-TIME POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (QPCR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A laboratory technique used to amplify and quantify DNA, applicable in gut microbiota studies and detecting methanogenic communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REAL-TIME POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Real-time polymerase chain reaction is a technique used to amplify and simultaneously quantify targeted DNA, useful for detecting methanogenic communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b8cc3aa81b03290b589ccf0a1548ca0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTENTIAL DIAZOTROPHIC BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2</data>
      <data key="d1">"Verrucomicrobia are identified as part of the less abundant diazotrophic community in larvae fed polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TM1 AND ZM1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TM1 and ZM1 are two bacterial strains isolated from mealworm guts, capable of growing with polystyrene as their sole carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL. (2015A, 2015B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yang and colleagues conducted studies on the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae and identified specific gut bacteria involved in the process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TANG ET AL. (2017)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tang and colleagues isolated two bacterial strains from mealworm guts capable of using polystyrene as a carbon source, contributing to the understanding of polystyrene biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTICSEUROPE (PEMRG)/CONSULTIC/ECEBD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PlasticsEurope and associated groups are sources for data on polystyrene production and environmental impact statistics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BANDYOPADHYAY AND BASAK (2007)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bandyopadhyay and Basak identified properties of polystyrene, including its resistance to photo-oxidation, contributing to environmental persistence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAHARANA ET AL. (2007)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maharana and colleagues discussed various recycling methods for polystyrene, including mechanical, chemical, and thermal processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFE STAGES OF TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The life stages of Tenebrio molitor include egg, larva, pupa, and imago, characteristic of holometabolic insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOLOGICAL PROCESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physiological processes in this context refer to maintenance, growth, development, and reproduction of organisms as modeled by the DEB framework."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLOMETABOLIC INSECTS DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An extension of the standard DEB model specifically adapted for holometabolic insects with specific assumptions and equations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMPLIFIED DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A version of the DEB model that allows for significant simplifications and is used to assess the impact of toxic substances on the energy budgets of organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY FLUXES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy fluxes refer to the flow of energy through different physiological processes such as maintenance, growth, and reproduction in organisms as described in the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY RESERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy reserves are the stored energy within organisms that is mobilized for various physiological functions, including growth and reproduction in the DEB context."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAGER ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jager et al. refers to the authors of studies and research papers that have contributed to the development and application of the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOOIJMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kooijman is a researcher who has significantly contributed to the development of the DEB model and its applications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLANDRES ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Llandres et al. are researchers who have contributed to the adaptations of the DEB model for holometabolic insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAGER AND ZIMMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jager and Zimmer developed or significantly contributed to the DEB model and assumptions for analyzing larval development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jager and Zimmer have developed the simplified version of the DEB model to evaluate toxic substances' effects on organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD AVAILABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food availability refers to the supply of food that influences the energy reserves and physiological processes of organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH TRAJECTORIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth trajectories are the patterns of growth observed in organisms over time, influenced by various factors such as environment and food type within the DEB model framework."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATURATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maturation is the developmental phase involving reaching maturity in organisms, modeled in the DEB context as part of their life cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic Maintenance is the physiological upkeep of larval structure and metabolic functions, impaired in starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic maintenance refers to the energy expenditure required to maintain the structural integrity, health, and function of an organism's body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic maintenance refers to the energy needed to maintain cellular and physiological functions necessary for survival, as considered in the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEB model refers to the Dynamic Energy Budget theory, used to model growth and energy allocation."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEB model, or Dynamic Energy Budget model, is used to analyze and predict biological and ecological dynamics concerning energy allocation in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynamic Energy Budget model used to analyze development changes and reserve dynamics in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model is a theoretical framework used to describe how organisms uptake and utilize energy, involving parameters like growth, metabolism, and reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Von Bertalanffy growth rate (\(\dot{r}_B\)) is a parameter in the DEB model explaining the rate of growth to maximum body length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROL SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Control sample refers here to the group of larvae fed with oatmeal ad libitum under standard conditions for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Control sample serves as a baseline group against which other experimental groups are compared to assess changes in density and growth of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation 1 is a diet regimen where larvae are kept without food in isolation, highlighting the impact of severe nutrient deprivation on development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation 1 is one of the groups in the study subjected to insufficient feeding conditions, impacting the growth of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation 2 involves larvae being kept without food but with access to droppings and moult residues, reflecting less severe deprivation conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation 2 is another group in the study with limited nutrition, similar to Starvation 1, affecting larval growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS LARGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS Large represents older and larger larvae fed with Styrofoam, emphasizing size and age as factors in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS large refers to older and larger larvae compared to the standard PS group, specifically marked by their greater mass and tested for dietary responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PS + Oat. diet involves a combination of Styrofoam and crushed oatmeal, introducing periodic nutrient supply every 10 days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation 1 in the DEB model describes reserve dynamics in the organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation 2 in the DEB model describes changes in the structural length of organisms over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation 3 in the DEB model describes the reproduction rate of organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION 4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation 4 in the DEB model is used to express growth equations in terms of specific parameters like growth rate and body length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIALS AND METHODS SECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Materials and Methods section provides additional information on assumptions and model extensions specific for T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The experiment involved studying T. molitor larvae under different feeding conditions to understand growth dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS (STYROFOAM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS, also known as Styrofoam, is a material used in the experiment as a dietary component for larvae to analyze their ability to digest or process synthetic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS, or Styrofoam, is used as an alternative diet for T. molitor larvae, examining its impact on larval development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM CHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrofoam chips are used as a transport package in the experiment, serving as a food source for larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMINS AND MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamins and minerals are mixed with crushed oatmeal and provided to the larvae every 10 days to enhance their diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURAL BODY LENGTH (L)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural body length refers to a measured parameter of the larvae, used to track development and growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC BODY LENGTH (L_V)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric body length is a parameter representing the volume-related growth of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL BODY LENGTH (L_W)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical body length is another measured parameter of larvae, indicating physical growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONDUCTANCE (V)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy conductance refers to the rate at which energy is conducted through the organism, an important physiological parameter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE RATE COEFFICIENT (K_M)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This coefficient represents the maintenance energy requirements of the larvae under study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY INVESTMENT RATIO (G)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The energy investment ratio indicates the proportion of energy allocated to growth and maintenance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS + oat represents a dietary regimen for larvae, combining Styrofoam with crushed oatmeal to test the effects on growth and metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT + VIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS + oat + vit denotes a dietary treatment for larvae that includes Styrofoam, crushed oatmeal, and added vitamins and minerals, designed to enhance nutrient intake."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( R \), \( R_S \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Symbolizes the reproduction rate and its scaled equivalent, critical for understanding the reproductive success of larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( E \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Represents scaled reserve density, an indicator of the energy reserves available within the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( E_R \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to the amount of energy stored in the reproduction buffer, crucial for reproductive potential."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( F \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Denotes the scaled functional response, signifying the efficiency and ability of the larvae to convert consumed food into energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \DOT{R}_M \), \( \DOT{R}_{SM} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indicates the maximum reproduction rate (at optimal conditions) and its scaled form, essential for assessing reproduction capacity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_M(E), L_{V0}(E) \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Describes the maximum structural or volumetric body lengths, important for evaluating growth capacity in relation to energy reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{0}, L_{V0} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refers to the initial structural and volumetric body lengths at the start of the experiment, providing baseline measurements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{P}, L_{VP} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specifies the structural and volumetric body lengths at puberty, marking a key developmental stage in larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( L_{EM} \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Represents the maximum volumetric length of reserve based on given factors, critical for understanding reserve capacity and energy storage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \KAPPA \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraction of mobilized reserves allocated to body maintenance, reflecting energy management efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( \KAPPA_R \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraction of reserves fixed in eggs, indicating the reproductive investment of the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( R_B \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Von Bertalanffy growth rate, a measure used to describe growth dynamics over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [P_M] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volume-specific somatic maintenance power, emphasizing the energy expenditure for maintaining body functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E_C] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volume-specific costs for structure, reflecting the energetic investment needed for structural components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( E_0, E_T \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy content of a single egg versus energy over a total number of eggs, key for understanding reproductive energy allocation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;\( [E_R] \)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy density threshold for pupation, critical for larval development and transition to the next life stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC LENGTH (L_V)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric length (L_V) refers to the structural volume of an organism that changes due to dynamics in reserve density, particularly under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCALED RESERVES DENSITY (E)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scaled reserves density (e) is a measure of how reserves within an organism are distributed or concentrated, influenced by the organism's maximum volume of reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYNAMICAL ENERGY BUDGET (DEB) MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DEB model describes how organisms allocate energy for maintenance, growth, and reproduction to predict survival based on energy constraints."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM POLYSTYRENE CHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrofoam polystyrene chips are used in an experiment to assess mass loss and are weighed at intervals after being conditioned with larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE COSTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic maintenance costs refer to the energy expenditure necessary for an organism to maintain its basic physical and physiological functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLANDRES ET AL. (2015)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A study that provides insights into energy dynamics during the pupation process, indicating specific thresholds for biological transformations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION (15)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation (15) is used to estimate parameters in the control sample, reflecting changes relevant to the study's context."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION (4)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation (4) describes the dynamics of growth concerning structure volume, indicating how certain conditions like starvation affect growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REARING BOXES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rearing boxes are used to house larvae during experimental conditions, facilitating controlled study settings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUATION (3)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Equation (3) is used in the context of pupation to estimate the threshold for the reproduction buffer density necessary for developmental transitions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAGER AND ZIMMER (2012)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jager and Zimmer (2012) is a study referenced for understanding energy density thresholds and toxic actions in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jager and Zimmer (2012) provide foundational definitions and proportionality coefficients important to understanding energy budgets in biological systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY FLUX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy flux refers to the transfer of energy from reserves into reproductive functions, represented by a mathematical model in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OOGENESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oogenesis is the process of egg development in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_T is a threshold energy density for reproduction, determining when the reproduction buffer is full and reproduction processes like pupation can begin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_R(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_R(t) represents the time-dependent energy density relative to the reproduction threshold during an organism's development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;[E_R]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"[E_R] is the energy density threshold for pupation, necessary for transitioning from larval to pupal stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_I represents the total energy available for egg production during the imago stage of an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E_0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E_0 is the baseline energy, used as a reference point to scale reproductive outputs like the number of eggs produced."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC AND MATURITY MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic and maturity maintenance involves energy expended to sustain both physical body structures and developmental progression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOOIJMAN (2010)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"REFERENCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kooijman (2010) is a study providing foundational insights into DEB models and primary parameters like energy allocation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P(t) represents the probability of reaching a reproductive threshold at a given time, modeled by a sigmoidal distribution curve."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAU (Τ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tau (τ) is the specific time when pupation is most likely to occur, identified as the distribution curve's inflection point."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tau (τ) represents the average time of pupation from the beginning of the experiment in days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOG-LOGISTIC MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The log-logistic model is used to describe the distribution of pupation probability over time, presenting a sigmoidal form."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRANDON ET AL. (2020)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"REFERENCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brandon et al. (2020) is cited for analyzing the impact of PS diet on T. molitor larvae, including potential toxic effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIT.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vit. refers to vitamins added to the diet of larvae to improve survival and mass loss of PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL. (2018A)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"REFERENCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yang et al. (2018a) is a referenced study focusing on the potential inconsistencies noted when observing PS ingestion's effect on larval survival and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. (2018a) is a study reference, comparing PS consumption and survival rates in larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yang et al. (2018a) provides reference data for comparison in diet effects on T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL. (2018B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"REFERENCE"</data>
