      <data key="d1">"The mass loss of PS is measured to determine how much polystyrene is consumed by the larvae during the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT. GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PS + oat. group refers to the set of larvae fed with PS and oats, showing improved survival and mass loss compared to other groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT. + VIT. GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PS + oat. + vit. group refers to the set of larvae fed with PS, oats, and vitamins, which showed improved survival and consumption rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION 1 AND STARVATION 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EXPERIMENTAL CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Subsets of the Starvation group that demonstrated very low survival rates over the experiment's duration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Control is a comparison group in the experiment that likely received a standard or adequate diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORALES-RAMOS ET AL. (2010)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morales-Ramos et al. (2010) documents nutritional influences on larval instars and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E(T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"e(t) is the scaled reserve density, an indicator of available reserves for somatic maintenance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSTARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Instars refer to the developmental stages of larvae, which vary in duration based on diet and other conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTIVE THRESHOLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproductive threshold is a concept indicating the required reserve level needed for reproducing and forming pupae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric Length refers to the size of larval structures, which decreases in response to insufficient dietary energy or starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Volumetric length is a measure used to evaluate the growth of larvae in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIG. 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Figure 3 illustrates the growth curve fitting and other experimental data resulting from the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUM OF SQUARED ERRORS (SSE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SSE is a statistical measure of data variability around the fitted model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROOT MEAN SQUARE ERROR (RMSE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RMSE is the standard deviation of the residuals used to assess model fit quality."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEB MODEL PARAMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEB Model Parameters such as $k_M$ and $g$ represent metabolic rates and are affected by the energy availability in larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve Density represents the energy reserves in larvae, which decrease during starvation or insufficient dietary intake."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserve density refers to the amount of energy reserves, like lipids, stored within an organism, influencing its capacity to survive, particularly during food shortages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONDUCTANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy Conductance (ν) is a fixed parameter used to model energy flow in larvae under different nutritional conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD AVAILABILITY (F)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food Availability (f) indicates the access to energy sources in the diet, directly influencing larval growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;$K_M$ AND $G$&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"$k_M$ and $g$ are DEB parameters representing metabolic rates, both of which decrease under starvation conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DROPPINGS AND MOULT RESIDUES&quot;">
