      <data key="d3">63.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms are studied for their ability to biodegrade plastics, offering a sustainable solution to plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were used in this study to achieve biodegradation of plastics over a set number of days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms, as larvae of Tenebrio species, contribute to the biodegradation process of polyethylene, breaking it down biologically."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms utilize biological processes to biodegrade polystyrene and polyethylene within their gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms facilitate the biodegradation of polystyrene, demonstrating their ability to break down complex polymer structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms facilitate biodegradation of microplastics, breaking them down through grinding and microbial actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms participate in the biodegradation of various plastics, revealing potential for eco-friendly waste management processes."</data>
