    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">276.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Polystyrene affects the fatty acid profile and growth of Tenebrio molitor, indicating degradation and dietary impacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene as a feed option increases larval mortality but boosts nitrogenous substance content in Tenebrio molitor excreta."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is ingested by Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating a biological pathway for plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, indicating a potential natural method for managing plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor, commonly known as mealworms, is a species of beetle larvae that has garnered significant attention for its potential role in biodegrading polystyrene, a common plastic. Research indicates that these larvae are capable of consuming and breaking down polystyrene foam, leveraging their unique gut microbiome to facilitate this process. The biodegradation ability of Tenebrio molitor is largely attributed to the interactions between the larvae and the microorganisms present in their gut, which are capable of degrading polystyrene and altering the gut's microbial composition. This process not only allows the larvae to survive on polystyrene as their sole carbon source but also suggests the presence of polystyrene-degrading bacteria within their digestive systems. The potential for Tenebrio molitor to contribute to reducing plastic waste highlights its importance in environmental waste management and entomoremediation, providing a promising biological solution to mitigate plastic pollution. Consequently, these larvae are being used in numerous studies focused on polystyrene biodegradation, showcasing their significant environmental impact and ability to transform plastic waste into a more manageable form.&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of ingesting and biodegrading polystyrene, thereby reducing plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene due to their symbiotic bacteria, showing potential for environmental sustainability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is used in studies to understand the degradation of polystyrene waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae exhibit the ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene waste can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, influenced by factors affecting its degradation rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae play a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene through their gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is biodegraded by the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, which is key to understanding the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, bioavailability"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, ecological interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, ecological studies"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, environmental solution"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, environmental sustainability"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, gut-microbe interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbial action"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbiome alteration"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbiome interactions"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic waste management"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic waste reduction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, waste management"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, waste processing"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, waste reduction"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"degradation, dietary influence"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary component, degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"ecological adaptation, biodegradation potential"&lt;SEP&gt;"feeding experiment, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"microbial degradation, plastic processing"&lt;SEP&gt;"microbiota shift, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic biodegradation, waste management"&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372aa232f6e8aad1d8e0a93f16a42b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a</data>
