    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">95.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Polyethylene is a material subjected to biodegradation studies using Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor demonstrates the ability to biodegrade polyethylene, contributing to efforts in reducing plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polyethylene, contributing to reducing plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor successfully biodegrades polyethylene foam, contributing to sustainable waste management practices."|&gt;"entomoremediation, sustainability"&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor, or mealworms, show the potential for breaking down polyethylene, contributing to understanding biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor's gut microbiome is involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, contributing to the breakdown process of this plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor enhances microbial biodegradation of polyethylene, showcasing potential environmental benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polyethylene foam as part of their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polyethylene, influencing research on biological solutions to plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor are capable of degrading polyethylene, contributing to the study of plastic waste reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae, along with gut microbes, degrade polyethylene, highlighting the plastic's susceptibility to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, dietary adaptation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, environmental benefit"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbial activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbial interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, waste reduction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biological degradation, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"decomposition, biological interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"material breakdown, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"microbial interaction, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
