    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE (PS)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">113.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms are capable of ingesting and degrading polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecules and eventually converting some of it to CO2 among other products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor can degrade polystyrene, highlighting its role in plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading polystyrene in its digestive system, serving as a model for studying this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae degrade polystyrene through their gut microbiome, thus modifying and oxidizing it in the process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The T. molitor larvae are used in experiments to assess their ability to consume and degrade PS under different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae consume polystyrene, evidencing this through the presence of holes and tunnels in PS sheets, although PS is not sufficient for biomass gain in the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of degrading PS through its gut microbiome which involves specific bacteria and enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbes of Tenebrio molitor are capable of degrading polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is biodegraded by mealworm (Tenebrio molitor) larva under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae also degrade polystyrene through processes evidenced by chemical changes in their frass similar to those in Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polystyrene, though less effectively compared to Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is degraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, which possess the capability to depolymerize PS by breaking down the benzene ring structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae consumed and biodegraded polystyrene, allowing researchers to study changes in mass and biochemical composition."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, chemical transformation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, degradation capability"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, experimental biology"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, feeding experiments"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbial interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbiome activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, model study"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, waste reduction"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic biodegradation, gut microbiome"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3</data>
    </edge>
