    <edge source="&quot;BRAN&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">120.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bran in the diet of mealworms provides essential nutrients, aiding in resistance to microplastic-induced harm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is used in cofeeding experiments with mealworms to observe its effects on their growth and mortality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume bran as a nutrient source, impacting their ability to degrade plastic effectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is combined with PS in mealworms' diets, significantly affecting their survival rates and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is part of the diet used to assess mealworm's ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran was combined with PS in the diet of mealworms to provide necessary nutrients lacking in PS alone, thereby improving survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were fed with bran as a dietary component in the control group of the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is a more palatable and nutritious diet for mealworms compared to PU, supporting their growth and metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of bran alongside plastic affected mealworm growth and resulted in different levels of plastic degradation and mineralization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran serves as a nutritional supplement to mealworms, enhancing their growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran serves as a nutritional supplement to support mealworm health and potentially enhance PS degradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplements the diet of mealworms, enhancing their ability to degrade polystyrene faster."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran was used as a supplementary feed ingredient to support mealworm growth during the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran was used as a comparison diet in the study, showing that mealworms have lower nitrogen-fixing activity when consuming conventional diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is used as a control nutrient to compare against microplastic-fed mealworms in biodegradation trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is used as a nutritional control in the study to compare against PS-fed mealworms in terms of growth and health."</data>
      <data key="d5">"control diet, nutritional comparison"&lt;SEP&gt;"control study, comparative analysis"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet comparison, nutrient intake"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary aid, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary component, control group"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary impact, experimental variable"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary influence, growth impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary supplementation, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"enhanced nutrition, degradation rate increase"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, diet comparison"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, supplementation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, support"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional support, dietary impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutritional support, experimental design"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a14229bceb339a4ca1baf0772b47ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52</data>
    </edge>
