    <edge source="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">150.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Feeding polystyrene to mealworms results in high mortality due to its negligible nutritional content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are capable of degrading polystyrene, an application useful in managing plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is biodegraded by mealworms, particularly Tenebrio molitor, through processes involving their gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can digest polystyrene, showcasing an organic solution to plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have the ability to consume and degrade polystyrene, which is a finding observed across various countries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are used in the study to biodegrade polystyrene, illustrating an interaction where the organisms help break down the polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can consume and degrade polystyrene, offering an eco-friendly solution to plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are known to biodegrade polystyrene through their gut microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms, specifically Tenebrio molitor, biodegrade polystyrene through the activity of gut microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can biodegrade polystyrene, transforming it into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene is examined for its unique role in mealworms' energy metabolism despite being a non-traditional feed material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are capable of degrading polystyrene, reducing the accumulation of this synthetic material in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have the ability to biodegrade polystyrene, making them an important subject in polystyrene waste management studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms, particularly the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, can biodegrade polystyrene, facilitating its breakdown and mineralization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume and biodegrade polystyrene, showcasing their role in waste reduction and environmental management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are being studied for their potential to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have been studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene, showcasing a unique interaction between organisms and synthetic materials."</data>
