    <edge source="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;" target="&quot;PS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">163.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms are capable of biodegrading polystyrene through consumption and gut microbial digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are used to feed upon and biodegrade PS, showing significant changes in PS molecular structure as they process it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are used to consume and degrade PS, showing varying degrees of plastic utilization in experiments across different regions and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume PS, contributing to the biodegradation process of this plastic in waste management experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms ingest PS and show different metabolism effects based on location, linking mealworm physiology to microplastic digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms degrade and mineralize PS through their gut bacteria, showing a notable capacity to break down this plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can consume PS material to some extent, as indicated by a percentage of mass loss when used in feeding experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume PS as part of a study to determine its degradation through microbial activity in their gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms fed with PS experienced changes in carbohydrate and lipid levels, suggesting a metabolic shift due to the ingestion of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have difficulty consuming PS due to its hardness and gloss, affecting the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms fed with PS displayed chemical changes in the polymer, confirming the role of mealworms in breaking down PS through biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are used to study the biodegradation of PS, showing significant changes in its molecular structure after digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have the ability to consume PS, which demonstrates potential for reducing plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms degrade PS when fed with nutrients such as soy protein and bran, allowing assessment of PS decomposition under different conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have been studied for their ability to biodegrade PS through biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms ingest and biodegrade PS through depolymerization, effectively reducing its molecular size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms were used to study the mass loss of PS and the biochemical impact on nutrients like proteins, carbohydrates, and lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume PS, and their survival is influenced by the amount and type of PS consumed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study evaluates how PS affects the survival, growth, and reproduction of mealworm larvae through DEB modelling."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, biological interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, digestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, ecological impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, experimental subjects"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, waste management"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption difficulty, material characteristics"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, material degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet effects, plastic consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary impact, metabolic change"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental impact, plastic consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"feeding, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"impact assessment, substance effect"&lt;SEP&gt;"metabolism, regional variation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, consumption activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic degradation, biological impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic degradation, digestive process"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic degradation, experimental study"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4</data>
