      <data key="d3">31.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lipid peroxidation is a consequence of oxidative stress from plastic ingestion in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation is a result of oxidative stress experienced by mealworm larvae when exposed to microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The occurrence of oxidative stress can lead to lipid peroxidation, which damages cell membranes due to free radicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid peroxidation serves as a measure of oxidative stress in macroinvertebrates while degrading plastics."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biological effect, stress response"&lt;SEP&gt;"cell damage, free radicals"&lt;SEP&gt;"damage, stress effect"&lt;SEP&gt;"stress biomarker, cellular damage"</data>
