      <data key="d3">64.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Higher ROS levels are a direct indicator of oxidative stress in mealworm larvae feeding on PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of ROS is a key indicator and driver of oxidative stress in mealworm larvae exposed to microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS levels are measured to assess oxidative stress within cells, indicating cellular health status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reactive Oxygen Species are indicative of oxidative stress, acting as a biological marker for this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress involves the production of ROS as a key factor in the physiological response during plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS contribute to oxidative stress by damaging cellular components in Tenebrio larvae fed with different PEs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is associated with elevated production of ROS, indicating cellular imbalance."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biomarker, stress indicator"&lt;SEP&gt;"cellular response, stress markers"&lt;SEP&gt;"free radicals, cellular imbalance"&lt;SEP&gt;"oxidative stress, biomarkers"&lt;SEP&gt;"stress causation, reactive damage"&lt;SEP&gt;"stress marker, physiological impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"stress measurement, cellular health"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
