    <edge source="&quot;T. MOLITOR LARVAE&quot;" target="&quot;PET&quot;">
      <data key="d3">64.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"T. molitor larvae biodegrade and consume PET at a faster rate than known microbial methods, demonstrating their efficiency in reducing plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae consume and partially digest PET to obtain energy, although it is insufficient for complete nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae degrade PET polymers through biological digestion, which causes significant reductions in molecular weight and structural properties of the PET polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of consuming and biodegrading PET efficiently, showing a significant mass reduction of the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae are capable of decomposing PET polymers through a process of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae contribute to the biodegradation of PET through their gut microbes and other biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae were observed for changes in gut microbiota related to PET biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, digestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, organism-product interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biotic interaction, consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, degradation efficiency"&lt;SEP&gt;"experimental subject, biodegradation observation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317</data>
    </edge>
